---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateBatchPredictionJobsRequest
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob entered any of the following states: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field modelVersionId? string Output only. The version ID of the Model that produces the predictions via this job.
---@field partialFailures? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatusList Output only. Partial failures encountered. For example, single files that can't be read. This field never exceeds 20 entries. Status details fields contain standard Google Cloud error details.
---@field outputConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobOutputConfig Required. The Configuration specifying where output predictions should be written. The schema of any single prediction may be specified as a concatenation of Model's PredictSchemata's instance_schema_uri and prediction_schema_uri.
---@field modelMonitoringConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringConfig Model monitoring config will be used for analysis model behaviors, based on the input and output to the batch prediction job, as well as the provided training dataset.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field explanationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpec Explanation configuration for this BatchPredictionJob. Can be specified only if generate_explanation is set to `true`. This value overrides the value of Model.explanation_spec. All fields of explanation_spec are optional in the request. If a field of the explanation_spec object is not populated, the corresponding field of the Model.explanation_spec object is inherited.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field instanceConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobInstanceConfig Configuration for how to convert batch prediction input instances to the prediction instances that are sent to the Model.
---@field modelMonitoringStatsAnomalies? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringStatsAnomaliesList Get batch prediction job monitoring statistics.
---@field outputInfo? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobOutputInfo Output only. Information further describing the output of this job.
---@field modelParameters? any The parameters that govern the predictions. The schema of the parameters may be specified via the Model's PredictSchemata's parameters_schema_uri.
---@field dedicatedResources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchDedicatedResources The config of resources used by the Model during the batch prediction. If the Model supports DEDICATED_RESOURCES this config may be provided (and the job will use these resources), if the Model doesn't support AUTOMATIC_RESOURCES, this config must be provided.
---@field manualBatchTuningParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ManualBatchTuningParameters Immutable. Parameters configuring the batch behavior. Currently only applicable when dedicated_resources are used (in other cases Vertex AI does the tuning itself).
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob was created.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account that the DeployedModel's container runs as. If not specified, a system generated one will be used, which has minimal permissions and the custom container, if used, may not have enough permission to access other Google Cloud resources. Users deploying the Model must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account.
---@field inputConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobInputConfig Required. Input configuration of the instances on which predictions are performed. The schema of any single instance may be specified via the Model's PredictSchemata's instance_schema_uri.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of this BatchPredictionJob.
---@field resourcesConsumed? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ResourcesConsumed Output only. Information about resources that had been consumed by this job. Provided in real time at best effort basis, as well as a final value once the job completes. Note: This field currently may be not populated for batch predictions that use AutoML Models.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when the job's state is JOB_STATE_FAILED or JOB_STATE_CANCELLED.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the BatchPredictionJob.
---@field model? string The name of the Model resource that produces the predictions via this job, must share the same ancestor Location. Starting this job has no impact on any existing deployments of the Model and their resources. Exactly one of model, unmanaged_container_model, or endpoint must be set. The model resource name may contain version id or version alias to specify the version. Example: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@2` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@golden` if no version is specified, the default version will be deployed. The model resource could also be a publisher model. Example: `publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}`
---@field endpoint? string For Bring-Your-Own-Endpoint (BYOE), the name of the Endpoint resource that produces the predictions via this job, must share the same ancestor Location. Exactly one of model, unmanaged_container_model, or endpoint must be set. Example: `projects/193595526740/locations/us-central1/endpoints/4203439000301600768`
---@field modelMonitoringStatus? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. The running status of the model monitoring pipeline.
---@field unmanagedContainerModel? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1UnmanagedContainerModel Contains model information necessary to perform batch prediction without requiring uploading to model registry. Exactly one of model, unmanaged_container_model, or endpoint must be set.
---@field generateExplanation? boolean Generate explanation with the batch prediction results. When set to `true`, the batch prediction output changes based on the `predictions_format` field of the BatchPredictionJob.output_config object: * `bigquery`: output includes a column named `explanation`. The value is a struct that conforms to the Explanation object. * `jsonl`: The JSON objects on each line include an additional entry keyed `explanation`. The value of the entry is a JSON object that conforms to the Explanation object. * `csv`: Generating explanations for CSV format is not supported. If this field is set to true, either the Model.explanation_spec or explanation_spec must be populated.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize BatchPredictionJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a BatchPredictionJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the BatchPredictionJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field disableContainerLogging? boolean For custom-trained Models and AutoML Tabular Models, the container of the DeployedModel instances will send `stderr` and `stdout` streams to Cloud Logging by default. Please note that the logs incur cost, which are subject to [Cloud Logging pricing](https://cloud.google.com/logging/pricing). User can disable container logging by setting this flag to true.
---@field completionStats? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CompletionStats Output only. Statistics on completed and failed prediction instances.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob was most recently updated.
---@field parent? string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the BatchPredictionJob in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateDatasetsDatasetVersionsRequest
---@field bigQueryDatasetName? string Output only. Name of the associated BigQuery dataset.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. The resource name of the DatasetVersion. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}/datasetVersions/{dataset_version}`
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field metadata? any Required. Output only. Additional information about the DatasetVersion.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this DatasetVersion was created.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this DatasetVersion was last updated.
---@field modelReference? string Output only. Reference to the public base model last used by the dataset version. Only set for prompt dataset versions.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field displayName? string The user-defined name of the DatasetVersion. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field parent string Required. The name of the Dataset resource. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateDatasetsRequest
---@field metadata? any Required. Additional information about the Dataset.
---@field savedQueries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SavedQueryList All SavedQueries belong to the Dataset will be returned in List/Get Dataset response. The annotation_specs field will not be populated except for UI cases which will only use annotation_spec_count. In CreateDataset request, a SavedQuery is created together if this field is set, up to one SavedQuery can be set in CreateDatasetRequest. The SavedQuery should not contain any AnnotationSpec.
---@field description? string The description of the Dataset.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a Dataset. If set, this Dataset and all sub-resources of this Dataset will be secured by this key.
---@field modelReference? string Optional. Reference to the public base model last used by the dataset. Only set for prompt datasets.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Dataset was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Dataset was last updated.
---@field metadataArtifact? string Output only. The resource name of the Artifact that was created in MetadataStore when creating the Dataset. The Artifact resource name pattern is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/metadataStores/{metadata_store}/artifacts/{artifact}`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the Dataset. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field metadataSchemaUri? string Required. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing additional information about the Dataset. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 Schema Object. The schema files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/dataset/metadata/.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. The resource name of the Dataset. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}`
---@field dataItemCount? string Output only. The number of DataItems in this Dataset. Only apply for non-structured Dataset.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Datasets. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Dataset (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable. Following system labels exist for each Dataset: * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/dataset_metadata_schema": output only, its value is the metadata_schema's title.
---@field parent? string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the Dataset in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateMemoryBanksMemoriesRequest
---@field scope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Required. Immutable. Represents the scope of the Memory. Memories are isolated within their scope. The scope is defined when creating or generating memories. Scope values cannot contain the wildcard character '*'.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was created.
---@field description? string Optional. Represents the description of the Memory.
---@field fact? string Optional. Represents semantic knowledge extracted from the source content.
---@field revisionTtl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for the revision. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field structuredContent? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryStructuredContent Optional. Represents the structured content of the memory.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for this resource. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field topics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryTopicIdList Optional. Represents the Topics of the Memory.
---@field name? string Identifier. Represents the resource name of the Memory. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/memories/{memory}`
---@field memoryType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMemoryTypeEnum|string Optional. Represents the type of the memory. If not set, the `NATURAL_LANGUAGE_COLLECTION` type is used. If `STRUCTURED_COLLECTION` or `STRUCTURED_PROFILE` is used, then `structured_data` must be provided.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Represents the display name of the Memory.
---@field expireTime? string Optional. Represents the timestamp of when this resource is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output when `expiration` is set on input, regardless of whether `expire_time` or `ttl` was provided.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was most recently updated.
---@field context? string Optional. Represents the context of the memory.
---@field revisionLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Represents the labels to apply to the Memory Revision created as a result of this request.
---@field revisionExpireTime? string Optional. Input only. Represents the timestamp of when the revision is considered expired. If not set, the memory revision will be kept until manually deleted.
---@field disableMemoryRevisions? boolean Optional. Input only. Indicates whether no revision will be created for this request.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMetadataValueMap Optional. Represents user-provided metadata for the Memory. This information was provided when creating, updating, or generating the Memory. It was not generated by Memory Bank.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the ReasoningEngine to create the Memory under. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}`
---@field memoryId? string Optional. The user defined ID to use for memory, which will become the final component of the memory resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9-]`. The first character must be a letter, and the last character must be a letter or number.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsAgentAnomalyDetectionScopesRequest
---@field logBuckets? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Customer-owned Cloud Logging bucket resource names attached to this scope. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/buckets/{bucket}`.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScopeStateEnum|string Output only. The lifecycle state of the scope.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agentAnomalyDetectionScopes/{agent_anomaly_detection_scope}`
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Immutable. Specifies the customer-managed encryption key spec for a Scope. If set, this Scope and all sub-resources will be secured by this key. The key is immutable after the Scope is created and must be a multi-region (`us` or `eu`) key in the same region as the Scope.
---@field displayName? string Optional. User-provided display name of the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope.
---@field autoEnroll? boolean Optional. When true, agents created in Agent Engine that share log and observability buckets with this scope are automatically enrolled as MonitoredAgents. When false, agents must be enrolled explicitly via MonitoredAgent operations.
---@field observabilityBuckets? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Customer-owned Cloud Observability bucket resource names attached to this scope. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/observationBuckets/{observation_bucket}`.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`
---@field agentAnomalyDetectionScopeId? string Required. The ID to use for the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope, which will become the final component of the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope's resource name. This value should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are /[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?/.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsAgentsRequest
---@field created? string Output only. The time the agent was created.
---@field memoryConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentMemoryConfig Optional. Memory settings for the agent.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The metadata for the agent.
---@field effectiveIdentity? string Output only. The resolved Agent Identity (SPIFFE principal) of the agent.
---@field base_agent? string Required. Immutable. The base agent for the agent. Supported values: * `antigravity-preview-05-2026` Immutable: `UpdateAgent` rejects a change, including clearing it. The kind of agent this is gets derived from this field when the agent is created and is recorded then; nothing recomputes it afterwards, so a later change would leave the agent described as one kind and behaving as another. Create a new agent instead.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentModelConfig Optional. Model configuration for the agent. When set, tasks running under this agent default to this model configuration if they do not specify their own.
---@field persona? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Persona Optional. The persona (presentation) of the agent. Mutable: presentation only, not an archetype-derivation signal.
---@field id? string Immutable. The user-specified ID for the agent. This ID becomes the final component of the agent resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. The ID can be up to 63 characters and must match the regular expression `[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?`.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the agent.
---@field agentIdentity? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentIdentity Optional. Immutable. The identity configuration of the agent. Immutable: the agent's own identity determines the A2 (CoWorker) archetype and the minted SPIFFE, so it cannot change after creation (no A1<->A2 transition).
---@field object? string Output only. The object type of the resource. For agents, the value is `agent`.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability settings for this agent's sessions.
---@field updated? string Output only. The time the agent was last updated.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for an Agent. If set, this agent's user data will be secured by this key; if not set, it is secured by a Google-managed key. Cannot be changed after the agent is created.
---@field base_environment? any Optional. The base environment configuration for the agent. Valid types: * A string value for the environment ID, or `remote` for the default. * A struct value for the `environment_config`.
---@field owner? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Principal Optional. The human owner (principal) the agent acts on behalf of (A1 Personal). Mutable by design: ownership is meant to be reassignable (e.g. by an admin). On create an A1 (Personal) agent may omit it and the control plane defaults it to the caller; an A2 (CoWorker) agent must set it explicitly. `owner.id` must be an *obfuscated* Gaia id. A raw Gaia id is rejected with INVALID_ARGUMENT naming the rule -- both forms are strings of decimal digits, so the surface would otherwise have two indistinguishable spellings of one identity. Not yet: `UpdateAgent` currently rejects a change to this field. The control plane authorizes every agent method against the owner Gaia id it persists internally at create time, and the update path does not maintain that copy — so a field write here would move the reported owner without moving the one access control uses. The guard comes out once reassignment moves both, along with the Workspace identity provisioned under the owner.
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentToolList Optional. The tools available to the agent.
---@field aiApplication? string Output only. The resource name of the AI Application provisioned for this agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/aiApplications/{ai_application}`.
---@field system_instruction? string Optional. The instructions for the agent to follow. These instructions are passed to the LLM as a system instruction.
---@field allowedTeammates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AllowedTeammates Optional. The identities this agent is allowed to contact outbound (for example over Gmail or Chat). Stored on the agent and always returned by `GetAgent`; see the field comments on `AllowedTeammates`.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatus Output only. The current operational state of the agent.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the location to create the agent in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsAgentsTasksRequest
---@field summary? string Output only. A rolling, system-generated summary of the task's progress/result.
---@field statusDetail? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetail Output only. Explanation for the current state, when the state alone is not enough to act on (today: `SUSPENDED`). Cleared when the task leaves that state.
---@field scheduleState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskScheduleStateEnum|string Output only. Scheduling lifecycle of a recurring template. Unset unless `spec.schedule.recurring` is set.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEnum|string Output only. The coarse, durable status of the task.
---@field rootTaskId? string Output only. Lineage group key: the root of this task's tree, materialized from `parent_task_id` (a root task's own short-form name). Same short form, and for the same reason, as `parent_task_id`. One `ListTasks(filter: "root_task_id=")` returns the whole tree as a flat, paginated collection, instead of a level-by-level walk that costs one round trip per depth. The client reassembles the tree from `parent_task_id`; a page may therefore contain a task whose parent lands on a later page.
---@field spec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpec Required. The full specification of what to do, how to run it, and how to know it is done.
---@field budgetConsumptionDetail? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BudgetConsumptionDetail Output only. Current budget consumption detail of the Task.
---@field assignedAgentIdentity? string Output only. The resolved Agent Identity (SPIFFE ID) of the `Agent` this task is assigned to. Populated on single-task RPCs (`CreateTask`, `GetTask`, `UpdateTask`, `SuspendTask`, `ResumeTask`, `CancelTask`); not populated by `ListTasks`.
---@field runCount? string Output only. Runs minted so far by a recurring template, so a client can show progress against `RecurringSchedule.max_run_count`.
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Next scheduled firing of a recurring template. Unset once the template is `SCHEDULE_FINISHED`, and for cron-less (event) schedules.
---@field goals? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoalList Output only. Goals of the Task, including both active and completed/failed. A Task may pursue several concurrently active goals .
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the task was created.
---@field assignedAgent? string Output only. The resource name of the `Agent` this task is assigned to, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`. It is derived from the create parent; any value set by the client is ignored.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name of the task.
---@field statusUpdateTime? string Output only. The time the task's status was last updated.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Optional caller-supplied labels. Must follow the unified cloud labels spec (keys/values lowercase `[a-z0-9_-]`, <=63 chars). Stored as-is and returned verbatim on Get/ListTask, so the caller owns what goes in and reads back. Label names starting with `goog-` or `google-` are reserved for predefined labels. Besides user-defined billing/reporting labels, callers may stamp non-PII operational traffic annotations here under the reserved prefix (persisted on the task, so they apply to every turn and survive reconnection). Predefined: `goog-golden-query-id`: stable golden-query / CUJ id (e.g. `hello-world`); absent for organic traffic. Lets per-CUJ latency be trended independently.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the task was last updated.
---@field parentTaskId? string Optional. If this task is a subtask, the parent task's short-form, agent-independent resource name: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tasks/{task} The short form is used here on purpose (NOT the agent-scoped .../agents/{agent}/tasks/{task}): it stays stable when the parent is reassigned to another agent, so subtasks never need rewriting, and the task tree does not imply agent relationships .
---@field title? string Optional. Optional human-readable title for listing surfaces.
---@field parent string Required. The parent agent that owns this task. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}
---@field uniqueCreationToken? string Optional. Optional idempotency token to guarantee the task is created only once. Suggest a UUID. A create carrying a token that a live task of the same agent already holds fails with `ALREADY_EXISTS`, naming that task in the response. The token is free again once that task finishes.
---@field ["userContext.location"]? string Optional. The user's coarse, human-readable location, e.g. "Mountain View, CA, US". Must be no more precise than city level; never send street addresses, postal codes, or coordinates. The agent uses it for location-dependent requests, e.g. weather or nearby places.
---@field ["userContext.channel"]? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsAgentsTasksUserContext_channelEnum|string Optional. How the user's input reached the agent. Leave unset when the user talks to the agent directly in an AI-native interface.
---@field ["userContext.timeZone"]? string Optional. The user's IANA time zone name, e.g. "America/Los_Angeles". The agent uses it to interpret and present dates and times, e.g. to resolve "tomorrow morning".

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsAgentsTasksUserContext_channelEnum "CHANNEL_UNSPECIFIED"|"CHAT"|"EMAIL"

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsBatchPredictionJobsRequest
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob entered any of the following states: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field modelVersionId? string Output only. The version ID of the Model that produces the predictions via this job.
---@field partialFailures? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatusList Output only. Partial failures encountered. For example, single files that can't be read. This field never exceeds 20 entries. Status details fields contain standard Google Cloud error details.
---@field outputConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobOutputConfig Required. The Configuration specifying where output predictions should be written. The schema of any single prediction may be specified as a concatenation of Model's PredictSchemata's instance_schema_uri and prediction_schema_uri.
---@field modelMonitoringConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringConfig Model monitoring config will be used for analysis model behaviors, based on the input and output to the batch prediction job, as well as the provided training dataset.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field explanationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpec Explanation configuration for this BatchPredictionJob. Can be specified only if generate_explanation is set to `true`. This value overrides the value of Model.explanation_spec. All fields of explanation_spec are optional in the request. If a field of the explanation_spec object is not populated, the corresponding field of the Model.explanation_spec object is inherited.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field instanceConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobInstanceConfig Configuration for how to convert batch prediction input instances to the prediction instances that are sent to the Model.
---@field modelMonitoringStatsAnomalies? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringStatsAnomaliesList Get batch prediction job monitoring statistics.
---@field outputInfo? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobOutputInfo Output only. Information further describing the output of this job.
---@field modelParameters? any The parameters that govern the predictions. The schema of the parameters may be specified via the Model's PredictSchemata's parameters_schema_uri.
---@field dedicatedResources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchDedicatedResources The config of resources used by the Model during the batch prediction. If the Model supports DEDICATED_RESOURCES this config may be provided (and the job will use these resources), if the Model doesn't support AUTOMATIC_RESOURCES, this config must be provided.
---@field manualBatchTuningParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ManualBatchTuningParameters Immutable. Parameters configuring the batch behavior. Currently only applicable when dedicated_resources are used (in other cases Vertex AI does the tuning itself).
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob was created.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account that the DeployedModel's container runs as. If not specified, a system generated one will be used, which has minimal permissions and the custom container, if used, may not have enough permission to access other Google Cloud resources. Users deploying the Model must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account.
---@field inputConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobInputConfig Required. Input configuration of the instances on which predictions are performed. The schema of any single instance may be specified via the Model's PredictSchemata's instance_schema_uri.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of this BatchPredictionJob.
---@field resourcesConsumed? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ResourcesConsumed Output only. Information about resources that had been consumed by this job. Provided in real time at best effort basis, as well as a final value once the job completes. Note: This field currently may be not populated for batch predictions that use AutoML Models.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when the job's state is JOB_STATE_FAILED or JOB_STATE_CANCELLED.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the BatchPredictionJob.
---@field model? string The name of the Model resource that produces the predictions via this job, must share the same ancestor Location. Starting this job has no impact on any existing deployments of the Model and their resources. Exactly one of model, unmanaged_container_model, or endpoint must be set. The model resource name may contain version id or version alias to specify the version. Example: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@2` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@golden` if no version is specified, the default version will be deployed. The model resource could also be a publisher model. Example: `publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}`
---@field endpoint? string For Bring-Your-Own-Endpoint (BYOE), the name of the Endpoint resource that produces the predictions via this job, must share the same ancestor Location. Exactly one of model, unmanaged_container_model, or endpoint must be set. Example: `projects/193595526740/locations/us-central1/endpoints/4203439000301600768`
---@field modelMonitoringStatus? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. The running status of the model monitoring pipeline.
---@field unmanagedContainerModel? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1UnmanagedContainerModel Contains model information necessary to perform batch prediction without requiring uploading to model registry. Exactly one of model, unmanaged_container_model, or endpoint must be set.
---@field generateExplanation? boolean Generate explanation with the batch prediction results. When set to `true`, the batch prediction output changes based on the `predictions_format` field of the BatchPredictionJob.output_config object: * `bigquery`: output includes a column named `explanation`. The value is a struct that conforms to the Explanation object. * `jsonl`: The JSON objects on each line include an additional entry keyed `explanation`. The value of the entry is a JSON object that conforms to the Explanation object. * `csv`: Generating explanations for CSV format is not supported. If this field is set to true, either the Model.explanation_spec or explanation_spec must be populated.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize BatchPredictionJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a BatchPredictionJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the BatchPredictionJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchPredictionJobStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field disableContainerLogging? boolean For custom-trained Models and AutoML Tabular Models, the container of the DeployedModel instances will send `stderr` and `stdout` streams to Cloud Logging by default. Please note that the logs incur cost, which are subject to [Cloud Logging pricing](https://cloud.google.com/logging/pricing). User can disable container logging by setting this flag to true.
---@field completionStats? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CompletionStats Output only. Statistics on completed and failed prediction instances.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the BatchPredictionJob was most recently updated.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the BatchPredictionJob in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsCachedContentsRequest
---@field usageMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CachedContentUsageMetadata Output only. Metadata on the usage of the cached content.
---@field name? string Immutable. Identifier. The server-generated resource name of the cached content Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/cachedContents/{cached_content}
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Input only. Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for a `CachedContent`. If set, this `CachedContent` and all its sub-resources will be secured by this key.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Creation time of the cache entry.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. When the cache entry was last updated in UTC time.
---@field model? string Immutable. The name of the `Model` to use for cached content. Currently, only the published Gemini base models are supported, in form of projects/{PROJECT}/locations/{LOCATION}/publishers/google/models/{MODEL}
---@field expireTime? string Timestamp of when this resource is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output, regardless of what was sent on input.
---@field systemInstruction? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Content Optional. Input only. Immutable. Developer set system instruction. Currently, text only
---@field contents? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ContentList Optional. Input only. Immutable. The content to cache
---@field toolConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolConfig Optional. Input only. Immutable. Tool config. This config is shared for all tools
---@field ttl? string Input only. The TTL for this resource. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Immutable. The user-generated meaningful display name of the cached content.
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolList Optional. Input only. Immutable. A list of `Tools` the model may use to generate the next response
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource where the cached content will be created

