---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsReasoningEnginesSandboxEnvironmentsRequest
---@field name? string Identifier. The name of the SandboxEnvironment.
---@field sandboxEnvironmentTemplate? string Optional. The name of the SandboxEnvironmentTemplate specified in the parent Agent Engine resource that this SandboxEnvironment is created from.
---@field latestSandboxEnvironmentSnapshot? string Output only. The resource name of the latest snapshot taken for this SandboxEnvironment.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the SandboxEnvironment.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this SandboxEnvironment was most recently updated.
---@field sandboxEnvironmentSnapshot? string Optional. The resource name of the SandboxEnvironmentSnapshot to use for creating this SandboxEnvironment. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/sandboxEnvironmentSnapshots/{sandbox_environment_snapshot}`
---@field expireTime? string Optional. Timestamp in UTC of when this SandboxEnvironment is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output, regardless of what `expiration` was sent on input.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentStateEnum|string Output only. The runtime state of the SandboxEnvironment.
---@field owner? string Optional. Owner information for this sandbox environment. A Sandbox can only be restored from a snapshot that belongs to the same owner. If not set, sandbox will be created as the default owner.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this SandboxEnvironment was created.
---@field connectionInfo? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentConnectionInfo Output only. The connection information of the SandboxEnvironment.
---@field spec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentSpec Optional. The configuration of the SandboxEnvironment.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. The TTL for the sandbox environment. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the reasoning engine to create the SandboxEnvironment in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}`.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsReasoningEnginesSessionsRequest
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. The TTL for this session. The minimum value is 24 hours.
---@field expireTime? string Optional. Timestamp of when this session is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output, regardless of what was sent on input. The minimum value is 24 hours from the time of creation.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Sessions. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the session was updated.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session.
---@field userId? string Required. Immutable. String id provided by the user
---@field sessionState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Session specific memory which stores key conversation points.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the session. Format: 'projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/sessions/{session}'.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the session was created.
---@field sessionId? string Optional. The user defined ID to use for session, which will become the final component of the session resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9-]`. The first and last characters must be a letter or number.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the location to create the session in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsSchedulesRequest
---@field endTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which no new runs can be scheduled. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either end_time is reached or when scheduled_run_count >= max_run_count. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field cron? string Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) to launch scheduled runs. To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or "TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, "CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *", or "TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *".
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule should schedule the next run. Having a next_run_time in the past means the runs are being started behind schedule.
---@field maxRunCount? string Optional. Maximum run count of the schedule. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either started_run_count >= max_run_count or when end_time is reached. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field maxConcurrentRunCount? string Required. Maximum number of runs that can be started concurrently for this Schedule. This is the limit for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable).
---@field createPipelineJobRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreatePipelineJobRequest Request for PipelineService.CreatePipelineJob. CreatePipelineJobRequest.parent field is required (format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}).
---@field catchUp? boolean Output only. Whether to backfill missed runs when the schedule is resumed from PAUSED state. If set to true, all missed runs will be scheduled. New runs will be scheduled after the backfill is complete. Default to false.
---@field createModelMonitoringJobRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateModelMonitoringJobRequest Request for ModelMonitoringService.CreateModelMonitoringJob.
---@field lastScheduledRunResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleRunResponse Output only. Response of the last scheduled run. This is the response for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable). Unset if no run has been scheduled yet.
---@field maxConcurrentActiveRunCount? string Optional. Specifies the maximum number of active runs that can be executed concurrently for this Schedule. This limits the number of runs that can be in a non-terminal state at the same time. Currently, this field is only supported for requests of type CreatePipelineJobRequest.
---@field startTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which the first run can be scheduled. Default to Schedule create time if not specified.
---@field createNotebookExecutionJobRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateNotebookExecutionJobRequest Request for NotebookService.CreateNotebookExecutionJob.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was updated.
---@field lastPauseTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last paused. Unset if never paused.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleStateEnum|string Output only. The state of this Schedule.
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of the Schedule. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field startedRunCount? string Output only. The number of runs started by this schedule.
---@field lastResumeTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last resumed. Unset if never resumed from pause.
---@field name? string Immutable. The resource name of the Schedule.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was created.
---@field allowQueueing? boolean Optional. Whether new scheduled runs can be queued when max_concurrent_runs limit is reached. If set to true, new runs will be queued instead of skipped. Default to false.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the Schedule in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsSemanticGovernancePoliciesRequest
---@field naturalLanguageConstraint? string Required. The natural language constraint of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field mcpTools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SemanticGovernancePolicyMcpToolList Optional. The McpTools that are affected by this policy.
---@field agentResponseCustomization? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResponseCustomization Optional. Settings for customizing the agent's response to end users when this policy is evaluated, such as messages displayed when the policy denies a request.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this SemanticGovernancePolicy was last updated.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write transactions. If provided, the request will only succeed if the etag matches the current value. Otherwise, an ABORTED error will be returned.
---@field agent? string Required. The name of the agent in Agent Registry that is affected by this policy. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`
---@field dryRun? boolean Optional. If true, this policy is evaluated and its result is reported, but the policy is not enforced: a violation does not block the agent's action. Use this to validate a policy against real traffic before turning enforcement on. Defaults to `false`, meaning the policy is enforced. This setting applies only to this policy. If the SemanticGovernancePolicyEngine for the project is itself in dry run, every policy behaves as dry run regardless of this field.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The user-defined name of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field agentIdentity? string Output only. Represents the principal of the agent, used by the Policy Decision Point (PDP) for governance checks. For more information, see https://docs.cloud.google.com/agent-builder/agent-engine/agent-identity Format: `principal://TRUST_DOMAIN/NAMESPACE/AGENT_NAME` Example: `principal://agents.global.org-ORGANIZATION_ID.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/PROJECT_NUMBER/locations/LOCATION/reasoningEngines/AGENT_ENGINE_ID`
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name of the SemanticGovernancePolicy.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this SemanticGovernancePolicy was created.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location into which to create the SemanticGovernancePolicy. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`
---@field semanticGovernancePolicyId? string Required. The ID to use for the SemanticGovernancePolicy, which will become the final component of the SemanticGovernancePolicy's resource name. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9-]`. The first character cannot be a number or hyphen. The last character must be a letter or a number.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsServingProfilesRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the ServingProfile. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field scope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ServingProfileScopeEnum|string Required. The specific API this ServingProfile applies to.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the ServingProfile was created.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the ServingProfile.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the ServingProfile.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when the ServingProfile was last updated.
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ServingProfileCmekConfig CMEK configuration for the ServingProfile.
---@field servingProfileId? string Required. The ID to use for the ServingProfile, which will become the final component of the ServingProfile's resource name. This value should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are `^[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$`.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the ServingProfile in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsSkillsRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. Provides the display name of the Skill. This should align with `name` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SkillStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the Skill.
---@field skillSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SkillSkillSourceEnum|string Output only. The source of the Skill.
---@field license? string Optional. Specifies the license of the Skill. This should be an SPDX license identifier (e.g., "MIT", "Apache-2.0"). See https://spdx.org/licenses/. This should align with `license` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the Skill. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/skills/{skill}`
---@field sha256? string Output only. The SHA256 checksum of the zipped filesystem.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Skill was created.
---@field zippedFilesystem? string Required. Provides the zipped filesystem of the Skill. This should contain the `SKILL.md` file at the root of the zip and optional directories for scripts, references, and assets. Directory should align with the directory structure specified at https://agentskills.io/specification#directory-structure.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize Skills.
---@field description? string Required. Describes the Skill. Should describe both what the skill does and when to use it. Should include specific keywords that help agents identify relevant tasks. This should align with `description` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field compatibility? string Optional. Specifies the compatibility of the Skill. Indicates environment requirements (intended product, system packages, network access, etc.). This should align with `compatibility` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Skill was most recently updated.
---@field parent string Required. The location to create the Skill in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`
---@field skillId? string Required. The ID to use for the Skill, which will become the final component of the Skill's resource name. If not provided, a system-generated ID will be used. This value must be 1-63 characters. Valid characters are lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens. The first character must be a lowercase letter, and the last character must be a lowercase letter or a number. Specifically, the ID must match the regular expression: `^[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$` See [AIP-122](https://aip.dev/122#resource-id-segments) for more details.

