---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsStudiesTrialsRequest
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the Trial's status changed to `SUCCEEDED` or `INFEASIBLE`.
---@field customJob? string Output only. The CustomJob name linked to the Trial. It's set for a HyperparameterTuningJob's Trial.
---@field id? string Output only. The identifier of the Trial assigned by the service.
---@field measurements? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MeasurementList Output only. A list of measurements that are strictly lexicographically ordered by their induced tuples (steps, elapsed_duration). These are used for early stopping computations.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TrialStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the Trial.
---@field webAccessUris? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Output only. URIs for accessing [interactive shells](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/monitor-debug-interactive-shell) (one URI for each training node). Only available if this trial is part of a HyperparameterTuningJob and the job's trial_job_spec.enable_web_access field is `true`. The keys are names of each node used for the trial; for example, `workerpool0-0` for the primary node, `workerpool1-0` for the first node in the second worker pool, and `workerpool1-1` for the second node in the second worker pool. The values are the URIs for each node's interactive shell.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the Trial was started.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the Trial assigned by the service.
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TrialParameterList Output only. The parameters of the Trial.
---@field clientId? string Output only. The identifier of the client that originally requested this Trial. Each client is identified by a unique client_id. When a client asks for a suggestion, Vertex AI Vizier will assign it a Trial. The client should evaluate the Trial, complete it, and report back to Vertex AI Vizier. If suggestion is asked again by same client_id before the Trial is completed, the same Trial will be returned. Multiple clients with different client_ids can ask for suggestions simultaneously, each of them will get their own Trial.
---@field finalMeasurement? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Measurement Output only. The final measurement containing the objective value.
---@field infeasibleReason? string Output only. A human readable string describing why the Trial is infeasible. This is set only if Trial state is `INFEASIBLE`.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Study to create the Trial in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/studies/{study}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsTaskStoresA2aTaskRecordsRequest
---@field artifacts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordArtifactList Output only. The artifacts produced by the task.
---@field appId? string Optional. Agent application which created the task.
---@field contextId? string Optional. A generic identifier for grouping related tasks (e.g., session_id, workflow_id).
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordStatus Optional. The status of the task, including the state, status message, and timestamp.
---@field purgeTime? string Output only. The purge timestamp of the task.
---@field generation? string Output only. The task generation number.
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. The deletion timestamp of the task.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of the task.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. A flexible key-value map for protocol extensions to attach custom attributes to core data structures.
---@field userId? string Optional. Task owner user ID.
---@field expireTime? string Output only. Timestamp of when this task is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output, and is calculated based on the `update_time` and the `ttl`.
---@field serviceMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Metadata relevant to the A2ATaskRecordService, not the agent to agent communication.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. The TTL (Time To Live) for the task. If not set, the task will expire in 24 hours by default. Valid range: [1 second, 1000 days], at second precision. The `nanos` component MUST be zero; sub-second TTLs are not supported because the task's expiration is persisted at second granularity.
---@field history? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordMessageList Output only. The history of the task messages.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the task. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/taskStores/{task_store}/a2aTaskRecords/{a2a_task_record}`
---@field createTime? string Output only. The creation timestamp of the task.
---@field a2aTaskRecordId? string Optional. The user defined ID to use for the A2ATaskRecord, which will become the final component of the A2ATaskRecord resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9-]`. The first and last characters must be a letter or number. This accepts A2A task IDs such as UUIDs, which may start with a digit.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the TaskStore to create the A2ATaskRecord under. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/taskStores/{task_store}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsExperimentsRequest
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the TensorboardExperiment. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}`
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardExperiment was last updated.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your TensorboardExperiment. Label keys and values cannot be longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Dataset (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with `aiplatform.googleapis.com/` and are immutable. The following system labels exist for each Dataset: * `aiplatform.googleapis.com/dataset_metadata_schema`: output only. Its value is the metadata_schema's title.
---@field source? string Immutable. Source of the TensorboardExperiment. Example: a custom training job.
---@field displayName? string User provided name of this TensorboardExperiment.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardExperiment was created.
---@field description? string Description of this TensorboardExperiment.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Tensorboard to create the TensorboardExperiment in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}`
---@field tensorboardExperimentId? string Required. The ID to use for the Tensorboard experiment, which becomes the final component of the Tensorboard experiment's resource name. This value should be 1-128 characters, and valid characters are `/a-z-/`.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsExperimentsRunsRequest
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardRun was last updated.
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of this TensorboardRun. This value must be unique among all TensorboardRuns belonging to the same parent TensorboardExperiment.
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field description? string Description of this TensorboardRun.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the TensorboardRun. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}/runs/{run}`
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your TensorboardRuns. This field will be used to filter and visualize Runs in the Tensorboard UI. For example, a Vertex AI training job can set a label aiplatform.googleapis.com/training_job_id=xxxxx to all the runs created within that job. An end user can set a label experiment_id=xxxxx for all the runs produced in a Jupyter notebook. These runs can be grouped by a label value and visualized together in the Tensorboard UI. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one TensorboardRun (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this TensorboardRun was created.
---@field tensorboardRunId? string Required. The ID to use for the Tensorboard run, which becomes the final component of the Tensorboard run's resource name. This value should be 1-128 characters, and valid characters are `/a-z-/`.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the TensorboardExperiment to create the TensorboardRun in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsTensorboardsExperimentsRunsTimeSeriesRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of this TensorboardTimeSeries. This value should be unique among all TensorboardTimeSeries resources belonging to the same TensorboardRun resource (parent resource).
