---@field isDefault? boolean Used to indicate if the TensorBoard instance is the default one. Each project & region can have at most one default TensorBoard instance. Creation of a default TensorBoard instance and updating an existing TensorBoard instance to be default will mark all other TensorBoard instances (if any) as non default.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field blobStoragePathPrefix? string Output only. Consumer project Cloud Storage path prefix used to store blob data, which can either be a bucket or directory. Does not end with a '/'.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Tensorboard was last updated.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the Tensorboard in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsTrainingPipelinesRequest
---@field trainingTaskMetadata? any Output only. The metadata information as specified in the training_task_definition's `metadata`. This metadata is an auxiliary runtime and final information about the training task. While the pipeline is running this information is populated only at a best effort basis. Only present if the pipeline's training_task_definition contains `metadata` object.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline was created.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of this TrainingPipeline.
---@field trainingTaskInputs? any Required. The training task's parameter(s), as specified in the training_task_definition's `inputs`.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the TrainingPipeline.
---@field trainingTaskDefinition? string Required. A Google Cloud Storage path to the YAML file that defines the training task which is responsible for producing the model artifact, and may also include additional auxiliary work. The definition files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/trainingjob/definition/. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline was most recently updated.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TrainingPipelineStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the pipeline.
---@field modelId? string Optional. The ID to use for the uploaded Model, which will become the final component of the model resource name. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9_-]`. The first character cannot be a number or hyphen.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when the pipeline's state is `PIPELINE_STATE_FAILED` or `PIPELINE_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize TrainingPipelines. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a TrainingPipeline. If set, this TrainingPipeline will be secured by this key. Note: Model trained by this TrainingPipeline is also secured by this key if model_to_upload is not set separately.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline entered any of the following states: `PIPELINE_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `PIPELINE_STATE_FAILED`, `PIPELINE_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field modelToUpload? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Model Describes the Model that may be uploaded (via ModelService.UploadModel) by this TrainingPipeline. The TrainingPipeline's training_task_definition should make clear whether this Model description should be populated, and if there are any special requirements regarding how it should be filled. If nothing is mentioned in the training_task_definition, then it should be assumed that this field should not be filled and the training task either uploads the Model without a need of this information, or that training task does not support uploading a Model as part of the pipeline. When the Pipeline's state becomes `PIPELINE_STATE_SUCCEEDED` and the trained Model had been uploaded into Vertex AI, then the model_to_upload's resource name is populated. The Model is always uploaded into the Project and Location in which this pipeline is.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the TrainingPipeline for the first time entered the `PIPELINE_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field parentModel? string Optional. When specify this field, the `model_to_upload` will not be uploaded as a new model, instead, it will become a new version of this `parent_model`.
---@field inputDataConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1InputDataConfig Specifies Vertex AI owned input data that may be used for training the Model. The TrainingPipeline's training_task_definition should make clear whether this config is used and if there are any special requirements on how it should be filled. If nothing about this config is mentioned in the training_task_definition, then it should be assumed that the TrainingPipeline does not depend on this configuration.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the Location to create the TrainingPipeline in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsTuningJobsRequest
---@field preferenceOptimizationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationSpec Tuning Spec for Preference Optimization.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field pipelineJob? string Output only. The resource name of the PipelineJob associated with the TuningJob. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/pipelineJobs/{pipeline_job}`.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the TuningJob.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TuningJobStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a TuningJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the TuningJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when job's state is `JOB_STATE_FAILED` or `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob entered any of the following JobStates: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`, `JOB_STATE_EXPIRED`.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob was created.
---@field outputUri? string Optional. Cloud Storage path to the directory where tuning job outputs are written to. This field is only available and required for open source models.
---@field fullFineTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FullFineTuningSpec Tuning Spec for Full Fine Tuning.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field distillationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DistillationSpec Tuning Spec for Distillation.
---@field veoLoraTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1VeoLoraTuningSpec Tuning Spec for Veo LoRA Tuning.
---@field preTunedModel? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreTunedModel The pre-tuned model for continuous tuning.
---@field tuningJobState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TuningJobTuningJobStateEnum|string Output only. The detail state of the tuning job (while the overall `JobState` is running).
---@field tuningJobMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TuningJobMetadata Output only. Tuning Job metadata.
---@field reinforcementTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReinforcementTuningSpec Tuning Spec for Reinforcement Tuning.
---@field evaluateDatasetRuns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluateDatasetRunList Output only. Evaluation runs for the Tuning Job.
---@field tuningDataStats? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TuningDataStats Output only. The tuning data statistics associated with this TuningJob.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. Resource name of a TuningJob. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tuningJobs/{tuning_job}`
---@field experiment? string Output only. The Experiment associated with this TuningJob.
---@field tunedModelDisplayName? string Optional. The display name of the TunedModel. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters. For continuous tuning, tuned_model_display_name will by default use the same display name as the pre-tuned model. If a new display name is provided, the tuning job will create a new model instead of a new version.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account that the tuningJob workload runs as. If not specified, the Vertex AI Secure Fine-Tuned Service Agent in the project will be used. See https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/service-agents#vertex-ai-secure-fine-tuning-service-agent Users starting the pipeline must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account.
---@field partnerModelTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartnerModelTuningSpec Tuning Spec for open sourced and third party Partner models.
---@field baseModel? string The base model that is being tuned. See [Supported models](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model-reference/tuning#supported_models).
---@field veoTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1VeoTuningSpec Tuning Spec for Veo Tuning.
---@field supervisedTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SupervisedTuningSpec Tuning Spec for Supervised Fine Tuning.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the TuningJob was most recently updated.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize TuningJob and generated resources such as Model and Endpoint. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field tunedModel? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TunedModel Output only. The tuned model resources associated with this TuningJob.
---@field gcsMetricsUri? string Output only. The Cloud Storage metrics URI associated with this TuningJob.
---@field customBaseModel? string Optional. The user-provided path to custom model weights. Set this field to tune a custom model. The path must be a Cloud Storage directory that contains the model weights in .safetensors format along with associated model metadata files. If this field is set, the base_model field must still be set to indicate which base model the custom model is derived from. This feature is only available for open source models.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the location to create the tuning job in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateProjectsLocationsVoicesRequest
---@field voice? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiVertexV1beta1Voice Required. The voice to create. `voice.model` is optional; if omitted, the service selects the default voice creation model. Output-only fields on `Voice` (`id`, `key`, `expire_time`, `usage`) are ignored if set.
---@field store? boolean Optional. Whether the created voice is persisted and managed by Google. * When `true`, Google stores the voice and returns `Voice.id` (for example, `voice_abc123def456`), which can be managed via `GetVoice`, `ListVoices`, and `DeleteVoice` and referenced by ID in synthesis requests. Stored voices expire after 1 year of inactivity; using a stored voice in speech synthesis or as a `base_voice` in `CreateVoice` extends its `expire_time`. Projects are subject to a maximum active stored voice quota; exceeding the quota returns `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`. * When `false` (default), the voice is not stored by Google and `Voice.key` (for example, `voicekey_...`) is returned for client-side storage and synthesis. Optional discovery metadata fields on `voice` are not persisted or returned when `store` is `false`. * Required to be `true` when `voice.type` is `"prompted"` (otherwise fails with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`).
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource where this voice will be created. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}` Supported only by the Vertex API.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.CreateReasoningEnginesMemoriesRequest
---@field scope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Required. Immutable. Represents the scope of the Memory. Memories are isolated within their scope. The scope is defined when creating or generating memories. Scope values cannot contain the wildcard character '*'.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was created.
---@field description? string Optional. Represents the description of the Memory.
---@field fact? string Optional. Represents semantic knowledge extracted from the source content.
---@field revisionTtl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for the revision. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field structuredContent? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryStructuredContent Optional. Represents the structured content of the memory.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for this resource. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field topics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryTopicIdList Optional. Represents the Topics of the Memory.
---@field name? string Identifier. Represents the resource name of the Memory. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/memories/{memory}`
---@field memoryType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMemoryTypeEnum|string Optional. Represents the type of the memory. If not set, the `NATURAL_LANGUAGE_COLLECTION` type is used. If `STRUCTURED_COLLECTION` or `STRUCTURED_PROFILE` is used, then `structured_data` must be provided.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Represents the display name of the Memory.
---@field expireTime? string Optional. Represents the timestamp of when this resource is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output when `expiration` is set on input, regardless of whether `expire_time` or `ttl` was provided.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was most recently updated.
---@field context? string Optional. Represents the context of the memory.
---@field revisionLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Represents the labels to apply to the Memory Revision created as a result of this request.
---@field revisionExpireTime? string Optional. Input only. Represents the timestamp of when the revision is considered expired. If not set, the memory revision will be kept until manually deleted.
---@field disableMemoryRevisions? boolean Optional. Input only. Indicates whether no revision will be created for this request.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMetadataValueMap Optional. Represents user-provided metadata for the Memory. This information was provided when creating, updating, or generating the Memory. It was not generated by Memory Bank.
---@field parent string Required. The resource name of the ReasoningEngine to create the Memory under. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}`
---@field memoryId? string Optional. The user defined ID to use for memory, which will become the final component of the memory resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. This value may be up to 63 characters, and valid characters are `[a-z0-9-]`. The first character must be a letter, and the last character must be a letter or number.

