---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DeleteProjectsLocationsAgentsRequest
---@field name string Required. The resource name of the agent to delete. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`.
---@field force? boolean Optional. If true, any `Task` belonging to this agent is deleted along with it. If false or unset and the agent still has at least one `Task`, the request fails with `FAILED_PRECONDITION` and nothing is deleted. This governs `Task` and nothing else. Resources the agent owns but a caller never named -- its AI Application and the tenant project bound to it, its Workspace identity, its service-extension binding -- are torn down with the agent on every delete, whatever this field says.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DeleteProjectsLocationsAgentsTasksRequest
---@field name string Required. The name of the task to delete. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}/tasks/{task}
---@field operateOnSelf? boolean Optional. Whether to skip cascading deletion to all descendant subtasks. Defaults to false (cascades to all descendants by default). Matches google.cloud.aiplatform.master.CancelTaskRequest.operate_on_self. Behavior: UNSET or false ⇒ cascade: delete this task and every non-terminal descendant (gated by Mendel flag sobi_enable_cascading_delete_task; returns FAILED_PRECONDITION when the flag is OFF and the task has non-terminal children). true ⇒ delete this task only. Each descendant deletion signals the runtime for the live-session case (Actor.OnCancel finalizes trajectory + reclaims sandbox VM) before removing the Sobi DB rows, matching the single-DeleteTask contract.

