---Information to read/write to blobstore2.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataBlobstore2Info
---@field readToken? string The blob read token. Needed to read blobs that have not been replicated. Might not be available until the final call.
---@field downloadReadHandle? string Read handle passed from Bigstore -> Scotty for a GCS download. This is a signed, serialized blobstore2.ReadHandle proto which must never be set outside of Bigstore, and is not applicable to non-GCS media downloads.
---@field blobGeneration? string The blob generation id.
---@field uploadFragmentListCreationInfo? string A serialized Object Fragment List Creation Info passed from Bigstore -> Scotty for a GCS upload. This field must never be consumed outside of Bigstore, and is not applicable to non-GCS media uploads.
---@field downloadExternalReadToken? string A serialized External Read Token passed from Bigstore -> Scotty for a GCS download. This field must never be consumed outside of Bigstore, and is not applicable to non-GCS media uploads.
---@field uploadMetadataContainer? string Metadata passed from Blobstore -> Scotty for a new GCS upload. This is a signed, serialized blobstore2.BlobMetadataContainer proto which must never be consumed outside of Bigstore, and is not applicable to non-GCS media uploads.
---@field blobId? string The blob id, e.g., /blobstore/prod/playground/scotty

---A sequence of media data references representing composite data. Introduced to support Bigstore composite objects. For details, visit http://go/bigstore-composites.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia
---@field objectId? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataObjectId Reference to a TI Blob, set if reference_type is BIGSTORE_REF.
---@field referenceType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMediaReferenceTypeEnum Describes what the field reference contains.
---@field blobstore2Info? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataBlobstore2Info Blobstore v2 info, set if reference_type is BLOBSTORE_REF and it refers to a v2 blob.
---@field sha1Hash? string SHA-1 hash for the payload.
---@field inline? string Media data, set if reference_type is INLINE
---@field length? string Size of the data, in bytes
---@field cosmoBinaryReference? string A binary data reference for a media download. Serves as a technology-agnostic binary reference in some Google infrastructure. This value is a serialized storage_cosmo.BinaryReference proto. Storing it as bytes is a hack to get around the fact that the cosmo proto (as well as others it includes) doesn't support JavaScript. This prevents us from including the actual type of this field.
---@field blobRef? string Blobstore v1 reference, set if reference_type is BLOBSTORE_REF This should be the byte representation of a blobstore.BlobRef. Since Blobstore is deprecating v1, use blobstore2_info instead. For now, any v2 blob will also be represented in this field as v1 BlobRef.
---@field md5Hash? string MD5 hash for the payload.
---@field path? string Path to the data, set if reference_type is PATH
---@field crc32cHash? number crc32.c hash for the payload.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMediaList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMediaReferenceTypeEnum "PATH"|"BLOB_REF"|"INLINE"|"BIGSTORE_REF"|"COSMO_BINARY_REFERENCE"

---Detailed Content-Type information from Scotty. The Content-Type of the media will typically be filled in by the header or Scotty's best_guess, but this extended information provides the backend with more information so that it can make a better decision if needed. This is only used on media upload requests from Scotty.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataContentTypeInfo
---@field fromUrlPath? string The content type of the file derived from the file extension of the URL path. The URL path is assumed to represent a file name (which is typically only true for agents that are providing a REST API).
---@field fromFileName? string The content type of the file derived from the file extension of the original file name used by the client.
---@field fromHeader? string The content type of the file as specified in the request headers, multipart headers, or RUPIO start request.
---@field fusionIdDetectionMetadata? string Metadata information from Fusion ID detection. Serialized FusionIdDetectionMetadata proto. Only set if from_fusion_id is set.
---@field fromFusionId? string The content type of the file detected by Fusion ID. go/fusionid
---@field bestGuess? string Scotty's best guess of what the content type of the file is.
---@field fromBytes? string The content type of the file derived by looking at specific bytes (i.e. "magic bytes") of the actual file.

---Backend response for a Diff get checksums response. For details on the Scotty Diff protocol, visit http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffChecksumsResponse
---@field checksumsLocation? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia Exactly one of these fields must be populated. If checksums_location is filled, the server will return the corresponding contents to the user. If object_location is filled, the server will calculate the checksums based on the content there and return that to the user. For details on the format of the checksums, see http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@field objectVersion? string The object version of the object the checksums are being returned for.
---@field objectSizeBytes? string The total size of the server object.
---@field objectLocation? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia If set, calculate the checksums based on the contents and return them to the caller.
---@field chunkSizeBytes? string The chunk size of checksums. Must be a multiple of 256KB.

---Backend response for a Diff download response. For details on the Scotty Diff protocol, visit http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffDownloadResponse
---@field objectLocation? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia The original object location.

---A Diff upload request. For details on the Scotty Diff protocol, visit http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffUploadRequest
---@field checksumsInfo? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia The location of the checksums for the new object. Agents must clone the object located here, as the upload server will delete the contents once a response is received. For details on the format of the checksums, see http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@field objectInfo? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia The location of the new object. Agents must clone the object located here, as the upload server will delete the contents once a response is received.
---@field objectVersion? string The object version of the object that is the base version the incoming diff script will be applied to. This field will always be filled in.

---Backend response for a Diff upload request. For details on the Scotty Diff protocol, visit http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffUploadResponse
---@field objectVersion? string The object version of the object at the server. Must be included in the end notification response. The version in the end notification response must correspond to the new version of the object that is now stored at the server, after the upload.
---@field originalObject? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMedia The location of the original file for a diff upload request. Must be filled in if responding to an upload start notification.

---Backend response for a Diff get version response. For details on the Scotty Diff protocol, visit http://go/scotty-diff-protocol.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffVersionResponse
---@field objectVersion? string The version of the object stored at the server.
---@field objectSizeBytes? string The total size of the server object.

---Parameters specific to media downloads.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDownloadParameters
---@field allowGzipCompression? boolean A boolean to be returned in the response to Scotty. Allows/disallows gzip encoding of the payload content when the server thinks it's advantageous (hence, does not guarantee compression) which allows Scotty to GZip the response to the client.
---@field ignoreRange? boolean Determining whether or not Apiary should skip the inclusion of any Content-Range header on its response to Scotty.

---A reference to data stored on the filesystem, on GFS or in blobstore.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataMedia
---@field contentTypeInfo? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataContentTypeInfo Extended content type information provided for Scotty uploads.
---@field algorithm? string Deprecated, use one of explicit hash type fields instead. Algorithm used for calculating the hash. As of 2011/01/21, "MD5" is the only possible value for this field. New values may be added at any time.
---@field compositeMedia? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataCompositeMediaList A composite media composed of one or more media objects, set if reference_type is COMPOSITE_MEDIA. The media length field must be set to the sum of the lengths of all composite media objects. Note: All composite media must have length specified.
---@field path? string Path to the data, set if reference_type is PATH
---@field isPotentialRetry? boolean |is_potential_retry| is set false only when Scotty is certain that it has not sent the request before. When a client resumes an upload, this field must be set true in agent calls, because Scotty cannot be certain that it has never sent the request before due to potential failure in the session state persistence.
---@field blobRef? string Blobstore v1 reference, set if reference_type is BLOBSTORE_REF This should be the byte representation of a blobstore.BlobRef. Since Blobstore is deprecating v1, use blobstore2_info instead. For now, any v2 blob will also be represented in this field as v1 BlobRef.
---@field md5Hash? string Scotty-provided MD5 hash for an upload.
---@field contentType? string MIME type of the data
---@field diffChecksumsResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffChecksumsResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_CHECKSUMS_RESPONSE.
---@field diffDownloadResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffDownloadResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_DOWNLOAD_RESPONSE.
---@field length? string Size of the data, in bytes
---@field diffVersionResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffVersionResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_VERSION_RESPONSE.
---@field filename? string Original file name
---@field blobstore2Info? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataBlobstore2Info Blobstore v2 info, set if reference_type is BLOBSTORE_REF and it refers to a v2 blob.
---@field hashVerified? boolean For Scotty uploads only. If a user sends a hash code and the backend has requested that Scotty verify the upload against the client hash, Scotty will perform the check on behalf of the backend and will reject it if the hashes don't match. This is set to true if Scotty performed this verification.
---@field diffUploadRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffUploadRequest Set if reference_type is DIFF_UPLOAD_REQUEST.
---@field objectId? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataObjectId Reference to a TI Blob, set if reference_type is BIGSTORE_REF.
---@field referenceType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataMediaReferenceTypeEnum Describes what the field reference contains.
---@field bigstoreObjectRef? string Use object_id instead.
---@field sha256Hash? string Scotty-provided SHA256 hash for an upload.
---@field inline? string Media data, set if reference_type is INLINE
---@field cosmoBinaryReference? string A binary data reference for a media download. Serves as a technology-agnostic binary reference in some Google infrastructure. This value is a serialized storage_cosmo.BinaryReference proto. Storing it as bytes is a hack to get around the fact that the cosmo proto (as well as others it includes) doesn't support JavaScript. This prevents us from including the actual type of this field.
---@field timestamp? string Time at which the media data was last updated, in milliseconds since UNIX epoch
---@field crc32cHash? number For Scotty Uploads: Scotty-provided hashes for uploads For Scotty Downloads: (WARNING: DO NOT USE WITHOUT PERMISSION FROM THE SCOTTY TEAM.) A Hash provided by the agent to be used to verify the data being downloaded. Currently only supported for inline payloads. Further, only crc32c_hash is currently supported.
---@field sha512Hash? string Scotty-provided SHA512 hash for an upload.
---@field sha1Hash? string Scotty-provided SHA1 hash for an upload.
---@field diffUploadResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDiffUploadResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_UPLOAD_RESPONSE.
---@field hash? string Deprecated, use one of explicit hash type fields instead. These two hash related fields will only be populated on Scotty based media uploads and will contain the content of the hash group in the NotificationRequest: http://cs/#google3/blobstore2/api/scotty/service/proto/upload_listener.proto&q=class:Hash Hex encoded hash value of the uploaded media.
---@field mediaId? string Media id to forward to the operation GetMedia. Can be set if reference_type is GET_MEDIA.
---@field token? string A unique fingerprint/version id for the media data
---@field downloadParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataDownloadParameters Parameters for a media download.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataMediaReferenceTypeEnum "PATH"|"BLOB_REF"|"INLINE"|"GET_MEDIA"|"COMPOSITE_MEDIA"|"BIGSTORE_REF"|"DIFF_VERSION_RESPONSE"|"DIFF_CHECKSUMS_RESPONSE"|"DIFF_DOWNLOAD_RESPONSE"|"DIFF_UPLOAD_REQUEST"|"DIFF_UPLOAD_RESPONSE"|"COSMO_BINARY_REFERENCE"|"ARBITRARY_BYTES"

---This is a copy of the tech.blob.ObjectId proto, which could not be used directly here due to transitive closure issues with JavaScript support; see http://b/8801763.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GdataObjectId
---@field objectName? string The name of the object.
---@field bucketName? string The name of the bucket to which this object belongs.
---@field generation? string Generation of the object. Generations are monotonically increasing across writes, allowing them to be be compared to determine which generation is newer. If this is omitted in a request, then you are requesting the live object. See http://go/bigstore-versions

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiArgumentsDelta
---@field arguments? string

