---@field serverExecutedCount? number Of `tool_call_count`, calls dispatched to and run by the server, whether or not they succeeded.
---@field name? string The function name as declared in the request. Set only when `tool_type` is TOOL_TYPE_FUNCTION; empty for all other tool types.
---@field toolType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiInteractionUsageToolCallUsageToolTypeEnum

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiInteractionUsageToolCallUsageList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiInteractionUsageToolCallUsage[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiInteractionUsageToolCallUsageToolTypeEnum "TOOL_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"TOOL_TYPE_FUNCTION"|"TOOL_TYPE_CODE_EXECUTION_PYTHON"|"TOOL_TYPE_CODE_EXECUTION_BASH"|"TOOL_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH_WEB"|"TOOL_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH_IMAGE"|"TOOL_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH_VISUAL"|"TOOL_TYPE_URL_CONTEXT"|"TOOL_TYPE_GOOGLE_MAPS"|"TOOL_TYPE_FILE_SEARCH"|"TOOL_TYPE_TOOL_SEARCH"|"TOOL_TYPE_VIDEO_UNDERSTANDING"

---`ListValue` is a wrapper around a repeated field of values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiListValue
---@field values? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiValueList Repeated field of dynamically typed values.

---Configuration for an environment that lives on the client connection rather than in a server-managed sandbox. When set (via Interaction.local_environment), the agent's filesystem and shell are treated as living on the client: the agent's built-in environment operations (e.g. reading/listing/editing files and running commands) are suspended on the server and yielded back to the client to execute, with their results returned on a subsequent turn. This is mutually exclusive with a server-managed `EnvironmentConfig` (remote_environment), since the environment is either on the client or in a server sandbox, never both. This governs only the agent's built-in environment. Client-declared function tools are always executed on the client regardless of this field.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiLocalEnvironmentConfig

