---Message that represents an arbitrary HTTP body. It should only be used for payload formats that can't be represented as JSON, such as raw binary or an HTML page. This message can be used both in streaming and non-streaming API methods in the request as well as the response. It can be used as a top-level request field, which is convenient if one wants to extract parameters from either the URL or HTTP template into the request fields and also want access to the raw HTTP body. Example: message GetResourceRequest { // A unique request id. string request_id = 1; // The raw HTTP body is bound to this field. google.api.HttpBody http_body = 2; } service ResourceService { rpc GetResource(GetResourceRequest) returns (google.api.HttpBody); rpc UpdateResource(google.api.HttpBody) returns (google.protobuf.Empty); } Example with streaming methods: service CaldavService { rpc GetCalendar(stream google.api.HttpBody) returns (stream google.api.HttpBody); rpc UpdateCalendar(stream google.api.HttpBody) returns (stream google.api.HttpBody); } Use of this type only changes how the request and response bodies are handled, all other features will continue to work unchanged.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleApiHttpBody
---@field data? string The HTTP request/response body as raw binary.
---@field contentType? string The HTTP Content-Type header value specifying the content type of the body.
---@field extensions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMapList Application specific response metadata. Must be set in the first response for streaming APIs.

---A single part of a message or artifact. A part carries exactly one kind of content.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2APart
---@field text? string Optional. Textual content.
---@field mediaType? string Optional. The IANA media type of the content, e.g. "text/plain" or "image/png".
---@field raw? string Optional. Raw binary content.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Additional context or parameters related to the part. Extensions can be used to strongly type metadata values for specific use cases.
---@field filename? string Optional. The name of the file, when the part represents a file.
---@field url? string Optional. A URL pointing to the content.
---@field data? any Optional. Arbitrary data content.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2APartList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2APart[]

---An A2ATaskRecord represents an A2ATask (unit of work) persisted in storage.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecord
---@field artifacts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordArtifactList Output only. The artifacts produced by the task.
---@field appId? string Optional. Agent application which created the task.
---@field contextId? string Optional. A generic identifier for grouping related tasks (e.g., session_id, workflow_id).
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordStatus Optional. The status of the task, including the state, status message, and timestamp.
---@field purgeTime? string Output only. The purge timestamp of the task.
---@field generation? string Output only. The task generation number.
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. The deletion timestamp of the task.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of the task.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. A flexible key-value map for protocol extensions to attach custom attributes to core data structures.
---@field userId? string Optional. Task owner user ID.
---@field expireTime? string Output only. Timestamp of when this task is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output, and is calculated based on the `update_time` and the `ttl`.
---@field serviceMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Metadata relevant to the A2ATaskRecordService, not the agent to agent communication.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. The TTL (Time To Live) for the task. If not set, the task will expire in 24 hours by default. Valid range: [1 second, 1000 days], at second precision. The `nanos` component MUST be zero; sub-second TTLs are not supported because the task's expiration is persisted at second granularity.
---@field history? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordMessageList Output only. The history of the task messages.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the task. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/taskStores/{task_store}/a2aTaskRecords/{a2a_task_record}`
