---A Vertex agent contains instructions and configurations for the LLM to execute a certain task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Agent
---@field created? string Output only. The time the agent was created.
---@field memoryConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentMemoryConfig Optional. Memory settings for the agent.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The metadata for the agent.
---@field effectiveIdentity? string Output only. The resolved Agent Identity (SPIFFE principal) of the agent.
---@field base_agent? string Required. Immutable. The base agent for the agent. Supported values: * `antigravity-preview-05-2026` Immutable: `UpdateAgent` rejects a change, including clearing it. The kind of agent this is gets derived from this field when the agent is created and is recorded then; nothing recomputes it afterwards, so a later change would leave the agent described as one kind and behaving as another. Create a new agent instead.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentModelConfig Optional. Model configuration for the agent. When set, tasks running under this agent default to this model configuration if they do not specify their own.
---@field persona? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Persona Optional. The persona (presentation) of the agent. Mutable: presentation only, not an archetype-derivation signal.
---@field id? string Immutable. The user-specified ID for the agent. This ID becomes the final component of the agent resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. The ID can be up to 63 characters and must match the regular expression `[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?`.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the agent.
---@field agentIdentity? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentIdentity Optional. Immutable. The identity configuration of the agent. Immutable: the agent's own identity determines the A2 (CoWorker) archetype and the minted SPIFFE, so it cannot change after creation (no A1<->A2 transition).
---@field object? string Output only. The object type of the resource. For agents, the value is `agent`.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability settings for this agent's sessions.
---@field updated? string Output only. The time the agent was last updated.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for an Agent. If set, this agent's user data will be secured by this key; if not set, it is secured by a Google-managed key. Cannot be changed after the agent is created.
---@field base_environment? any Optional. The base environment configuration for the agent. Valid types: * A string value for the environment ID, or `remote` for the default. * A struct value for the `environment_config`.
---@field owner? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Principal Optional. The human owner (principal) the agent acts on behalf of (A1 Personal). Mutable by design: ownership is meant to be reassignable (e.g. by an admin). On create an A1 (Personal) agent may omit it and the control plane defaults it to the caller; an A2 (CoWorker) agent must set it explicitly. `owner.id` must be an *obfuscated* Gaia id. A raw Gaia id is rejected with INVALID_ARGUMENT naming the rule -- both forms are strings of decimal digits, so the surface would otherwise have two indistinguishable spellings of one identity. Not yet: `UpdateAgent` currently rejects a change to this field. The control plane authorizes every agent method against the owner Gaia id it persists internally at create time, and the update path does not maintain that copy — so a field write here would move the reported owner without moving the one access control uses. The guard comes out once reassignment moves both, along with the Workspace identity provisioned under the owner.
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentToolList Optional. The tools available to the agent.
---@field aiApplication? string Output only. The resource name of the AI Application provisioned for this agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/aiApplications/{ai_application}`.
---@field system_instruction? string Optional. The instructions for the agent to follow. These instructions are passed to the LLM as a system instruction.
---@field allowedTeammates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AllowedTeammates Optional. The identities this agent is allowed to contact outbound (for example over Gmail or Chat). Stored on the agent and always returned by `GetAgent`; see the field comments on `AllowedTeammates`.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatus Output only. The current operational state of the agent.

---Represents an Agent Anomaly Detection Scope.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScope
---@field logBuckets? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Customer-owned Cloud Logging bucket resource names attached to this scope. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/buckets/{bucket}`.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScopeStateEnum Output only. The lifecycle state of the scope.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agentAnomalyDetectionScopes/{agent_anomaly_detection_scope}`
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Immutable. Specifies the customer-managed encryption key spec for a Scope. If set, this Scope and all sub-resources will be secured by this key. The key is immutable after the Scope is created and must be a multi-region (`us` or `eu`) key in the same region as the Scope.
---@field displayName? string Optional. User-provided display name of the AgentAnomalyDetectionScope.
---@field autoEnroll? boolean Optional. When true, agents created in Agent Engine that share log and observability buckets with this scope are automatically enrolled as MonitoredAgents. When false, agents must be enrolled explicitly via MonitoredAgent operations.
---@field observabilityBuckets? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Customer-owned Cloud Observability bucket resource names attached to this scope. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/observationBuckets/{observation_bucket}`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScopeList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScope[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScopeStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CREATING"|"ACTIVE"|"DELETING"|"FAILED"|"UPDATING"

---Represents configuration for an Agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentConfig
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolList Optional. The list of tools available to this agent.
---@field agentId? string Required. Unique identifier of the agent. This ID is used to refer to this agent, e.g., in AgentEvent.author, or in the `sub_agents` field. It must be unique within the `agents` map.
---@field instruction? string Optional. Provides instructions for the LLM model, guiding the agent's behavior. Can be static or dynamic. Dynamic instructions can contain placeholders like {variable_name} that will be resolved at runtime using the `AgentEvent.state_delta` field.
---@field agentType? string Optional. The type or class of the agent (e.g., "LlmAgent", "RouterAgent", "ToolUseAgent"). Useful for the autorater to understand the expected behavior of the agent.
---@field description? string Optional. A high-level description of the agent's role and responsibilities. Critical for evaluating if the agent is routing tasks correctly.
---@field subAgents? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The list of valid agent IDs that this agent can delegate to. This defines the directed edges in the multi-agent system graph topology.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentConfigMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentConfig }

---Represents data specific to multi-turn agent evaluations.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentData
---@field agents? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentConfigMap Optional. A map containing the static configurations for each agent in the system. Key: agent_id (matches the `author` field in events). Value: The static configuration of the agent.
---@field turns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ConversationTurnList Optional. A chronological list of conversation turns. Each turn represents a logical execution cycle (e.g., User Input -> Agent Response).

---Represents a single event in the execution trace.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentEvent
---@field activeTools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolList Optional. The list of tools that were active/available to the agent at the time of this event. This overrides the `AgentConfig.tools` if set.
---@field author? string Required. The ID of the agent or entity that generated this event. Use "user" to denote events generated by the end-user.
---@field content? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Content Required. The content of the event (e.g., text response, tool call, tool response).
---@field stateDelta? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. The change in the session state caused by this event. This is a key-value map of fields that were modified or added by the event.
---@field eventTime? string Optional. The timestamp when the event occurred.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentEventList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentEvent[]

---Identity configuration for an agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentIdentity
---@field email? string Optional. The email address representing the agent's principal identity. For Google Workspace agents, the email should be on a verified customer domain.
---@field gaiaId? string Output only. The agent's own obfuscated Gaia id. Set only for an A2 (CoWorker) agent, which is the only kind that has a first-class Gaia account of its own. An A1 (Personal) agent has no `AgentIdentity` at all: it acts on behalf of its owner, so the identity it runs as is `Agent.owner`, and there is no separate Gaia account to name. Populated asynchronously once the agent identity is provisioned, so it may be absent from the `CreateAgent` LRO response and present on `GetAgent`/`ListAgents`.
---@field tenant? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Tenant Optional. The tenant / customer context under which this agent runs. For Google Workspace , this is the obfuscated Customer ID (e.g. "C0123abcd").

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Agent[]

---Agent-level memory settings. These apply across every task the agent runs and every user of the agent: this is an agent-wide control, not a per-user one. To turn memory off for a single end user of a shared agent, the calling surface sets `TaskSpec.scope.memory_config.disable_memory` on that user's tasks.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentMemoryConfig
---@field disableMemory? boolean Optional. If true, memory is disabled for the agent as a whole: across every task it runs, the agent neither reads existing memories into the prompt nor forms new ones. Memory is on by default, and this is the setting that wins. A task may turn memory off for itself alone with `TaskSpec.scope.memory_config.disable_memory`, but cannot turn it back on while this is true; the two are OR'ed. This level wins because it is the mutable one. Turning it on has to cover the tasks that already exist, whose stored specs still say whatever they were created with, so the agent's current value is re-applied every time a session opens, including on a resume. Memories already stored are retained and stay readable by the agent's users; this governs only whether the agent can access and modify them.

---Selects the model configuration for an agent. Starts with just the model id/alias; extensible with further model parameters without a breaking change.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentModelConfig
---@field model? string Optional. Publisher model resource name (an `aiplatform.googleapis.com/PublisherModel`) of the form "publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}", e.g. "publishers/anthropic/models/claude-opus-4-8" or "publishers/google/models/gemini-3-flash". Empty means the agent's default gemini model.
---@field temperature? number Optional. Sampling temperature for the model's generation config (valid range (0.0, 2.0]); a value outside that range leaves the backend default standing.

---Defines the identity of an agent being monitored.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResource
---@field agentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResourceAgentTypeEnum Required. The runtime type of the agent.
---@field agent? string Required. The resource name or identifier of the agent to monitor. The format depends on `agent_type`: * `REASONING_ENGINE`: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}` * `CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE`, `GKE_WORKLOAD`, `GCE_INSTANCE`: the resource name of the agent's runtime. * `AGENT_TYPE_OTHER`: a stable identifier for the agent.
---@field location? string Output only. The Google Cloud location (region) of the agent resource (for example, `us-central1`).
---@field agentFramework? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResourceAgentFrameworkEnum Optional. The framework used to build the agent, orthogonal to the runtime `agent_type`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResourceAgentFrameworkEnum "AGENT_FRAMEWORK_UNSPECIFIED"|"ADK"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResourceAgentTypeEnum "AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"REASONING_ENGINE"|"CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE"|"GKE_WORKLOAD"|"GCE_INSTANCE"|"AGENT_TYPE_OTHER"

---Customizes the agent's response to the end user when a `SemanticGovernancePolicy` is evaluated (for example, with a custom message shown on denial).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentResponseCustomization
---@field denialMessage? string Optional. Custom message shown to the end user when the policy check results in a denial. Use this to explain the rationale to the user. Max 1000 characters.

---Operational state of the agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatus
---@field suspensionReason? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatusSuspensionReason Output only. Context about the current active suspension.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatusStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of the agent.
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. The time at which the agent was soft-deleted.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatusStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"SUSPENDED"|"ARCHIVED"|"DELETED"

---Details about the active suspension. This message is only populated if the state is SUSPENDED.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatusSuspensionReason
---@field reason? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatusSuspensionReasonReasonEnum|string Output only. The reason for the current suspension.
---@field suspensionTime? string Output only. The time when the current suspension was applied.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatusSuspensionReasonReasonEnum "REASON_UNSPECIFIED"|"ABUSE"|"ADMIN"|"USER_INITIATED"

---A tool provides a list of actions available to the Agent during the process of executing a task. Example JSON for an MCP server tool: { "type": "mcp_server", "name": "my-mcp-server", "url": "https://api.example.com/mcp", "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer token123" } }
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentTool
---@field name? string Optional. The tool's Google Cloud resource name, used to resolve the tool. Applicable when `type` is `mcp_server` or `endpoint` (a tool registered in Agent Registry), for example `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/.../mcpServers/{id}` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/.../endpoints/{id}`.
---@field type? string Required. The type of the tool. Supported types: * `audio_generation` * `code_execution` * `endpoint` * `filesystem` * `google_search` * `image_generation` * `mcp_server` * `speech_generation` * `url_context` * `video_generation`
---@field headers? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The headers for the MCP server, such as for authentication. Only applicable when `type` is `mcp_server`.
---@field url? string Optional. Fallback for the tool's runtime reference, consumed by `CreateAgent` to create the downstream AI App. Applicable when `type` is `mcp_server` or `endpoint`, and optional: the Agent service derives the runtime reference from `name` via Agent Registry (`GetMcpServer` / `GetEndpoint`), and reads this only when that lookup yields none.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentToolList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentTool[]

---Contains aggregated AnalyzedSession statistics, grouped by MonitoredAgent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponse
---@field agentAggregates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregateList Aggregated statistics — exactly one entry per unique MonitoredAgent matched by the request.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token, which can be sent as `page_token` to retrieve the next page. If this field is omitted, there are no subsequent pages.
---@field summary? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ListAnalyzedSessionsResponseViewSummary Overall summary across every MonitoredAgent included in the response.

---Contains aggregated statistics for one MonitoredAgent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregate
---@field monitoredAgent? string The MonitoredAgent resource name. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/monitoredAgents/{monitored_agent}`
---@field latestSessionTime? string The latest session update_time observed for this agent.
---@field agentResourceName? string The resource name or identifier of the agent. Matches `AgentResource.agent` on the corresponding `MonitoredAgent`, so the format depends on that agent's `AgentResource.agent_type`: * `REASONING_ENGINE`: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}` * `CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE`, `GKE_WORKLOAD`, `GCE_INSTANCE`: the resource name of the agent's runtime. * `AGENT_TYPE_OTHER`: a stable identifier for the agent.
---@field agentDisplayName? string Output only. The human-readable display name of the MonitoredAgent.
---@field agentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregateAgentTypeEnum Output only. The runtime the agent is hosted on (for example, `CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE`). `AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED` means the runtime is unknown to this service, which is distinct from `AGENT_TYPE_OTHER` (known, and not one of the enumerated Google Cloud runtimes).
---@field agentStatus? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregateAgentStatusEnum Output only. The enablement state of the MonitoredAgent (for example, ACTIVE, DISABLED, or ENABLING).
---@field severities? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummaryMap Map of severity level (string representation of Severity) to detector summaries aggregated across all sessions for this agent. The key is the string representation of Severity enum: "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED", "SEVERITY_CRITICAL", "SEVERITY_HIGH", "SEVERITY_MEDIUM", "SEVERITY_LOW".
---@field location? string Output only. The Google Cloud location (region) of the agent (for example, `us-central1`). Empty when the agent is not enrolled or its location is unknown.
---@field totalSessionsCount? number The number of analyzed sessions for this agent matched by the request.
---@field anomalousSessionsCount? number The number of anomalous (SESSION_STATE_FLAGGED) sessions for this agent.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregateAgentStatusEnum "ENABLEMENT_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"ENABLING"|"DISABLED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregateAgentTypeEnum "AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"REASONING_ENGINE"|"CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE"|"GKE_WORKLOAD"|"GCE_INSTANCE"|"AGENT_TYPE_OTHER"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregateList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponseAgentAggregate[]

---The aggregation result for the entire dataset and all metrics.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationOutput
---@field aggregationResults? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationResultList One AggregationResult per metric.
---@field dataset? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationDataset The dataset used for evaluation & aggregation.

---The aggregation result for a single metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationResult
---@field aggregationMetric? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationResultAggregationMetricEnum|string Aggregation metric.
---@field rougeMetricValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeMetricValue Results for rouge metric.
---@field bleuMetricValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BleuMetricValue Results for bleu metric.
---@field customCodeExecutionResult? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomCodeExecutionResult Result for code execution metric.
---@field pointwiseMetricResult? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricResult Result for pointwise metric.
---@field pairwiseMetricResult? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PairwiseMetricResult Result for pairwise metric.
---@field exactMatchMetricValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchMetricValue Results for exact match metric.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationResultAggregationMetricEnum "AGGREGATION_METRIC_UNSPECIFIED"|"AVERAGE"|"MODE"|"STANDARD_DEVIATION"|"VARIANCE"|"MINIMUM"|"MAXIMUM"|"MEDIAN"|"PERCENTILE_P90"|"PERCENTILE_P95"|"PERCENTILE_P99"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationResultList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AggregationResult[]

---The set of identities an agent is allowed to contact outbound -- who the agent may talk to, not who may talk to the agent (that is IAM's job). The membership is stored on the agent, so the Agents API is authoritative for what this field reports.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AllowedTeammates
---@field teammates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TeammateList Optional. The teammates the agent is permitted to contact. At most 500. OUTPUT: always returned. An empty list means the agent has no teammates, not that the field went unread. INPUT: the complete desired set, not a delta -- teammates absent from it are removed. The backing roster is updated asynchronously and best-effort after the write returns, so it may briefly lag what `GetAgent` reports. What the agent is actually able to reach follows the roster, not this field, until the two converge.

---Represents an analyzed invocation for a monitored agent's session.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedInvocation
---@field assessment? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Assessment Output only. The assessment of the invocation.
---@field invocationId? string Output only. The invocation ID.
---@field invocationState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedInvocationInvocationStateEnum Output only. The state of the invocation.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the AnalyzedInvocation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedInvocationInvocationStateEnum "INVOCATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INVOCATION_STATE_ANOMALOUS"|"INVOCATION_STATE_NOT_ANOMALOUS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedInvocationList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedInvocation[]

---Represents an analyzed session for a monitored agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSession
---@field sessionState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSessionStateEnum Output only. The state of the session.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The creation time of the session.
---@field agentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionAgentTypeEnum Output only. The runtime that the agent which ran this session is hosted on (for example, `CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE`). `AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED` means the runtime is unknown to this service -- the agent is not enrolled as a `MonitoredAgent`, or was enrolled before its runtime was recorded. That is distinct from `AGENT_TYPE_OTHER`, which means the runtime is known and is not one of the enumerated Google Cloud runtimes.
---@field severities? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummaryMap Output only. Map of severity counts for listing analyzed sessions. The key is the string representation of Severity. Populated in BASIC view only.
---@field agentState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionAgentStateEnum Output only. The current enablement state of the MonitoredAgent that owns this session (for example, ACTIVE, DISABLED, or ENABLING). Defaults to ENABLEMENT_STATE_UNSPECIFIED when the agent is not enrolled or its state is unknown.
---@field location? string Output only. The Google Cloud location (region) of the agent that ran this session (for example, `us-central1`). Empty when the agent is not enrolled or its location is unknown.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the AnalyzedSession.
---@field sessionId? string Output only. The session ID.
---@field agentResourceName? string Output only. The resource name or identifier of the agent that ran this session. Matches `AgentResource.agent` on the corresponding `MonitoredAgent`, so the format depends on that agent's `AgentResource.agent_type`: * `REASONING_ENGINE`: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}` * `CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE`, `GKE_WORKLOAD`, `GCE_INSTANCE`: the resource name of the agent's runtime. * `AGENT_TYPE_OTHER`: a stable identifier for the agent.
---@field assessment? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Assessment Output only. Overall security assessment. Populated only in FULL view.
---@field userId? string Output only. The user ID.
---@field agentDisplayName? string Output only. The human-readable display name of the MonitoredAgent that owns this session. May be empty when the session's agent is not enrolled as a MonitoredAgent; the `agent_resource_name` is always present and can be used as a fallback identifier.
---@field latestAnalyzedTime? string Output only. The latest analyzed time of the session.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionAgentStateEnum "ENABLEMENT_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"ENABLING"|"DISABLED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionAgentTypeEnum "AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"REASONING_ENGINE"|"CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE"|"GKE_WORKLOAD"|"GCE_INSTANCE"|"AGENT_TYPE_OTHER"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSession[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSessionStateEnum "SESSION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SESSION_STATE_UNANALYZED"|"SESSION_STATE_NOT_FLAGGED"|"SESSION_STATE_FLAGGED"|"SESSION_STATE_LLM_UNFLAGGED"

---Breaks down anomalies by severity.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummary
---@field severityLevel? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummarySeverityLevelEnum The severity level of the detector.
---@field sessionsCount? number Output only. The number of distinct sessions whose maximum severity equals `severity_level`. Each session is counted in exactly one bucket (its highest severity). Scope depends on where this appears: a global count on `AggregateAnalyzedSessionsResponse.summary`, per-agent on `agent_aggregates` entries, and page-scoped on `ListAnalyzedSessionsResponse`.
---@field detectorDisplayNames? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Output only. The display names of the customer-defined detectors in `detector_ids`, keyed by detector ID. A detector ID with no entry -- a Google-managed detector, or a customer-defined detector that has since been deleted -- has no display name.
---@field detectorIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList The list of detectors summaries for this severity level.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummaryMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummary }

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnalyzedSessionSeveritySummarySeverityLevelEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEVERITY_LOW"|"SEVERITY_MEDIUM"|"SEVERITY_HIGH"|"SEVERITY_CRITICAL"

---Used to assign specific AnnotationSpec to a particular area of a DataItem or the whole part of the DataItem.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Annotation
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Annotation was last updated.
---@field payload? any Required. The schema of the payload can be found in payload_schema.
---@field payloadSchemaUri? string Required. Google Cloud Storage URI points to a YAML file describing payload. The schema is defined as an [OpenAPI 3.0.2 Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). The schema files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/dataset/annotation/, note that the chosen schema must be consistent with the parent Dataset's metadata.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the Annotation.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Annotations. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Annotation(System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable. Following system labels exist for each Annotation: * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/annotation_set_name": optional, name of the UI's annotation set this Annotation belongs to. If not set, the Annotation is not visible in the UI. * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/payload_schema": output only, its value is the payload_schema's title.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field annotationSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1UserActionReference Output only. The source of the Annotation.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Annotation was created.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnnotationList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Annotation[]

---Identifies a concept with which DataItems may be annotated with.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnnotationSpec
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when AnnotationSpec was last updated.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this AnnotationSpec was created.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the AnnotationSpec. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the AnnotationSpec.

---The generic reusable api auth config. Deprecated. Please use AuthConfig (google/cloud/aiplatform/master/auth.proto) instead.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ApiAuth
---@field apiKeyConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ApiAuthApiKeyConfig The API secret.

---The API secret.
