---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AppendEventResponse

---Instance of a general artifact.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Artifact
---@field schemaVersion? string The version of the schema in schema_name to use. Schema title and version is expected to be registered in earlier Create Schema calls. And both are used together as unique identifiers to identify schemas within the local metadata store.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Artifacts. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Artifact (System labels are excluded).
---@field etag? string An eTag used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Properties of the Artifact. Top level metadata keys' heading and trailing spaces will be trimmed. The size of this field should not exceed 200KB.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Artifact was created.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ArtifactStateEnum|string The state of this Artifact. This is a property of the Artifact, and does not imply or capture any ongoing process. This property is managed by clients (such as Vertex AI Pipelines), and the system does not prescribe or check the validity of state transitions.
---@field displayName? string User provided display name of the Artifact. May be up to 128 Unicode characters.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the Artifact.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Artifact was last updated.
---@field schemaTitle? string The title of the schema describing the metadata. Schema title and version is expected to be registered in earlier Create Schema calls. And both are used together as unique identifiers to identify schemas within the local metadata store.
---@field uri? string The uniform resource identifier of the artifact file. May be empty if there is no actual artifact file.
---@field description? string Description of the Artifact

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ArtifactList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Artifact[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ArtifactStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PENDING"|"LIVE"

---The definition of a artifact type in MLMD.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ArtifactTypeSchema
---@field instanceSchema? string Contains a raw YAML string, describing the format of the properties of the type.
---@field schemaVersion? string The schema version of the artifact. If the value is not set, it defaults to the latest version in the system.
---@field schemaUri? string Points to a YAML file stored on Cloud Storage describing the format. Deprecated. Use PipelineArtifactTypeSchema.schema_title or PipelineArtifactTypeSchema.instance_schema instead.
---@field schemaTitle? string The name of the type. The format of the title must be: `.`. Examples: - `aiplatform.Model` - `acme.CustomModel` When this field is set, the type must be pre-registered in the MLMD store.

