---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateTensorboardTimeSeriesRequest
---@field parent? string Required. The resource name of the TensorboardRun to create the TensorboardTimeSeries in. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}/experiments/{experiment}/runs/{run}`
---@field tensorboardTimeSeriesId? string Optional. The user specified unique ID to use for the TensorboardTimeSeries, which becomes the final component of the TensorboardTimeSeries's resource name. This value should match "a-z0-9{0, 127}"
---@field tensorboardTimeSeries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TensorboardTimeSeries Required. The TensorboardTimeSeries to create.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateTensorboardTimeSeriesRequestList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateTensorboardTimeSeriesRequest[]

---A recurring cron trigger.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CronSchedule
---@field timeZone? string Optional. Optional IANA time zone name, e.g. "America/Los_Angeles". Defaults to UTC.
---@field expression? string Required. The cron expression, e.g. "0 8 * * MON-FRI". Any field may also be `?` or `?/step` to let the service pick the value, so that schedules do not all fire at the same moment: `?` picks one value in the field's range, and `?/step` picks a start within the first step and repeats every step from there. The pick is made once, when the schedule is created or updated, and the expression is stored with the picked values in place of `?` (e.g. "?/30 * * * *" is stored as "17-59/30 * * * *"); sending a `?` again picks new values.

---The storage details for CSV output content.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CsvDestination
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination Required. Google Cloud Storage location.

---The storage details for CSV input content.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CsvSource
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource Required. Google Cloud Storage location.

---Result for custom code execution metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomCodeExecutionResult
---@field score? number Output only. Custom code execution score.

---Specificies a metric that is populated by evaluating user-defined Python code.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomCodeExecutionSpec
---@field codeExecutionRegion? string Optional. The region to use for code execution. If set, the Code Execution Sandbox will be invoked in the specified region regardless of the request's originating region. Must be a region where the Code Execution Sandbox is available. For the current list of [supported regions](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/agent-engine/locations). If unset, the request's originating region is used; requests from regions where the sandbox is unavailable will fail with UNIMPLEMENTED.
---@field evaluationFunction? string Required. Python function. Expected user to define the following function, e.g.: def evaluate(instance: dict[str, Any]) -> float: Please include this function signature in the code snippet. Instance is the evaluation instance, any fields populated in the instance are available to the function as instance[field_name]. Example: Example input: ``` instance= EvaluationInstance( response=EvaluationInstance.InstanceData(text="The answer is 4."), reference=EvaluationInstance.InstanceData(text="4") ) ``` Example converted input: ``` { 'response': {'text': 'The answer is 4.'}, 'reference': {'text': '4'} } ``` Example python function: ``` def evaluate(instance: dict[str, Any]) -> float: if instance'response' == instance'reference': return 1.0 return 0.0 ``` CustomCodeExecutionSpec is also supported in Batch Evaluation (EvalDataset RPC) and Tuning Evaluation. Each line in the input jsonl file will be converted to dict[str, Any] and passed to the evaluation function.

---The detection logic of a customer-defined detector: deterministic Filters, an LLM-evaluated AnomalyAnalysis, or both. At least one must be set.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfig
---@field filterCombination? string Optional. How the entries in `filters` combine, as a join over their 1-based positions, for example "1 AND 2" or "1 OR 2 OR 3". The operators are uppercase "AND" and "OR", and each level uses only one of them. To combine both, put one inside parentheses, as in "(1 AND 2) OR 3". Parentheses nest at most one level, and every filter must appear. Required when `filters` holds more than one entry, and validated whenever set.
---@field anomalyAnalysis? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigAnomalyAnalysis Optional. The anomaly criterion evaluated by an LLM against the sessions the filters admitted, or against every session when no filter is set.
---@field filters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterList Optional. Deterministic predicates a session must satisfy. At most five.

---A customer-authored description of the anomaly to detect, evaluated by an LLM.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigAnomalyAnalysis
---@field prompt? string Required. What the detector should flag, written as a description of the anomaly rather than as instructions to the model. Evaluated against each session's transcript.

---One deterministic predicate over a session: `(field, operation, value)`. A config may carry several; `CustomDetectorConfig.filter_combination` says how they join.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilter
---@field operation? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterOperation Required. How `field` is compared against `value`.
---@field dataType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterDataTypeEnum|string Optional. How to interpret the field and value. Required for TOOL_CALL_ARGS and TOOL_CALL_RESPONSE, whose underlying values are untyped; must be unset for every other field type, whose type the field itself determines.
---@field value? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterValue Required. The literal compared against `field`.
---@field field? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterField Required. What the filter observes.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterDataTypeEnum "DATA_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"BOOL"

---What the filter observes.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterField
---@field qualifiers? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterFieldQualifiers Optional. Additional context for `type`.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterFieldTypeEnum|string Required. The observable property.

---Additional context for a field type. One shared message covers every type; which members are required, optional, or rejected depends on `type`, and is validated on write.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterFieldQualifiers
---@field toolName? string Optional. The tool this field refers to. Required for TOOL_CALL_COUNT, TOOL_CALL_ARGS and TOOL_CALL_RESPONSE; enforced on write.
---@field toolParameterName? string Optional. The tool parameter whose argument this field refers to. Required for TOOL_CALL_ARGS; enforced on write.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterFieldTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER_PROMPT_TEXT"|"USER_PROMPT_LENGTH_CHARS"|"USER_PROMPT_TURN_COUNT"|"LLM_RESPONSE_TEXT"|"LLM_RESPONSE_LENGTH_CHARS"|"LLM_RESPONSE_TURN_COUNT"|"TOOL_CALL_COUNT"|"TOOL_CALL_ARGS"|"TOOL_CALL_RESPONSE"|"ERROR_COUNT"|"AGENT_ID"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilter[]

---How the field is compared against the value.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterOperation
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterOperationTypeEnum|string Required. The comparison to apply.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterOperationTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTAINS"|"NOT_CONTAINS"|"MATCH_REGEX"|"GREATER_THAN"|"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS"|"LESS_THAN"|"LESS_THAN_OR_EQUALS"|"EQUALS"|"NOT_EQUALS"

---The literal compared against the field.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomDetectorConfigFilterValue
---@field literal? string Required. The literal, always carried as a string. `Field.Type` determines how it is interpreted, except for TOOL_CALL_ARGS and TOOL_CALL_RESPONSE, where `Filter.data_type` does.

---Represents a job that runs custom workloads such as a Docker container or a Python package. A CustomJob can have multiple worker pools and each worker pool can have its own machine and input spec. A CustomJob will be cleaned up once the job enters terminal state (failed or succeeded).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJob
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of a CustomJob.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJobStateEnum Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the CustomJob was created.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the CustomJob entered any of the following states: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the CustomJob. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the CustomJob was most recently updated.
---@field webAccessUris? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Output only. URIs for accessing [interactive shells](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/monitor-debug-interactive-shell) (one URI for each training node). Only available if job_spec.enable_web_access is `true`. The keys are names of each node in the training job; for example, `workerpool0-0` for the primary node, `workerpool1-0` for the first node in the second worker pool, and `workerpool1-1` for the second node in the second worker pool. The values are the URIs for each node's interactive shell.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the CustomJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a CustomJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the CustomJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.
---@field jobSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJobSpec Required. Job spec.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize CustomJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when job's state is `JOB_STATE_FAILED` or `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJobList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJob[]

---Represents the spec of a CustomJob.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJobSpec
---@field baseOutputDirectory? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage location to store the output of this CustomJob or HyperparameterTuningJob. For HyperparameterTuningJob, the baseOutputDirectory of each child CustomJob backing a Trial is set to a subdirectory of name id under its parent HyperparameterTuningJob's baseOutputDirectory. The following Vertex AI environment variables will be passed to containers or python modules when this field is set: For CustomJob: * AIP_MODEL_DIR = `/model/` * AIP_CHECKPOINT_DIR = `/checkpoints/` * AIP_TENSORBOARD_LOG_DIR = `/logs/` For CustomJob backing a Trial of HyperparameterTuningJob: * AIP_MODEL_DIR = `//model/` * AIP_CHECKPOINT_DIR = `//checkpoints/` * AIP_TENSORBOARD_LOG_DIR = `//logs/`
---@field experiment? string Optional. The Experiment associated with this job. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/metadataStores/{metadataStores}/contexts/{experiment-name}`
---@field protectedArtifactLocationId? string The ID of the location to store protected artifacts. e.g. us-central1. Populate only when the location is different than CustomJob location. List of supported locations: https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/general/locations
---@field network? string Optional. The full name of the Compute Engine [network](/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks) to which the Job should be peered. For example, `projects/12345/global/networks/myVPC`. [Format](/compute/docs/reference/rest/v1/networks/insert) is of the form `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`. Where {project} is a project number, as in `12345`, and {network} is a network name. To specify this field, you must have already [configured VPC Network Peering for Vertex AI](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/general/vpc-peering). If this field is left unspecified, the job is not peered with any network.
---@field experimentRun? string Optional. The Experiment Run associated with this job. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/metadataStores/{metadataStores}/contexts/{experiment-name}-{experiment-run-name}`
---@field pscInterfaceConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PscInterfaceConfig Optional. Configuration for PSC-I for CustomJob.
---@field reservedIpRanges? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. A list of names for the reserved ip ranges under the VPC network that can be used for this job. If set, we will deploy the job within the provided ip ranges. Otherwise, the job will be deployed to any ip ranges under the provided VPC network. Example: ['vertex-ai-ip-range'].
---@field persistentResourceId? string Optional. The ID of the PersistentResource in the same Project and Location which to run If this is specified, the job will be run on existing machines held by the PersistentResource instead of on-demand short-live machines. The network and CMEK configs on the job should be consistent with those on the PersistentResource, otherwise, the job will be rejected.
---@field scheduling? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Scheduling Scheduling options for a CustomJob.
---@field models? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The name of the Model resources for which to generate a mapping to artifact URIs. Applicable only to some of the Google-provided custom jobs. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}` In order to retrieve a specific version of the model, also provide the version ID or version alias. Example: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@2` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@golden` If no version ID or alias is specified, the "default" version will be returned. The "default" version alias is created for the first version of the model, and can be moved to other versions later on. There will be exactly one default version.
---@field enableWebAccess? boolean Optional. Whether you want Vertex AI to enable [interactive shell access](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/monitor-debug-interactive-shell) to training containers. If set to `true`, you can access interactive shells at the URIs given by CustomJob.web_access_uris or Trial.web_access_uris (within HyperparameterTuningJob.trials).
---@field enableDashboardAccess? boolean Optional. Whether you want Vertex AI to enable access to the customized dashboard in training chief container. If set to `true`, you can access the dashboard at the URIs given by CustomJob.web_access_uris or Trial.web_access_uris (within HyperparameterTuningJob.trials).
---@field tensorboard? string Optional. The name of a Vertex AI Tensorboard resource to which this CustomJob will upload Tensorboard logs. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tensorboards/{tensorboard}`
---@field workerPoolSpecs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1WorkerPoolSpecList Required. The spec of the worker pools including machine type and Docker image. All worker pools except the first one are optional and can be skipped by providing an empty value.
---@field serviceAccount? string Specifies the service account for workload run-as account. Users submitting jobs must have act-as permission on this run-as account. If unspecified, the [Vertex AI Custom Code Service Agent](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/general/access-control#service-agents) for the CustomJob's project is used.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJobStateEnum "JOB_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"JOB_STATE_QUEUED"|"JOB_STATE_PENDING"|"JOB_STATE_RUNNING"|"JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED"|"JOB_STATE_FAILED"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLING"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLED"|"JOB_STATE_PAUSED"|"JOB_STATE_EXPIRED"|"JOB_STATE_UPDATING"|"JOB_STATE_PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED"

---Spec for custom output.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomOutput
---@field rawOutputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RawOutput Output only. List of raw output strings.

---Spec for custom output format configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomOutputFormatConfig
---@field returnRawOutput? boolean Optional. Whether to return raw output.

---Config for scraping a Gemini Data Analytics data agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataAgentConfig
---@field dataAgent? string Required. The resource name of the Gemini Data Analytics data agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/dataAgents/{data_agent}`. For example: `projects/123/locations/us-central1/dataAgents/my-agent`.

---Configuration for Gemini Enterprise MCP data connectors scoped to this task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataConnectorConfig
---@field engineResourceName? string Optional. Full resource name of the Discovery Engine Engine (e.g., "projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}").
---@field dataConnectors? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Map of active connector short name / data_source (e.g., "jira", "servicenow") to its full DataConnector resource name (e.g., "projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector"). If multiple connectors share a data_source, the first configured connector for that data_source is retained.

---A piece of data in a Dataset. Could be an image, a video, a document or plain text.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItem
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field payload? any Required. The data that the DataItem represents (for example, an image or a text snippet). The schema of the payload is stored in the parent Dataset's metadata schema's dataItemSchemaUri field.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your DataItems. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one DataItem(System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the DataItem.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this DataItem was last updated.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this DataItem was created.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItemList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItem[]

---A container for a single DataItem and Annotations on it.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItemView
---@field annotations? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AnnotationList The Annotations on the DataItem. If too many Annotations should be returned for the DataItem, this field will be truncated per annotations_limit in request. If it was, then the has_truncated_annotations will be set to true.
---@field hasTruncatedAnnotations? boolean True if and only if the Annotations field has been truncated. It happens if more Annotations for this DataItem met the request's annotation_filter than are allowed to be returned by annotations_limit. Note that if Annotations field is not being returned due to field mask, then this field will not be set to true no matter how many Annotations are there.
---@field dataItem? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItem The DataItem.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItemViewList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataItemView[]

---DataLabelingJob is used to trigger a human labeling job on unlabeled data from the following Dataset:
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataLabelingJob
---@field labelingProgress? number Output only. Current labeling job progress percentage scaled in interval [0, 100], indicating the percentage of DataItems that has been finished.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataLabelingJobStateEnum Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field annotationLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Labels to assign to annotations generated by this DataLabelingJob. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a DataLabelingJob. If set, this DataLabelingJob will be secured by this key. Note: Annotations created in the DataLabelingJob are associated with the EncryptionSpec of the Dataset they are exported to.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this DataLabelingJob was created.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. DataLabelingJob errors. It is only populated when job's state is `JOB_STATE_FAILED` or `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field specialistPools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList The SpecialistPools' resource names associated with this job.
---@field datasets? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Dataset resource names. Right now we only support labeling from a single Dataset. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}`
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the DataLabelingJob. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters. Display name of a DataLabelingJob.
---@field activeLearningConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ActiveLearningConfig Parameters that configure the active learning pipeline. Active learning will label the data incrementally via several iterations. For every iteration, it will select a batch of data based on the sampling strategy.
---@field labelerCount? number Required. Number of labelers to work on each DataItem.
---@field instructionUri? string Required. The Google Cloud Storage location of the instruction pdf. This pdf is shared with labelers, and provides detailed description on how to label DataItems in Datasets.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the DataLabelingJob.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this DataLabelingJob was updated most recently.
---@field currentSpend? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleTypeMoney Output only. Estimated cost(in US dollars) that the DataLabelingJob has incurred to date.
---@field inputs? any Required. Input config parameters for the DataLabelingJob.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your DataLabelingJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable. Following system labels exist for each DataLabelingJob: * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/schema": output only, its value is the inputs_schema's title.
---@field inputsSchemaUri? string Required. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the config for a specific type of DataLabelingJob. The schema files that can be used here are found in the https://storage.googleapis.com/google-cloud-aiplatform bucket in the /schema/datalabelingjob/inputs/ folder.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataLabelingJobList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataLabelingJob[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataLabelingJobStateEnum "JOB_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"JOB_STATE_QUEUED"|"JOB_STATE_PENDING"|"JOB_STATE_RUNNING"|"JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED"|"JOB_STATE_FAILED"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLING"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLED"|"JOB_STATE_PAUSED"|"JOB_STATE_EXPIRED"|"JOB_STATE_UPDATING"|"JOB_STATE_PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED"

---A collection of DataItems and Annotations on them.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Dataset
---@field metadata? any Required. Additional information about the Dataset.
---@field savedQueries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SavedQueryList All SavedQueries belong to the Dataset will be returned in List/Get Dataset response. The annotation_specs field will not be populated except for UI cases which will only use annotation_spec_count. In CreateDataset request, a SavedQuery is created together if this field is set, up to one SavedQuery can be set in CreateDatasetRequest. The SavedQuery should not contain any AnnotationSpec.
---@field description? string The description of the Dataset.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a Dataset. If set, this Dataset and all sub-resources of this Dataset will be secured by this key.
---@field modelReference? string Optional. Reference to the public base model last used by the dataset. Only set for prompt datasets.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Dataset was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Dataset was last updated.
---@field metadataArtifact? string Output only. The resource name of the Artifact that was created in MetadataStore when creating the Dataset. The Artifact resource name pattern is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/metadataStores/{metadata_store}/artifacts/{artifact}`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the Dataset. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field metadataSchemaUri? string Required. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing additional information about the Dataset. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 Schema Object. The schema files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/dataset/metadata/.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. The resource name of the Dataset. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}`
---@field dataItemCount? string Output only. The number of DataItems in this Dataset. Only apply for non-structured Dataset.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Datasets. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Dataset (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable. Following system labels exist for each Dataset: * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/dataset_metadata_schema": output only, its value is the metadata_schema's title.

---Defines a custom dataset-level aggregation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetCustomMetric
---@field aggregationFunction? string Required. The Python code string containing the aggregation function. Expected function signature: `def aggregate(instances: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, float]:` The `instances` argument is a list of dictionaries, where each dictionary represents a single evaluation result item. The structure of each dictionary corresponds to the fields in the `EvaluationResult` message. This includes: - `"request"`: Contains the original input data and model inputs (from `EvaluationResult.EvaluationRequest`). - `"candidate_results"`: Contains the results of any instance-level metrics (from `EvaluationResult.CandidateResults`). Example of a single item in the `instances` list: { "request": { "prompt": {"text": "What is the capital of France?"}, "golden_response": {"text": "Paris"}, "candidate_responses": [{"candidate": "model-v1", "text": "Paris"}] }, "candidate_results": [ {"metric": "exact_match", "score": 1.0}, {"metric": "bleu", "score": 0.9} ] }
---@field displayName? string Optional. A display name for this custom summary metric. Used to prefix keys in the output summaryMetrics map. If not provided, a default name like "dataset_custom_metric_1", "dataset_custom_metric_2", etc., will be generated based on the order in the repeated field.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetCustomMetricList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetCustomMetric[]

---Distribution computed over a tuning dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetDistribution
