---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationMetricList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationMetric[]

---Config for parsing LLM responses. It can be used to parse the LLM response to be evaluated, or the LLM response from LLM-based metrics/Autoraters.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationParserConfig
---@field customCodeParserConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationParserConfigCustomCodeParserConfig Optional. Use custom code to parse the LLM response.

---Configuration for parsing the LLM response using custom code.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationParserConfigCustomCodeParserConfig
---@field parsingFunction? string Required. Python function for parsing results. The function should be defined within this string. The function takes a list of strings (LLM responses) and should return either a list of dictionaries (for rubrics) or a single dictionary (for a metric result). Example function signature: def parse(responses: list[str]) -> list[dict[str, Any]] | dict[str, Any]: When parsing rubrics, return a list of dictionaries, where each dictionary represents a Rubric. Example for rubrics: [ { "content": {"property": {"description": "The response is factual."}}, "type": "FACTUALITY", "importance": "HIGH" }, { "content": {"property": {"description": "The response is fluent."}}, "type": "FLUENCY", "importance": "MEDIUM" } ] When parsing critique results, return a dictionary representing a MetricResult. Example for a metric result: { "score": 0.8, "explanation": "The model followed most instructions.", "rubric_verdicts": [...] } ... code for result extraction and aggregation
---@field codeExecutionRegion? string Optional. The region to use for code execution. If set, the Code Execution Sandbox will be invoked in the specified region regardless of the request's originating region. Must be a region where the Code Execution Sandbox is available. For the current list of [supported regions](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/agent-engine/locations). If unset, the request's originating region is used.

---Prompt to be evaluated. This can represent a single-turn prompt or a multi-turn conversation for agent evaluations.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationPrompt
---@field value? any Fields and values that can be used to populate the prompt template.
---@field text? string Text prompt.
---@field agentData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentData Optional. Represents the complete execution trace of a multi-turn conversation, which can involve single or multiple agents. This serves as the input context for agent scraping.
---@field userScenario? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationPromptUserScenario Optional. The generated user scenario used to drive multi-turn agent running results.
---@field promptTemplateData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationPromptPromptTemplateData Prompt template data.

---Message to hold a prompt template and the values to populate the template.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationPromptPromptTemplateData
---@field values? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ContentMap_ The values for fields in the prompt template.

---User scenario to help simulate multi-turn agent running results.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationPromptUserScenario
---@field conversationPlan? string Required. The plan for the conversation, used to drive the multi-turn agent run and generate the simulated agent evaluation dataset.
---@field startingPrompt? string Required. The prompt that starts the conversation between the simulated user and the agent under test.

---A single evaluation request supporting input for both single-turn model generation and multi-turn agent execution traces. Valid input modes: 1. Inference Mode: `prompt` is set (containing text or AgentData context). 2. Offline Eval Mode: `prompt` is unset, and `candidate_responses` contains `agent_data` (the completed execution trace). Validation Rule: Either `prompt` must be set, OR at least one of the `candidate_responses` must contain `agent_data`. Metrics receive each candidate as an `EvaluationInstance`, whose fields are the names metrics can reference: `prompt` -> `prompt`, the candidate -> `response` (or `agent_eval_data` for `agent_data`), `golden_response` -> `reference`, `rubrics` -> `rubric_groups`, and `prompt.prompt_template_data.values` and `extra_context` -> `other_data`.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRequest
---@field rubrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGroupMap Optional. Named groups of rubrics associated with this prompt. The key is a user-defined name for the rubric group.
---@field candidateResponses? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CandidateResponseList Optional. Responses from model under test and other baseline models for comparison.
---@field goldenResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CandidateResponse Optional. The Ideal response or ground truth.
---@field prompt? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationPrompt Optional. The request/prompt to evaluate.

---Evaluation result.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationResult
---@field evaluationRequest? string Required. The request item that was evaluated. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationItems/{evaluation_item}
---@field evaluationRequestRevision? string Output only. The EvaluationItemRevision that was evaluated, set when the evaluation run's data source is an EvaluationSetRevision. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationItems/{evaluation_item}/revisions/{revision}`.
---@field metric? string Required. The metric that was evaluated.
---@field candidateResults? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CandidateResultList Optional. The results for the metric.
---@field evaluationRun? string Required. The evaluation run that was used to generate the result. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationRuns/{evaluation_run}
---@field request? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRequest Required. The request that was evaluated.
---@field metadata? any Optional. Metadata about the evaluation result.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationResultList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationResult[]

---The results of the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationResults
---@field summaryMetrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SummaryMetrics Optional. The summary metrics for the evaluation run.
---@field evaluationSet? string The evaluation set where item level results are stored.
---@field lossAnalysisResults? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisResultList Output only. The results of the auto-loss analysis performed on the eval set associated with the run.

---Configuration for a rubric group to be generated/saved for evaluation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRubricConfig
---@field predefinedRubricGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricPredefinedMetricSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using a predefined spec.
---@field rubricGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using this specification.
---@field rubricGroupKey? string Required. The key used to save the generated rubrics. If a generation spec is provided, this key will be used for the name of the generated rubric group. Otherwise, this key will be used to look up the existing rubric group on the evaluation item. Note that if a rubric group key is specified on both a rubric config and an evaluation metric, the key from the metric will be used to select the rubrics for evaluation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRubricConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRubricConfig[]

---EvaluationRun is a resource that represents a single evaluation run, which includes a set of prompts, model responses, evaluation configuration and the resulting metrics.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRun
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Evaluation Run.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when the evaluation run's state is FAILED or CANCELLED.
---@field serviceAccount? string Optional. The service account to run the evaluation run as. If set, the run uses this service account to access Google Cloud resources. Access is limited to the IAM permissions that you grant to the service account. Must be provided if an inference config sets `harbor_run_config`, `data_agent_config`. If no inference config requires this field, setting it returns an error. The caller must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account, and the project's [Vertex AI Service Agent](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/general/access-control#service-agents) must have the `roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator` role on it.
---@field evaluationResults? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationResults Output only. The results of the evaluation run. Only populated when the evaluation run's state is SUCCEEDED.
---@field inferenceConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigMap Optional. The candidate to inference config map for the evaluation run. The candidate can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field completionTime? string Output only. Time when the evaluation run was completed.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunStateEnum Output only. The state of the evaluation run.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the evaluation run was created.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Labels for the evaluation run.
---@field dataSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunDataSource Required. The data source for the evaluation run.
---@field evaluationExperiment? string Optional. The resource name of the evaluation experiment for the evaluation run. Setting the evaluation experiment will add the run to the experiment. Multiple runs can be added to the same experiment. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationExperiments/{evaluation_experiment}`
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the EvaluationRun. This is a unique identifier. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationRuns/{evaluation_run}`
---@field metadata? any Optional. Metadata about the evaluation run, can be used by the caller to store additional tracking information about the evaluation run.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for this EvaluationRun. If set, this EvaluationRun will be secured by this key.
---@field evaluationSetSnapshot? string Output only. The specific evaluation set of the evaluation run. For runs with an evaluation set input, this will be that same set. For runs with BigQuery input, it's the sampled BigQuery dataset.
---@field evaluationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfig Optional. The configuration used for the evaluation. Optional when analysis_configs is provided.

---The data source for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunDataSource
---@field evaluationSet? string The EvaluationSet resource name. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationSets/{evaluation_set}`
---@field evaluationSetRevision? string The EvaluationSetRevision resource name. The run evaluates the item revisions frozen in the revision, so later changes to the EvaluationSet and its EvaluationItems do not affect it. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationSets/{evaluation_set}/revisions/{revision}`
---@field bigqueryRequestSet? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryRequestSet Evaluation data in bigquery.

---The Evalution configuration used for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfig
---@field cloudLoggingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CloudLoggingConfig Optional. Configuration for exporting evaluation results to Cloud Logging.
---@field autoraterConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig Optional. The autorater config for the evaluation run.
---@field datasetCustomMetrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetCustomMetricList Optional. Specifications for custom dataset-level aggregations.
---@field allowCrossRegionModel? boolean Optional. Allows the evaluation run to use cross region models. When this flag is set, the service may route traffic to other regions if a model is unavailable in the current region (e.g., to a `global` endpoint). If a fully-qualified model endpoint resource name with a different region than the run location is provided elsewhere in the run config, this flag must be set to true or the request will fail.
---@field outputConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigOutputConfig Optional. The output config for the evaluation run.
---@field rubricConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRubricConfigList Optional. The rubric configs for the evaluation run. They are used to generate rubrics which can be used by rubric-based metrics. Multiple rubric configs can be specified for rubric generation but only one rubric config can be used for a rubric-based metric. If more than one rubric config is provided, the evaluation metric must specify a rubric group key. Note that if a generation spec is specified on both a rubric config and an evaluation metric, the rubrics generated for the metric will be used for evaluation.
---@field promptTemplate? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigPromptTemplate The prompt template used for inference. The values for variables in the prompt template are defined in EvaluationItem.EvaluationPrompt.PromptTemplateData.values.
---@field lossAnalysisConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisConfigList Optional. Specifications for loss analysis. Each config can be specified for one metric.
---@field metrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricList Optional. The metrics to be calculated in the evaluation run. Required when analysis_configs is not set.

---The autorater config used for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig
---@field generationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfig Optional. Configuration options for model generation and outputs.
---@field autoraterModel? string Optional. The fully qualified name of the publisher model or tuned autorater endpoint to use. Publisher model format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/*/models/*` Tuned model endpoint format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/endpoints/{endpoint}`
---@field sampleCount? number Optional. Number of samples for each instance in the dataset. If not specified, the default is 4. Minimum value is 1, maximum value is 32.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfigMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig }

---The output config for the evaluation run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigOutputConfig
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination BigQuery destination for evaluation output.
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination Cloud Storage destination for evaluation output.

---Prompt template used for inference.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigPromptTemplate
---@field gcsUri? string Prompt template stored in Cloud Storage. Format: "gs://my-bucket/file-name.txt".
---@field promptTemplate? string Inline prompt template. Template variables should be in the format "{var_name}". Example: "Translate the following from {source_lang} to {target_lang}: {text}"

---Defines the configuration for a candidate model or agent being evaluated. `InferenceConfig` encapsulates all the necessary information to invoke or scrape the candidate during the evaluation run. This includes direct model inference parameters, agent execution settings, and multi-turn scraping configurations (such as user simulators). It serves as the primary representation of the candidate across different stages of the evaluation process.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfig
---@field agentConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigInferenceAgentConfig Optional. Deprecated: Use `agents` instead. Agent config used to generate responses.
---@field promptTemplate? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigPromptTemplate Optional. The prompt template used for inference. The values for variables in the prompt template are defined in EvaluationItem.EvaluationPrompt.PromptTemplateData.values. If not specified, the prompt template in the EvaluationConfig will be used.
---@field generationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfig Optional. Generation config.
---@field agents? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentConfigMap Optional. Contains the static configurations for each agent in the system. Key: agent_id (matches the `author` field in events). Value: The static configuration of the agent.
---@field model? string Optional. The fully qualified name of the publisher model or endpoint to use. Anthropic and Llama third-party models are also supported through Model Garden. Publisher model format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/*/models/*` Third-party model formats: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/anthropic/models/{model}` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/llama/models/{model}` Endpoint format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/endpoints/{endpoint}`
---@field rawAgentTrajectoryDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigRawAgentTrajectoryDestination Optional. The destination for the raw, unconverted agent trajectory data the run produces.
---@field harborRunConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborRunConfig Optional. Config for running an agent on tasks in Harbor format in a sandboxed batch environment. Its presence routes the run to the Harbor batch inference path; which datasets and tasks run is carried by the `harbor_task` of each evaluation item. If this field is set, the evaluation run must set `service_account`. The Harbor task run in sandbox will use the service account.
---@field agentRunConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfig Optional. Agent run config.
---@field parallelism? number Optional. The parallelism of the evaluation run for the inference step. If not specified, the default parallelism will be used.

---Configuration for Agent Run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfig
---@field discoveryEngineAssistantConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DiscoveryEngineAssistantConfig Optional. Config for scraping a Discovery Engine Assistant. The scraping service runs the assistant via the Discovery Engine AssistantService and returns the resulting trajectory for evaluation.
---@field geminiAgentConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GeminiAgentConfig Optional. Config for scraping a Gemini Agent via the Interactions API. The scraping service creates interactions against the agent and returns the resulting interaction traces for evaluation.
---@field sessionInput? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigSessionInput Optional. The session input to get agent running results.
---@field userSimulatorConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfigUserSimulatorConfig The configuration for a user simulator that uses an LLM to generate messages on behalf of the user.
---@field dataAgentConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DataAgentConfig Optional. Config for scraping a Gemini Data Analytics data agent. The scraping service runs the agent via the DataChatService Chat API and returns the resulting trajectory for evaluation.
---@field agentEngine? string Optional. The resource name of the Agent Engine. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine} For example: projects/123/locations/us-central1/reasoningEngines/456

---Used for multi-turn agent scraping. Contains configuration for a user simulator that uses an LLM to generate messages on behalf of the user.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigAgentRunConfigUserSimulatorConfig
---@field maxTurn? number Maximum number of invocations allowed by the multi-turn agent scraping. This property allows us to stop a run-off conversation, where the agent and the user simulator get into a never ending loop. The initial fixed prompt is also counted as an invocation.
---@field modelName? string The model name to use for multi-turn agent scraping to get next user message, e.g. "gemini-3-flash-preview".
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfig The configuration for the model.

---Configuration that describes an agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigInferenceAgentConfig
---@field developerInstruction? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Content Optional. The developer instruction for the agent.
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolList Optional. The tools available to the agent.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfig }

---The destination for the raw, unconverted agent trace data the run produces.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigRawAgentTrajectoryDestination
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination BigQuery destination for the raw agent trace data.
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination Cloud Storage destination for the raw agent trace data.

---Session input to run an Agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunInferenceConfigSessionInput
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Additional parameters for the session, like app_name, etc. For example, {"app_name": "my-app"}.
---@field userId? string Optional. The user id for the agent session. The ID can be up to 128 characters long.
---@field sessionState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Session specific memory which stores key conversation points.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRun[]

---The metric used for evaluation runs.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetric
---@field computationBasedMetricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricComputationBasedMetricSpec Spec for a computation based metric.
---@field metricConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Metric The metric config.
---@field metricResourceName? string Optional. The resource name of the metric definition.
---@field metric? string Required. The name of the metric.
---@field rubricBasedMetricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricBasedMetricSpec Spec for rubric based metric.
---@field predefinedMetricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricPredefinedMetricSpec Spec for a pre-defined metric.
---@field llmBasedMetricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricLLMBasedMetricSpec Spec for an LLM based metric.

---Specification for a computation based metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricComputationBasedMetricSpec
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. A map of parameters for the metric, e.g. {"rouge_type": "rougeL"}.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricComputationBasedMetricSpecTypeEnum|string Required. The type of the computation based metric.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricComputationBasedMetricSpecTypeEnum "COMPUTATION_BASED_METRIC_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXACT_MATCH"|"BLEU"|"ROUGE"

---Specification for an LLM based metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricLLMBasedMetricSpec
---@field rubricGroupKey? string Use a pre-defined group of rubrics associated with the input. Refers to a key in the rubric_groups map of EvaluationInstance.
---@field systemInstruction? string Optional. System instructions for the judge model.
---@field metricPromptTemplate? string Required. Template for the prompt sent to the judge model.
---@field predefinedRubricGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricPredefinedMetricSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using a predefined spec.
---@field judgeAutoraterConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig Optional. Optional configuration for the judge LLM (Autorater).
---@field additionalConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Optional additional configuration for the metric.
---@field rubricGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpec Dynamically generate rubrics using this specification.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetric[]

---Specification for a pre-defined metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricPredefinedMetricSpec
---@field stepAutoraterConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfigMap Optional. Per-step autorater overrides for this predefined metric. Keys are evaluation stage names: "intent_extraction", "rubric_generation", "rubric_validation".
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. The parameters needed to run the pre-defined metric.
---@field metricSpecName? string Required. The name of a pre-defined metric, such as "instruction_following_v1" or "text_quality_v1".

---Specification for a metric that is based on rubrics.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricBasedMetricSpec
---@field metricPromptTemplate? string Optional. Template for the prompt used by the judge model to evaluate against rubrics.
---@field rubricGroupKey? string Use a pre-defined group of rubrics associated with the input content. This refers to a key in the `rubric_groups` map of `RubricEnhancedContents`.
---@field rubricGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpec Dynamically generate rubrics for evaluation using this specification.
---@field inlineRubrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricBasedMetricSpecRepeatedRubrics Use rubrics provided directly in the spec.
---@field judgeAutoraterConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig Optional. Optional configuration for the judge LLM (Autorater). The definition of AutoraterConfig needs to be provided.

---Defines a list of rubrics, used when providing rubrics inline.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricBasedMetricSpecRepeatedRubrics
---@field rubrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricList The list of rubrics.

---Specification for how rubrics should be generated.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpec
---@field promptTemplate? string Optional. Template for the prompt used to generate rubrics. The details should be updated based on the most-recent recipe requirements.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunEvaluationConfigAutoraterConfig Optional. Configuration for the model used in rubric generation. Configs including sampling count and base model can be specified here. Flipping is not supported for rubric generation.
---@field rubricTypeOntology? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. An optional, pre-defined list of allowed types for generated rubrics. If this field is provided, it implies `include_rubric_type` should be true, and the generated rubric types should be chosen from this ontology.
---@field rubricContentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpecRubricContentTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of rubric content to be generated.
---@field metricResourceName? string Optional. Resource name of the metric definition.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunMetricRubricGenerationSpecRubricContentTypeEnum "RUBRIC_CONTENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROPERTY"|"NL_QUESTION_ANSWER"|"PYTHON_CODE_ASSERTION"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationRunStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PENDING"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"CANCELLED"|"INFERENCE"|"GENERATING_RUBRICS"|"GENERATING_LOSS_CLUSTERS"

---EvaluationSet is a collection of related EvaluationItems that are evaluated together.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSet
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the EvaluationSet. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationSets/{evaluation_set}`
---@field agentConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentConfigMap Optional. Static configurations for each agent associated with the items in this set. Key: `agent_id` (matches the `author` field in `events`). Value: The static configuration of the agent.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this item was last updated.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for this EvaluationSet. If set, this EvaluationSet and its sub-resources will be secured by this key.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the EvaluationSet.
---@field evaluationItems? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. The EvaluationItems that are part of this dataset.
---@field harborDataset? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborDataset Output only. Set when the items were imported from a Harbor dataset.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this item was created.
---@field metadata? any Optional. Metadata for the EvaluationSet.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSetList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSet[]

---An immutable snapshot of an EvaluationSet and its EvaluationItems. Evaluation runs on a revision are reproducible because the revision and its item revisions cannot change.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSetRevision
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the EvaluationSetRevision. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/evaluationSets/{evaluation_set}/revisions/{revision}`
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this revision was created.
---@field snapshot? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSet Output only. A copy of the EvaluationSet at the time the revision was created. Only `display_name`, `metadata` and `labels` are copied from the source set; `agent_configs` is not. `snapshot.name` is the name of the source EvaluationSet, and `snapshot.evaluation_items` contains EvaluationItemRevision resource names instead of EvaluationItem resource names.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSetRevisionList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationSetRevision[]

---An edge describing the relationship between an Artifact and an Execution in a lineage graph.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Event
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to annotate Events. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Event (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field execution? string Output only. The relative resource name of the Execution in the Event.
---@field artifact? string Required. The relative resource name of the Artifact in the Event.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EventTypeEnum|string Required. The type of the Event.
---@field eventTime? string Output only. Time the Event occurred.

---Actions are parts of events that are executed by the agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EventActions
---@field requestedAuthConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Will only be set by a tool response indicating tool request euc. Struct key is the function call id since one function call response (from model) could correspond to multiple function calls. Struct value is the required auth config, which can be another struct.
---@field transferAgent? string Optional. If set, the event transfers to the specified agent.
---@field stateDelta? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Indicates that the event is updating the state with the given delta.
---@field escalate? boolean Optional. The agent is escalating to a higher level agent.
---@field skipSummarization? boolean Optional. If true, it won't call model to summarize function response. Only used for function_response event.
---@field artifactDelta? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.IntegerMap Optional. Indicates that the event is updating an artifact. key is the filename, value is the version.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EventList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Event[]

---Metadata relating to a LLM response event.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EventMetadata
---@field inputTranscription? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Transcription Optional. Audio transcription of user input.
---@field customMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap The custom metadata of the LlmResponse.
---@field groundingMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadata Optional. Metadata returned to client when grounding is enabled.
---@field partial? boolean Optional. Indicates whether the text content is part of a unfinished text stream. Only used for streaming mode and when the content is plain text.
---@field interrupted? boolean Optional. Flag indicating that LLM was interrupted when generating the content. Usually it's due to user interruption during a bidi streaming.
---@field turnComplete? boolean Optional. Indicates whether the response from the model is complete. Only used for streaming mode.
---@field outputTranscription? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Transcription Optional. Audio transcription of model output.
---@field branch? string Optional. The branch of the event. The format is like agent_1.agent_2.agent_3, where agent_1 is the parent of agent_2, and agent_2 is the parent of agent_3. Branch is used when multiple child agents shouldn't see their siblings' conversation history.
---@field longRunningToolIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Set of ids of the long running function calls. Agent client will know from this field about which function call is long running. Only valid for function call event.

---An event-driven trigger.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EventSchedule
---@field eventSource? string Required. Identifier of a registered event source / webhook subscription whose events fire the task.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EventTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INPUT"|"OUTPUT"

---Input for exact match metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchInput
---@field metricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchSpec Required. Spec for exact match metric.
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchInstanceList Required. Repeated exact match instances.

---Spec for exact match instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchInstance
---@field reference? string Required. Ground truth used to compare against the prediction.
---@field prediction? string Required. Output of the evaluated model.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchInstanceList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchInstance[]

---Exact match metric value for an instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchMetricValue
---@field score? number Output only. Exact match score.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchMetricValueList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchMetricValue[]

---Results for exact match metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchResults
---@field exactMatchMetricValues? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchMetricValueList Output only. Exact match metric values.

---Spec for exact match metric - returns 1 if prediction and reference exactly matches, otherwise 0.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExactMatchSpec

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Example
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Example was created.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name for Example.
---@field storedContentsExample? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1StoredContentsExample An example of chat history and its expected outcome to be used with GenerateContent.
---@field exampleId? string Optional. Immutable. Unique identifier of an example. If not specified when upserting new examples, the example_id will be generated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Example[]

---Represents an executable service to manage and retrieve examples.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleStore
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the ExampleStore.
---@field displayName? string Required. Display name of the ExampleStore.
---@field exampleStoreConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleStoreConfig Required. Example Store config.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this ExampleStore was created.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the ExampleStore. This is a unique identifier. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/exampleStores/{example_store}
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this ExampleStore was most recently updated.

---Configuration for the Example Store.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleStoreConfig
---@field vertexEmbeddingModel? string Required. The embedding model to be used for vector embedding. Immutable. Supported models: * "text-embedding-005" * "text-multilingual-embedding-002"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleStoreList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleStore[]

---Example-based explainability that returns the nearest neighbors from the provided dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Examples
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource The Cloud Storage locations that contain the instances to be indexed for approximate nearest neighbor search.
---@field presets? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Presets Simplified preset configuration, which automatically sets configuration values based on the desired query speed-precision trade-off and modality.
---@field nearestNeighborSearchConfig? any The full configuration for the generated index, the semantics are the same as metadata and should match [NearestNeighborSearchConfig](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/explainable-ai/configuring-explanations-example-based#nearest-neighbor-search-config).
---@field neighborCount? number The number of neighbors to return when querying for examples.
---@field exampleGcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesExampleGcsSource The Cloud Storage input instances.

---Filters for examples' array metadata fields. An array field is example metadata where multiple values are attributed to a single example.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesArrayFilter
---@field values? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. The values by which to filter examples.
---@field arrayOperator? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesArrayFilterArrayOperatorEnum|string Required. The operator logic to use for filtering.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesArrayFilterArrayOperatorEnum "ARRAY_OPERATOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTAINS_ANY"|"CONTAINS_ALL"

---The Cloud Storage input instances.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesExampleGcsSource
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource The Cloud Storage location for the input instances.
---@field dataFormat? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesExampleGcsSourceDataFormatEnum|string The format in which instances are given, if not specified, assume it's JSONL format. Currently only JSONL format is supported.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesExampleGcsSourceDataFormatEnum "DATA_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"JSONL"

---Overrides for example-based explanations.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesOverride
---@field restrictions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesRestrictionsNamespaceList Restrict the resulting nearest neighbors to respect these constraints.
---@field neighborCount? number The number of neighbors to return.
---@field returnEmbeddings? boolean If true, return the embeddings instead of neighbors.
---@field dataFormat? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesOverrideDataFormatEnum|string The format of the data being provided with each call.
---@field crowdingCount? number The number of neighbors to return that have the same crowding tag.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesOverrideDataFormatEnum "DATA_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"INSTANCES"|"EMBEDDINGS"

---Restrictions namespace for example-based explanations overrides.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesRestrictionsNamespace
---@field deny? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList The list of deny tags.
---@field namespaceName? string The namespace name.
---@field allow? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList The list of allowed tags.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesRestrictionsNamespaceList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesRestrictionsNamespace[]

---Code generated by the model that is meant to be executed, and the result returned to the model. Generated when using the `CodeExecution` tool, in which the code will be automatically executed, and a corresponding CodeExecutionResult will also be generated.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutableCode
---@field id? string Optional. Unique identifier of the `ExecutableCode` part. The server returns the `CodeExecutionResult` with the matching `id`.
---@field code? string Required. The code to be executed.
---@field language? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutableCodeLanguageEnum|string Required. Programming language of the `code`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutableCodeLanguageEnum "LANGUAGE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PYTHON"

---Response message for SandboxEnvironmentExecutionService.ExecuteCode.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecuteCodeResponse
---@field outputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ChunkList The outputs from the sandbox environment.

---Response message for ExtensionExecutionService.ExecuteExtension.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecuteExtensionResponse
---@field content? string Response content from the extension. The content should be conformant to the response.content schema in the extension's manifest/OpenAPI spec.

---Response message for SandboxEnvironmentExecutionService.Execute.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecuteSandboxEnvironmentResponse
---@field outputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ChunkList The outputs from the sandbox environment.

---Instance of a general execution.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Execution
---@field etag? string An eTag used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Properties of the Execution. Top level metadata keys' heading and trailing spaces will be trimmed. The size of this field should not exceed 200KB.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutionStateEnum|string The state of this Execution. This is a property of the Execution, and does not imply or capture any ongoing process. This property is managed by clients (such as Vertex AI Pipelines) and the system does not prescribe or check the validity of state transitions.
---@field schemaVersion? string The version of the schema in `schema_title` to use. Schema title and version is expected to be registered in earlier Create Schema calls. And both are used together as unique identifiers to identify schemas within the local metadata store.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Execution was created.
---@field displayName? string User provided display name of the Execution. May be up to 128 Unicode characters.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the Execution.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Executions. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Execution (System labels are excluded).
---@field schemaTitle? string The title of the schema describing the metadata. Schema title and version is expected to be registered in earlier Create Schema calls. And both are used together as unique identifiers to identify schemas within the local metadata store.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Execution was last updated.
---@field description? string Description of the Execution

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutionList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Execution[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutionStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NEW"|"RUNNING"|"COMPLETE"|"FAILED"|"CACHED"|"CANCELLED"

---Response message for PredictionService.Explain.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplainResponse
---@field concurrentExplanations? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplainResponseConcurrentExplanationMap This field stores the results of the explanations run in parallel with The default explanation strategy/method.
---@field deployedModelId? string ID of the Endpoint's DeployedModel that served this explanation.
---@field predictions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentList The predictions that are the output of the predictions call. Same as PredictResponse.predictions.
---@field explanations? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationList The explanations of the Model's PredictResponse.predictions. It has the same number of elements as instances to be explained.

---This message is a wrapper grouping Concurrent Explanations.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplainResponseConcurrentExplanation
---@field explanations? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationList The explanations of the Model's PredictResponse.predictions. It has the same number of elements as instances to be explained.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplainResponseConcurrentExplanationMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplainResponseConcurrentExplanation }

---Explanation of a prediction (provided in PredictResponse.predictions) produced by the Model on a given instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Explanation
---@field attributions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AttributionList Output only. Feature attributions grouped by predicted outputs. For Models that predict only one output, such as regression Models that predict only one score, there is only one attibution that explains the predicted output. For Models that predict multiple outputs, such as multiclass Models that predict multiple classes, each element explains one specific item. Attribution.output_index can be used to identify which output this attribution is explaining. By default, we provide Shapley values for the predicted class. However, you can configure the explanation request to generate Shapley values for any other classes too. For example, if a model predicts a probability of `0.4` for approving a loan application, the model's decision is to reject the application since `p(reject) = 0.6 > p(approve) = 0.4`, and the default Shapley values would be computed for rejection decision and not approval, even though the latter might be the positive class. If users set ExplanationParameters.top_k, the attributions are sorted by instance_output_value in descending order. If ExplanationParameters.output_indices is specified, the attributions are stored by Attribution.output_index in the same order as they appear in the output_indices.
---@field neighbors? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1NeighborList Output only. List of the nearest neighbors for example-based explanations. For models deployed with the examples explanations feature enabled, the attributions field is empty and instead the neighbors field is populated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Explanation[]

---Metadata describing the Model's input and output for explanation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadata
---@field featureAttributionsSchemaUri? string Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the format of the feature attributions. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML tabular Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI. Note: The URI given on output may be different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field inputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataMap Required. Map from feature names to feature input metadata. Keys are the name of the features. Values are the specification of the feature. An empty InputMetadata is valid. It describes a text feature which has the name specified as the key in ExplanationMetadata.inputs. The baseline of the empty feature is chosen by Vertex AI. For Vertex AI-provided Tensorflow images, the key can be any friendly name of the feature. Once specified, featureAttributions are keyed by this key (if not grouped with another feature). For custom images, the key must match with the key in instance.
---@field outputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOutputMetadataMap Required. Map from output names to output metadata. For Vertex AI-provided Tensorflow images, keys can be any user defined string that consists of any UTF-8 characters. For custom images, keys are the name of the output field in the prediction to be explained. Currently only one key is allowed.
---@field latentSpaceSource? string Name of the source to generate embeddings for example based explanations.

---Metadata of the input of a feature. Fields other than InputMetadata.input_baselines are applicable only for Models that are using Vertex AI-provided images for Tensorflow.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadata
---@field inputTensorName? string Name of the input tensor for this feature. Required and is only applicable to Vertex AI-provided images for Tensorflow.
---@field groupName? string Name of the group that the input belongs to. Features with the same group name will be treated as one feature when computing attributions. Features grouped together can have different shapes in value. If provided, there will be one single attribution generated in Attribution.feature_attributions, keyed by the group name.
---@field visualization? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualization Visualization configurations for image explanation.
---@field indicesTensorName? string Specifies the index of the values of the input tensor. Required when the input tensor is a sparse representation. Refer to Tensorflow documentation for more details: https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/sparse/SparseTensor.
---@field inputBaselines? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentList Baseline inputs for this feature. If no baseline is specified, Vertex AI chooses the baseline for this feature. If multiple baselines are specified, Vertex AI returns the average attributions across them in Attribution.feature_attributions. For Vertex AI-provided Tensorflow images (both 1.x and 2.x), the shape of each baseline must match the shape of the input tensor. If a scalar is provided, we broadcast to the same shape as the input tensor. For custom images, the element of the baselines must be in the same format as the feature's input in the instance[]. The schema of any single instance may be specified via Endpoint's DeployedModels' Model's PredictSchemata's instance_schema_uri.
---@field encodedTensorName? string Encoded tensor is a transformation of the input tensor. Must be provided if choosing Integrated Gradients attribution or XRAI attribution and the input tensor is not differentiable. An encoded tensor is generated if the input tensor is encoded by a lookup table.
---@field indexFeatureMapping? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList A list of feature names for each index in the input tensor. Required when the input InputMetadata.encoding is BAG_OF_FEATURES, BAG_OF_FEATURES_SPARSE, INDICATOR.
---@field featureValueDomain? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataFeatureValueDomain The domain details of the input feature value. Like min/max, original mean or standard deviation if normalized.
---@field modality? string Modality of the feature. Valid values are: numeric, image. Defaults to numeric.
---@field encodedBaselines? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentList A list of baselines for the encoded tensor. The shape of each baseline should match the shape of the encoded tensor. If a scalar is provided, Vertex AI broadcasts to the same shape as the encoded tensor.
---@field encoding? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataEncodingEnum|string Defines how the feature is encoded into the input tensor. Defaults to IDENTITY.
---@field denseShapeTensorName? string Specifies the shape of the values of the input if the input is a sparse representation. Refer to Tensorflow documentation for more details: https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/sparse/SparseTensor.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"IDENTITY"|"BAG_OF_FEATURES"|"BAG_OF_FEATURES_SPARSE"|"INDICATOR"|"COMBINED_EMBEDDING"|"CONCAT_EMBEDDING"

---Domain details of the input feature value. Provides numeric information about the feature, such as its range (min, max). If the feature has been pre-processed, for example with z-scoring, then it provides information about how to recover the original feature. For example, if the input feature is an image and it has been pre-processed to obtain 0-mean and stddev = 1 values, then original_mean, and original_stddev refer to the mean and stddev of the original feature (e.g. image tensor) from which input feature (with mean = 0 and stddev = 1) was obtained.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataFeatureValueDomain
---@field originalMean? number If this input feature has been normalized to a mean value of 0, the original_mean specifies the mean value of the domain prior to normalization.
---@field originalStddev? number If this input feature has been normalized to a standard deviation of 1.0, the original_stddev specifies the standard deviation of the domain prior to normalization.
---@field minValue? number The minimum permissible value for this feature.
---@field maxValue? number The maximum permissible value for this feature.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadata }

---Visualization configurations for image explanation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualization
---@field clipPercentLowerbound? number Excludes attributions below the specified percentile, from the highlighted areas. Defaults to 62.
---@field colorMap? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationColorMapEnum|string The color scheme used for the highlighted areas. Defaults to PINK_GREEN for Integrated Gradients attribution, which shows positive attributions in green and negative in pink. Defaults to VIRIDIS for XRAI attribution, which highlights the most influential regions in yellow and the least influential in blue.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationTypeEnum|string Type of the image visualization. Only applicable to Integrated Gradients attribution. OUTLINES shows regions of attribution, while PIXELS shows per-pixel attribution. Defaults to OUTLINES.
---@field overlayType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationOverlayTypeEnum|string How the original image is displayed in the visualization. Adjusting the overlay can help increase visual clarity if the original image makes it difficult to view the visualization. Defaults to NONE.
---@field polarity? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationPolarityEnum|string Whether to only highlight pixels with positive contributions, negative or both. Defaults to POSITIVE.
---@field clipPercentUpperbound? number Excludes attributions above the specified percentile from the highlighted areas. Using the clip_percent_upperbound and clip_percent_lowerbound together can be useful for filtering out noise and making it easier to see areas of strong attribution. Defaults to 99.9.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationColorMapEnum "COLOR_MAP_UNSPECIFIED"|"PINK_GREEN"|"VIRIDIS"|"RED"|"GREEN"|"RED_GREEN"|"PINK_WHITE_GREEN"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationOverlayTypeEnum "OVERLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"ORIGINAL"|"GRAYSCALE"|"MASK_BLACK"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationPolarityEnum "POLARITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"POSITIVE"|"NEGATIVE"|"BOTH"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataInputMetadataVisualizationTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PIXELS"|"OUTLINES"

---Metadata of the prediction output to be explained.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOutputMetadata
---@field outputTensorName? string Name of the output tensor. Required and is only applicable to Vertex AI provided images for Tensorflow.
---@field indexDisplayNameMapping? any Static mapping between the index and display name. Use this if the outputs are a deterministic n-dimensional array, e.g. a list of scores of all the classes in a pre-defined order for a multi-classification Model. It's not feasible if the outputs are non-deterministic, e.g. the Model produces top-k classes or sort the outputs by their values. The shape of the value must be an n-dimensional array of strings. The number of dimensions must match that of the outputs to be explained. The Attribution.output_display_name is populated by locating in the mapping with Attribution.output_index.
---@field displayNameMappingKey? string Specify a field name in the prediction to look for the display name. Use this if the prediction contains the display names for the outputs. The display names in the prediction must have the same shape of the outputs, so that it can be located by Attribution.output_index for a specific output.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOutputMetadataMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOutputMetadata }

---The ExplanationMetadata entries that can be overridden at online explanation time.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOverride
---@field inputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOverrideInputMetadataOverrideMap Required. Overrides the input metadata of the features. The key is the name of the feature to be overridden. The keys specified here must exist in the input metadata to be overridden. If a feature is not specified here, the corresponding feature's input metadata is not overridden.

---The input metadata entries to be overridden.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOverrideInputMetadataOverride
---@field inputBaselines? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentList Baseline inputs for this feature. This overrides the `input_baseline` field of the ExplanationMetadata.InputMetadata object of the corresponding feature's input metadata. If it's not specified, the original baselines are not overridden.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOverrideInputMetadataOverrideMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOverrideInputMetadataOverride }

---Parameters to configure explaining for Model's predictions.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationParameters
---@field examples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Examples Example-based explanations that returns the nearest neighbors from the provided dataset.
---@field integratedGradientsAttribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IntegratedGradientsAttribution An attribution method that computes Aumann-Shapley values taking advantage of the model's fully differentiable structure. Refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.01365
---@field topK? number If populated, returns attributions for top K indices of outputs (defaults to 1). Only applies to Models that predicts more than one outputs (e,g, multi-class Models). When set to -1, returns explanations for all outputs.
---@field sampledShapleyAttribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SampledShapleyAttribution An attribution method that approximates Shapley values for features that contribute to the label being predicted. A sampling strategy is used to approximate the value rather than considering all subsets of features. Refer to this paper for model details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1306.4265.
---@field xraiAttribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1XraiAttribution An attribution method that redistributes Integrated Gradients attribution to segmented regions, taking advantage of the model's fully differentiable structure. Refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.02825 XRAI currently performs better on natural images, like a picture of a house or an animal. If the images are taken in artificial environments, like a lab or manufacturing line, or from diagnostic equipment, like x-rays or quality-control cameras, use Integrated Gradients instead.
---@field outputIndices? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentList If populated, only returns attributions that have output_index contained in output_indices. It must be an ndarray of integers, with the same shape of the output it's explaining. If not populated, returns attributions for top_k indices of outputs. If neither top_k nor output_indices is populated, returns the argmax index of the outputs. Only applicable to Models that predict multiple outputs (e,g, multi-class Models that predict multiple classes).

---Specification of Model explanation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpec
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationParameters Required. Parameters that configure explaining of the Model's predictions.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadata Optional. Metadata describing the Model's input and output for explanation.

---The ExplanationSpec entries that can be overridden at online explanation time.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpecOverride
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationParameters The parameters to be overridden. Note that the attribution method cannot be changed. If not specified, no parameter is overridden.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationMetadataOverride The metadata to be overridden. If not specified, no metadata is overridden.
---@field examplesOverride? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExamplesOverride The example-based explanations parameter overrides.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpecOverrideMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpecOverride }

---Describes what part of the Dataset is to be exported, the destination of the export and how to export.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportDataConfig
---@field annotationsFilter? string An expression for filtering what part of the Dataset is to be exported. Only Annotations that match this filter will be exported. The filter syntax is the same as in ListAnnotations.
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination The Google Cloud Storage location where the output is to be written to. In the given directory a new directory will be created with name: `export-data--` where timestamp is in YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ ISO-8601 format. All export output will be written into that directory. Inside that directory, annotations with the same schema will be grouped into sub directories which are named with the corresponding annotations' schema title. Inside these sub directories, a schema.yaml will be created to describe the output format.
---@field fractionSplit? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportFractionSplit Split based on fractions defining the size of each set.

---Describes exporting all historical Feature values of all entities of the EntityType between [start_time, end_time].
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportFeatureValuesRequestFullExport
---@field endTime? string Exports Feature values as of this timestamp. If not set, retrieve values as of now. Timestamp, if present, must not have higher than millisecond precision.
---@field startTime? string Excludes Feature values with feature generation timestamp before this timestamp. If not set, retrieve oldest values kept in Feature Store. Timestamp, if present, must not have higher than millisecond precision.

---Describes exporting the latest Feature values of all entities of the EntityType between [start_time, snapshot_time].
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportFeatureValuesRequestSnapshotExport
---@field snapshotTime? string Exports Feature values as of this timestamp. If not set, retrieve values as of now. Timestamp, if present, must not have higher than millisecond precision.
---@field startTime? string Excludes Feature values with feature generation timestamp before this timestamp. If not set, retrieve oldest values kept in Feature Store. Timestamp, if present, must not have higher than millisecond precision.

---Assigns the input data to training, validation, and test sets as per the given fractions. Any of `training_fraction`, `validation_fraction` and `test_fraction` may optionally be provided, they must sum to up to 1. If the provided ones sum to less than 1, the remainder is assigned to sets as decided by Vertex AI. If none of the fractions are set, by default roughly 80% of data is used for training, 10% for validation, and 10% for test.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportFractionSplit
---@field trainingFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to train the Model.
---@field testFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to evaluate the Model.
---@field validationFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to validate the Model.

---Output configuration for the Model export.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportModelRequestOutputConfig
---@field imageDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ContainerRegistryDestination The Google Container Registry or Artifact Registry uri where the Model container image will be copied to. This field should only be set when the `exportableContent` field of the [Model.supported_export_formats] object contains `IMAGE`.
---@field artifactDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage location where the Model artifact is to be written to. Under the directory given as the destination a new one with name "`model-export--`", where timestamp is in YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ ISO-8601 format, will be created. Inside, the Model and any of its supporting files will be written. This field should only be set when the `exportableContent` field of the [Model.supported_export_formats] object contains `ARTIFACT`.
---@field exportFormatId? string The ID of the format in which the Model must be exported. Each Model lists the export formats it supports. If no value is provided here, then the first from the list of the Model's supported formats is used by default.

---Response message for TensorboardService.ExportTensorboardTimeSeriesData.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExportTensorboardTimeSeriesDataResponse
---@field timeSeriesDataPoints? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TimeSeriesDataPointList The returned time series data points.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token, which can be sent as page_token to retrieve the next page. If this field is omitted, there are no subsequent pages.

---The project for Vertex AI Express Mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExpressProject
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the project was created.
---@field tier? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExpressProjectTierEnum Output only. The tier of the project.
---@field defaultApiKey? string Output only. The default API key string of the project.
---@field projectNumber? string Output only. The number of the project.
---@field region? string Output only. The region of the project.
---@field projectId? string Output only. The ID of the project.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExpressProjectTierEnum "TIER_UNSPECIFIED"|"TIER_FREE"|"TIER_PAID"

---Extensions are tools for large language models to access external data, run computations, etc.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Extension
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Extension was created.
---@field toolUseExamples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolUseExampleList Optional. Examples to illustrate the usage of the extension as a tool.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field extensionOperations? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionOperationList Output only. Supported operations.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Extension was most recently updated.
---@field manifest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionManifest Required. Manifest of the Extension.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Extension. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field runtimeConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeConfig Optional. Runtime config controlling the runtime behavior of this Extension.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the Extension.
---@field privateServiceConnectConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionPrivateServiceConnectConfig Optional. The PrivateServiceConnect config for the extension. If specified, the service endpoints associated with the Extension should be [registered with private network access in the provided Service Directory](https://cloud.google.com/service-directory/docs/configuring-private-network-access). If the service contains more than one endpoint with a network, the service will arbitrarilty choose one of the endpoints to use for extension execution.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the Extension.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Extension[]

---Manifest spec of an Extension needed for runtime execution.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionManifest
---@field authConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AuthConfig Required. Immutable. Type of auth supported by this extension.
---@field apiSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionManifestApiSpec Required. Immutable. The API specification shown to the LLM.
---@field description? string Required. The natural language description shown to the LLM. It should describe the usage of the extension, and is essential for the LLM to perform reasoning. e.g., if the extension is a data store, you can let the LLM know what data it contains.
---@field name? string Required. Extension name shown to the LLM. The name can be up to 128 characters long.

---The API specification shown to the LLM.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionManifestApiSpec
---@field openApiGcsUri? string Cloud Storage URI pointing to the OpenAPI spec.
---@field openApiYaml? string The API spec in Open API standard and YAML format.

---Operation of an extension.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionOperation
---@field operationId? string Operation ID that uniquely identifies the operations among the extension. See: "Operation Object" in https://swagger.io/specification/. This field is parsed from the OpenAPI spec. For HTTP extensions, if it does not exist in the spec, we will generate one from the HTTP method and path.
---@field functionDeclaration? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclaration Output only. Structured representation of a function declaration as defined by the OpenAPI Spec.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionOperationList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExtensionOperation[]

