---Retrieve from data source powered by external API for grounding. The external API is not owned by Google, but need to follow the pre-defined API spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApi
---@field apiAuth? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ApiAuth The authentication config to access the API. Deprecated. Please use auth_config instead.
---@field elasticSearchParams? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApiElasticSearchParams Parameters for the elastic search API.
---@field endpoint? string The endpoint of the external API. The system will call the API at this endpoint to retrieve the data for grounding. Example: https://acme.com:443/search
---@field authConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AuthConfig The authentication config to access the API.
---@field simpleSearchParams? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApiSimpleSearchParams Parameters for the simple search API.
---@field apiSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApiApiSpecEnum|string The API spec that the external API implements.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApiApiSpecEnum "API_SPEC_UNSPECIFIED"|"SIMPLE_SEARCH"|"ELASTIC_SEARCH"

---The search parameters to use for the ELASTIC_SEARCH spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApiElasticSearchParams
---@field searchTemplate? string The ElasticSearch search template to use.
---@field numHits? number Optional. Number of hits (chunks) to request. When specified, it is passed to Elasticsearch as the `num_hits` param.
---@field index? string The ElasticSearch index to use.

---The search parameters to use for SIMPLE_SEARCH spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalApiSimpleSearchParams

---A browser on the connecting client (e.g. the user's own, signed-in Chrome) that a task's browser actions run on. The actions are relayed to the client, so the client must stay connected while they happen. The task's other operations (files, commands) still run where `environment_config` puts them.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalBrowser

---A directory on the connecting client (e.g. the user's local machine) mounted into a task's server-managed environment.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExternalMount
---@field mountPath? string Optional. Absolute path in the environment where the directory is mounted. Empty means `/workspace/desktop`. When set, must be `/workspace/{name}`, where `{name}` is 1-63 lowercase letters, digits, `_` or `-`, starts with a letter or digit, and is not one of the names other mounts own under `/workspace`: `skills`, `core`, `memory`, `inputs`, `artifacts`, `deliverables` or `userdata`.
---@field sourcePath? string Optional. Absolute path of the folder on the connecting client (the mount source). Interpreted only by the client; the server never resolves it.

---The fact used in grounding.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Fact
---@field summary? string If present, the summary/snippet of the fact.
---@field chunk? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagChunk If present, chunk properties.
---@field title? string If present, it refers to the title of this fact.
---@field uri? string If present, this uri links to the source of the fact.
---@field score? number If present, according to the underlying Vector DB and the selected metric type, the score can be either the distance or the similarity between the query and the fact and its range depends on the metric type. For example, if the metric type is COSINE_DISTANCE, it represents the distance between the query and the fact. The larger the distance, the less relevant the fact is to the query. The range is [0, 2], while 0 means the most relevant and 2 means the least relevant.
---@field vectorDistance? number If present, the distance between the query vector and this fact vector.
---@field query? string Query that is used to retrieve this fact.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FactList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Fact[]

---Represents a specific failed rubric and the associated analysis.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FailedRubric
---@field classificationRationale? string The rationale provided by the Loss Analysis Classifier for why this failure maps to this specific Loss Cluster. e.g., "The agent claimed an action without a tool call, matching 'Hallucination of Action'."
---@field rubricId? string The unique ID of the rubric (if available from the metric source). Clients use this ID to query the corresponding rubric verdict.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FailedRubricList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FailedRubric[]

---Configuration for faster model deployment.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FasterDeploymentConfig
---@field fastTryoutEnabled? boolean If true, enable fast tryout feature for this deployed model.

---Feature Metadata information. For example, color is a feature that describes an apple.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Feature
---@field pointOfContact? string Entity responsible for maintaining this feature. Can be comma separated list of email addresses or URIs.
---@field monitoringStats? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAnomalyList Output only. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). A list of historical SnapshotAnalysis stats requested by user, sorted by FeatureStatsAnomaly.start_time descending.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). Timestamp when this EntityType was created.
---@field featureStatsAndAnomaly? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAndAnomalyList Output only. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store. The list of historical stats and anomalies.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). Timestamp when this EntityType was most recently updated.
---@field monitoringConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfig Optional. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). Deprecated: The custom monitoring configuration for this Feature, if not set, use the monitoring_config defined for the EntityType this Feature belongs to. Only Features with type (Feature.ValueType) BOOL, STRING, DOUBLE or INT64 can enable monitoring. If this is populated with FeaturestoreMonitoringConfig.disabled = true, snapshot analysis monitoring is disabled; if FeaturestoreMonitoringConfig.monitoring_interval specified, snapshot analysis monitoring is enabled. Otherwise, snapshot analysis monitoring config is same as the EntityType's this Feature belongs to.
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field disableMonitoring? boolean Optional. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). If not set, use the monitoring_config defined for the EntityType this Feature belongs to. Only Features with type (Feature.ValueType) BOOL, STRING, DOUBLE or INT64 can enable monitoring. If set to true, all types of data monitoring are disabled despite the config on EntityType.
---@field description? string Description of the Feature.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Features. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information on and examples of labels. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Feature (System labels are excluded)." System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field name? string Immutable. Name of the Feature. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featurestores/{featurestore}/entityTypes/{entity_type}/features/{feature}` `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featureGroups/{feature_group}/features/{feature}` The last part feature is assigned by the client. The feature can be up to 64 characters long and can consist only of ASCII Latin letters A-Z and a-z, underscore(_), and ASCII digits 0-9 starting with a letter. The value will be unique given an entity type.
---@field versionColumnName? string Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store. The name of the BigQuery Table/View column hosting data for this version. If no value is provided, will use feature_id.
---@field monitoringStatsAnomalies? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureMonitoringStatsAnomalyList Output only. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). The list of historical stats and anomalies with specified objectives.
---@field valueType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueTypeEnum|string Immutable. Only applicable for Vertex AI Feature Store (Legacy). Type of Feature value.

---Vertex AI Feature Group.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroup
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the FeatureGroup.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this FeatureGroup was last updated.
---@field serviceAgentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupServiceAgentTypeEnum Optional. Service agent type used during jobs under a FeatureGroup. By default, the Vertex AI Service Agent is used. When using an IAM Policy to isolate this FeatureGroup within a project, a separate service account should be provisioned by setting this field to `SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_FEATURE_GROUP`. This will generate a separate service account to access the BigQuery source table.
---@field serviceAccountEmail? string Output only. A Service Account unique to this FeatureGroup. The role bigquery.dataViewer should be granted to this service account to allow Vertex AI Feature Store to access source data while running jobs under this FeatureGroup.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the FeatureGroup. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featureGroups/{featureGroup}`
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your FeatureGroup. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information on and examples of labels. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one FeatureGroup(System labels are excluded)." System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this FeatureGroup was created.
---@field bigQuery? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupBigQuery Indicates that features for this group come from BigQuery Table/View. By default treats the source as a sparse time series source. The BigQuery source table or view must have at least one entity ID column and a column named `feature_timestamp`.

---Input source type for BigQuery Tables and Views.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupBigQuery
---@field dense? boolean Optional. If set, all feature values will be fetched from a single row per unique entityId including nulls. If not set, will collapse all rows for each unique entityId into a singe row with any non-null values if present, if no non-null values are present will sync null. ex: If source has schema `(entity_id, feature_timestamp, f0, f1)` and the following rows: `(e1, 2020-01-01T10:00:00.123Z, 10, 15)` `(e1, 2020-02-01T10:00:00.123Z, 20, null)` If dense is set, `(e1, 20, null)` is synced to online stores. If dense is not set, `(e1, 20, 15)` is synced to online stores.
---@field timeSeries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupBigQueryTimeSeries Optional. If the source is a time-series source, this can be set to control how downstream sources (ex: FeatureView ) will treat time-series sources. If not set, will treat the source as a time-series source with `feature_timestamp` as timestamp column and no scan boundary.
---@field bigQuerySource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQuerySource Required. Immutable. The BigQuery source URI that points to either a BigQuery Table or View.
---@field entityIdColumns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Columns to construct entity_id / row keys. If not provided defaults to `entity_id`.
---@field staticDataSource? boolean Optional. Set if the data source is not a time-series.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupBigQueryTimeSeries
---@field timestampColumn? string Optional. Column hosting timestamp values for a time-series source. Will be used to determine the latest `feature_values` for each entity. Optional. If not provided, column named `feature_timestamp` of type `TIMESTAMP` will be used.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroup[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureGroupServiceAgentTypeEnum "SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_PROJECT"|"SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_FEATURE_GROUP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Feature[]

