---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreStateEnum Output only. State of the featureOnlineStore.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this FeatureOnlineStore was last updated.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your FeatureOnlineStore. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information on and examples of labels. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one FeatureOnlineStore(System labels are excluded)." System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this FeatureOnlineStore was created.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field dedicatedServingEndpoint? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreDedicatedServingEndpoint Optional. The dedicated serving endpoint for this FeatureOnlineStore, which is different from common Vertex service endpoint.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for data storage. If set, online store will be secured by this key.
---@field embeddingManagement? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreEmbeddingManagement Optional. Deprecated: This field is no longer needed anymore and embedding management is automatically enabled when specifying Optimized storage type.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field bigtable? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreBigtable Contains settings for the Cloud Bigtable instance that will be created to serve featureValues for all FeatureViews under this FeatureOnlineStore.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the FeatureOnlineStore. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featureOnlineStores/{featureOnlineStore}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreBigtable
---@field autoScaling? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreBigtableAutoScaling Required. Autoscaling config applied to Bigtable Instance.
---@field enableDirectBigtableAccess? boolean Optional. It true, enable direct access to the Bigtable instance.
---@field bigtableMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreBigtableBigtableMetadata Output only. Metadata of the Bigtable instance. Output only.
---@field zone? string Optional. The zone where the underlying Bigtable cluster for the primary Bigtable instance will be provisioned. Only the zone must be provided. For example, only "us-central1-a" should be provided.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreBigtableAutoScaling
---@field maxNodeCount? number Required. The maximum number of nodes to scale up to. Must be greater than or equal to min_node_count, and less than or equal to 10 times of 'min_node_count'.
---@field cpuUtilizationTarget? number Optional. A percentage of the cluster's CPU capacity. Can be from 10% to 80%. When a cluster's CPU utilization exceeds the target that you have set, Bigtable immediately adds nodes to the cluster. When CPU utilization is substantially lower than the target, Bigtable removes nodes. If not set will default to 50%.
---@field minNodeCount? number Required. The minimum number of nodes to scale down to. Must be greater than or equal to 1.

---Metadata of the Bigtable instance. This is used by direct read access to the Bigtable in tenant project.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreBigtableBigtableMetadata
---@field tenantProjectId? string Tenant project ID.
---@field tableId? string The Cloud Bigtable table id.
---@field instanceId? string The Cloud Bigtable instance id.

---The dedicated serving endpoint for this FeatureOnlineStore. Only need to set when you choose Optimized storage type. Public endpoint is provisioned by default.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreDedicatedServingEndpoint
---@field serviceAttachment? string Output only. The name of the service attachment resource. Populated if private service connect is enabled and after FeatureViewSync is created.
---@field privateServiceConnectConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrivateServiceConnectConfig Optional. Private service connect config. The private service connection is available only for Optimized storage type, not for embedding management now. If PrivateServiceConnectConfig.enable_private_service_connect set to true, customers will use private service connection to send request. Otherwise, the connection will set to public endpoint.
---@field publicEndpointDomainName? string Output only. This field will be populated with the domain name to use for this FeatureOnlineStore

---Deprecated: This sub message is no longer needed anymore and embedding management is automatically enabled when specifying Optimized storage type. Contains settings for embedding management.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreEmbeddingManagement
---@field enabled? boolean Optional. Immutable. Whether to enable embedding management in this FeatureOnlineStore. It's immutable after creation to ensure the FeatureOnlineStore availability.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStore[]

---Optimized storage type
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreOptimized

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureOnlineStoreStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STABLE"|"UPDATING"

---Feature selection configuration for the FeatureMonitor.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureSelectionConfig
---@field featureConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureSelectionConfigFeatureConfigList Optional. A list of features to be monitored and each feature's drift threshold.

---Feature configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureSelectionConfigFeatureConfig
---@field featureId? string Required. The ID of the feature resource. Final component of the Feature's resource name.
---@field driftThreshold? number Optional. Drift threshold. If calculated difference with baseline data larger than threshold, it will be considered as the feature has drift. If not present, the threshold will be default to 0.3. Must be in range [0, 1).

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureSelectionConfigFeatureConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureSelectionConfigFeatureConfig[]

---Selector for Features of an EntityType.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureSelector
---@field idMatcher? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IdMatcher Required. Matches Features based on ID.

---Stats and Anomaly generated by FeatureMonitorJobs. Anomaly only includes Drift.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAndAnomaly
---@field distributionDeviation? number Deviation from the current stats to baseline stats. 1. For categorical feature, the distribution distance is calculated by L-inifinity norm. 2. For numerical feature, the distribution distance is calculated by Jensen–Shannon divergence.
---@field driftDetected? boolean If set to true, indicates current stats is detected as and comparing with baseline stats.
---@field featureId? string Feature Id.
---@field statsTime? string The timestamp we take snapshot for feature values to generate stats.
---@field driftDetectionThreshold? number This is the threshold used when detecting drifts, which is set in FeatureMonitor.FeatureSelectionConfig.FeatureConfig.drift_threshold
---@field featureStats? any Feature stats. e.g. histogram buckets. In the format of tensorflow.metadata.v0.DatasetFeatureStatistics.
---@field featureMonitorId? string The ID of the FeatureMonitor that this FeatureStatsAndAnomaly generated according to.
---@field featureMonitorJobId? string The ID of the FeatureMonitorJob that generated this FeatureStatsAndAnomaly.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAndAnomalyList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAndAnomaly[]

---Stats and Anomaly generated at specific timestamp for specific Feature. The start_time and end_time are used to define the time range of the dataset that current stats belongs to, e.g. prediction traffic is bucketed into prediction datasets by time window. If the Dataset is not defined by time window, start_time = end_time. Timestamp of the stats and anomalies always refers to end_time. Raw stats and anomalies are stored in stats_uri or anomaly_uri in the tensorflow defined protos. Field data_stats contains almost identical information with the raw stats in Vertex AI defined proto, for UI to display.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAnomaly
---@field score? number Feature importance score, only populated when cross-feature monitoring is enabled. For now only used to represent feature attribution score within range [0, 1] for ModelDeploymentMonitoringObjectiveType.FEATURE_ATTRIBUTION_SKEW and ModelDeploymentMonitoringObjectiveType.FEATURE_ATTRIBUTION_DRIFT.
---@field startTime? string The start timestamp of window where stats were generated. For objectives where time window doesn't make sense (e.g. Featurestore Snapshot Monitoring), start_time is only used to indicate the monitoring intervals, so it always equals to (end_time - monitoring_interval).
---@field statsUri? string Path of the stats file for current feature values in Cloud Storage bucket. Format: gs:////stats. Example: gs://monitoring_bucket/feature_name/stats. Stats are stored as binary format with Protobuf message [tensorflow.metadata.v0.FeatureNameStatistics](https://github.com/tensorflow/metadata/blob/master/tensorflow_metadata/proto/v0/statistics.proto).
---@field distributionDeviation? number Deviation from the current stats to baseline stats. 1. For categorical feature, the distribution distance is calculated by L-inifinity norm. 2. For numerical feature, the distribution distance is calculated by Jensen–Shannon divergence.
---@field endTime? string The end timestamp of window where stats were generated. For objectives where time window doesn't make sense (e.g. Featurestore Snapshot Monitoring), end_time indicates the timestamp of the data used to generate stats (e.g. timestamp we take snapshots for feature values).
---@field anomalyUri? string Path of the anomaly file for current feature values in Cloud Storage bucket. Format: gs:////anomalies. Example: gs://monitoring_bucket/feature_name/anomalies. Stats are stored as binary format with Protobuf message Anoamlies are stored as binary format with Protobuf message [tensorflow.metadata.v0.AnomalyInfo] (https://github.com/tensorflow/metadata/blob/master/tensorflow_metadata/proto/v0/anomalies.proto).
---@field anomalyDetectionThreshold? number This is the threshold used when detecting anomalies. The threshold can be changed by user, so this one might be different from ThresholdConfig.value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAnomalyList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureStatsAnomaly[]

---Value for a feature.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValue
---@field int64Value? string Int64 feature value.
---@field boolArrayValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BoolArray A list of bool type feature value.
---@field bytesValue? string Bytes feature value.
---@field stringArrayValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1StringArray A list of string type feature value.
---@field boolValue? boolean Bool type feature value.
---@field int64ArrayValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Int64Array A list of int64 type feature value.
---@field doubleArrayValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DoubleArray A list of double type feature value.
---@field structValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1StructValue A struct type feature value.
---@field stringValue? string String feature value.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueMetadata Metadata of feature value.
---@field doubleValue? number Double type feature value.

---A destination location for Feature values and format.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueDestination
---@field tfrecordDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TFRecordDestination Output in TFRecord format. Below are the mapping from Feature value type in Featurestore to Feature value type in TFRecord: Value type in Featurestore | Value type in TFRecord DOUBLE, DOUBLE_ARRAY | FLOAT_LIST INT64, INT64_ARRAY | INT64_LIST STRING, STRING_ARRAY, BYTES | BYTES_LIST true -> byte_string("true"), false -> byte_string("false") BOOL, BOOL_ARRAY (true, false) | BYTES_LIST
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination Output in BigQuery format. BigQueryDestination.output_uri in FeatureValueDestination.bigquery_destination must refer to a table.
---@field csvDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CsvDestination Output in CSV format. Array Feature value types are not allowed in CSV format.

---Container for list of values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueList
---@field values? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueList_ A list of feature values. All of them should be the same data type.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueList_ gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValue[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValue }

---Metadata of feature value.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueMetadata
---@field generateTime? string Feature generation timestamp. Typically, it is provided by user at feature ingestion time. If not, feature store will use the system timestamp when the data is ingested into feature store. Legacy Feature Store: For streaming ingestion, the time, aligned by days, must be no older than five years (1825 days) and no later than one year (366 days) in the future.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValueTypeEnum "VALUE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BOOL"|"BOOL_ARRAY"|"DOUBLE"|"DOUBLE_ARRAY"|"INT64"|"INT64_ARRAY"|"STRING"|"STRING_ARRAY"|"BYTES"|"STRUCT"

---FeatureView is representation of values that the FeatureOnlineStore will serve based on its syncConfig.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureView
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field optimizedConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewOptimizedConfig Optional. Configuration for FeatureView created under Optimized FeatureOnlineStore.
---@field bigtableMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewBigtableMetadata Output only. Metadata containing information about the Cloud Bigtable.
---@field syncConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSyncConfig Configures when data is to be synced/updated for this FeatureView. At the end of the sync the latest featureValues for each entityId of this FeatureView are made ready for online serving.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the FeatureView. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featureOnlineStores/{feature_online_store}/featureViews/{feature_view}`
---@field vectorSearchConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfig Optional. Deprecated: please use FeatureView.index_config instead.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field indexConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfig Optional. Configuration for index preparation for vector search. It contains the required configurations to create an index from source data, so that approximate nearest neighbor (a.k.a ANN) algorithms search can be performed during online serving.
---@field bigQuerySource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewBigQuerySource Optional. Configures how data is supposed to be extracted from a BigQuery source to be loaded onto the FeatureOnlineStore.
---@field featureRegistrySource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewFeatureRegistrySource Optional. Configures the features from a Feature Registry source that need to be loaded onto the FeatureOnlineStore.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this FeatureView was last updated.
---@field serviceAccountEmail? string Output only. A Service Account unique to this FeatureView. The role bigquery.dataViewer should be granted to this service account to allow Vertex AI Feature Store to sync data to the online store.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this FeatureView was created.
---@field serviceAgentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewServiceAgentTypeEnum Optional. Service agent type used during data sync. By default, the Vertex AI Service Agent is used. When using an IAM Policy to isolate this FeatureView within a project, a separate service account should be provisioned by setting this field to `SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_FEATURE_VIEW`. This will generate a separate service account to access the BigQuery source table.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your FeatureViews. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information on and examples of labels. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one FeatureOnlineStore(System labels are excluded)." System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field vertexRagSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVertexRagSource Optional. The Vertex RAG Source that the FeatureView is linked to.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewBigQuerySource
---@field uri? string Required. The BigQuery view URI that will be materialized on each sync trigger based on FeatureView.SyncConfig.
---@field entityIdColumns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Columns to construct entity_id / row keys.

---Metadata for the Cloud Bigtable that supports directly interacting Bigtable instances.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewBigtableMetadata
---@field readAppProfile? string Output only. The Bigtable App Profile to use for reading from Bigtable.

---Lookup key for a feature view.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKey
---@field key? string String key to use for lookup.
---@field compositeKey? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKeyCompositeKey The actual Entity ID will be composed from this struct. This should match with the way ID is defined in the FeatureView spec.

---ID that is comprised from several parts (columns).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKeyCompositeKey
---@field parts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Parts to construct Entity ID. Should match with the same ID columns as defined in FeatureView in the same order.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKeyList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKey[]

---A data key and associated feature values to write to the feature view.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValues
---@field dataKey? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKey The data key.
---@field features? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesFeatureList List of features to write.

---Feature name & value pair.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesFeature
---@field value? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValue Feature value. A user provided timestamp may be set in the `FeatureValue.metadata.generate_time` field.
---@field name? string Feature short name.
---@field valueAndTimestamp? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesFeatureFeatureValueAndTimestamp Feature value and timestamp.

---Feature value and timestamp.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesFeatureFeatureValueAndTimestamp
---@field timestamp? string The feature timestamp to store with this value. If not set, then the Feature Store server will generate a timestamp when it receives the write request.
---@field value? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValue The feature value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesFeatureList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesFeature[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValuesList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteRequestDataKeyAndFeatureValues[]

---Response message for FeatureOnlineStoreService.FeatureViewDirectWrite.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteResponse
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Response status for the keys listed in FeatureViewDirectWriteResponse.write_responses. The error only applies to the listed data keys - the stream will remain open for further FeatureOnlineStoreService.FeatureViewDirectWriteRequest requests. Partial failures (e.g. if the first 10 keys of a request fail, but the rest succeed) from a single request may result in multiple responses - there will be one response for the successful request keys and one response for the failing request keys.
---@field writeResponses? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteResponseWriteResponseList Details about write for each key. If status is not OK, WriteResponse.data_key will have the key with error, but WriteResponse.online_store_write_time will not be present.

---Details about the write for each key.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteResponseWriteResponse
---@field dataKey? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKey What key is this write response associated with.
---@field onlineStoreWriteTime? string When the feature values were written to the online store. If FeatureViewDirectWriteResponse.status is not OK, this field is not populated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteResponseWriteResponseList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDirectWriteResponseWriteResponse[]

---A Feature Registry source for features that need to be synced to Online Store.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewFeatureRegistrySource
---@field projectNumber? string Optional. The project number of the parent project of the Feature Groups.
---@field featureGroups? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewFeatureRegistrySourceFeatureGroupList Required. List of features that need to be synced to Online Store.

---Features belonging to a single feature group that will be synced to Online Store.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewFeatureRegistrySourceFeatureGroup
---@field featureGroupId? string Required. Identifier of the feature group.
---@field featureIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Identifiers of features under the feature group.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewFeatureRegistrySourceFeatureGroupList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewFeatureRegistrySourceFeatureGroup[]

---Configuration for vector indexing.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfig
---@field treeAhConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfigTreeAHConfig Optional. Configuration options for the tree-AH algorithm (Shallow tree + Asymmetric Hashing). Please refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.10396
---@field distanceMeasureType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfigDistanceMeasureTypeEnum|string Optional. The distance measure used in nearest neighbor search.
---@field embeddingDimension? number Optional. The number of dimensions of the input embedding.
---@field bruteForceConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfigBruteForceConfig Optional. Configuration options for using brute force search, which simply implements the standard linear search in the database for each query. It is primarily meant for benchmarking and to generate the ground truth for approximate search.
---@field filterColumns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Columns of features that're used to filter vector search results.
---@field embeddingColumn? string Optional. Column of embedding. This column contains the source data to create index for vector search. embedding_column must be set when using vector search.
---@field crowdingColumn? string Optional. Column of crowding. This column contains crowding attribute which is a constraint on a neighbor list produced by FeatureOnlineStoreService.SearchNearestEntities to diversify search results. If NearestNeighborQuery.per_crowding_attribute_neighbor_count is set to K in SearchNearestEntitiesRequest, it's guaranteed that no more than K entities of the same crowding attribute are returned in the response.

---Configuration options for using brute force search.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfigBruteForceConfig

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfigDistanceMeasureTypeEnum "DISTANCE_MEASURE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SQUARED_L2_DISTANCE"|"COSINE_DISTANCE"|"DOT_PRODUCT_DISTANCE"

---Configuration options for the tree-AH algorithm.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewIndexConfigTreeAHConfig
---@field leafNodeEmbeddingCount? string Optional. Number of embeddings on each leaf node. The default value is 1000 if not set.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureView[]

---Configuration for FeatureViews created in Optimized FeatureOnlineStore.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewOptimizedConfig
---@field automaticResources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AutomaticResources Optional. A description of resources that the FeatureView uses, which to large degree are decided by Vertex AI, and optionally allows only a modest additional configuration. If min_replica_count is not set, the default value is 2. If max_replica_count is not set, the default value is 6. The max allowed replica count is 1000.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewServiceAgentTypeEnum "SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_PROJECT"|"SERVICE_AGENT_TYPE_FEATURE_VIEW"

---FeatureViewSync is a representation of sync operation which copies data from data source to Feature View in Online Store.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSync
---@field finalStatus? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Final status of the FeatureViewSync.
---@field runTime? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleTypeInterval Output only. Time when this FeatureViewSync is finished.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field syncSummary? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSyncSyncSummary Output only. Summary of the sync job.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the FeatureViewSync. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featureOnlineStores/{feature_online_store}/featureViews/{feature_view}/featureViewSyncs/{feature_view_sync}`
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when this FeatureViewSync is created. Creation of a FeatureViewSync means that the job is pending / waiting for sufficient resources but may not have started the actual data transfer yet.

---Configuration for Sync. Only one option is set.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSyncConfig
---@field continuous? boolean Optional. If true, syncs the FeatureView in a continuous manner to Online Store.
---@field cron? string Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) to launch scheduled runs. To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or "TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, "CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *", or "TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *".

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSyncList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSync[]

---Summary from the Sync job. For continuous syncs, the summary is updated periodically. For batch syncs, it gets updated on completion of the sync.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewSyncSyncSummary
---@field systemWatermarkTime? string Lower bound of the system time watermark for the sync job. This is only set for continuously syncing feature views.
---@field totalSlot? string Output only. BigQuery slot milliseconds consumed for the sync job.
---@field rowSynced? string Output only. Total number of rows synced.

---Deprecated. Use IndexConfig instead.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfig
---@field crowdingColumn? string Optional. Column of crowding. This column contains crowding attribute which is a constraint on a neighbor list produced by FeatureOnlineStoreService.SearchNearestEntities to diversify search results. If NearestNeighborQuery.per_crowding_attribute_neighbor_count is set to K in SearchNearestEntitiesRequest, it's guaranteed that no more than K entities of the same crowding attribute are returned in the response.
---@field embeddingColumn? string Optional. Column of embedding. This column contains the source data to create index for vector search. embedding_column must be set when using vector search.
---@field distanceMeasureType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfigDistanceMeasureTypeEnum|string Optional. The distance measure used in nearest neighbor search.
---@field treeAhConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfigTreeAHConfig Optional. Configuration options for the tree-AH algorithm (Shallow tree + Asymmetric Hashing). Please refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.10396
---@field filterColumns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Columns of features that're used to filter vector search results.
---@field embeddingDimension? number Optional. The number of dimensions of the input embedding.
---@field bruteForceConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfigBruteForceConfig Optional. Configuration options for using brute force search, which simply implements the standard linear search in the database for each query. It is primarily meant for benchmarking and to generate the ground truth for approximate search.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfigBruteForceConfig

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfigDistanceMeasureTypeEnum "DISTANCE_MEASURE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SQUARED_L2_DISTANCE"|"COSINE_DISTANCE"|"DOT_PRODUCT_DISTANCE"

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVectorSearchConfigTreeAHConfig
---@field leafNodeEmbeddingCount? string Optional. Number of embeddings on each leaf node. The default value is 1000 if not set.

---A Vertex Rag source for features that need to be synced to Online Store.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewVertexRagSource
---@field uri? string Required. The BigQuery view/table URI that will be materialized on each manual sync trigger. The table/view is expected to have the following columns and types at least: - `corpus_id` (STRING, NULLABLE/REQUIRED) - `file_id` (STRING, NULLABLE/REQUIRED) - `chunk_id` (STRING, NULLABLE/REQUIRED) - `chunk_data_type` (STRING, NULLABLE/REQUIRED) - `chunk_data` (STRING, NULLABLE/REQUIRED) - `embeddings` (FLOAT, REPEATED) - `file_original_uri` (STRING, NULLABLE/REQUIRED)
---@field ragCorpusId? string Optional. The RAG corpus id corresponding to this FeatureView.

---Vertex AI Feature Store provides a centralized repository for organizing, storing, and serving ML features. The Featurestore is a top-level container for your features and their values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Featurestore
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field etag? string Optional. Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Featurestore was last updated.
---@field onlineStorageTtlDays? number Optional. TTL in days for feature values that will be stored in online serving storage. The Feature Store online storage periodically removes obsolete feature values older than `online_storage_ttl_days` since the feature generation time. Note that `online_storage_ttl_days` should be less than or equal to `offline_storage_ttl_days` for each EntityType under a featurestore. If not set, default to 4000 days
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreStateEnum Output only. State of the featurestore.
---@field onlineServingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreOnlineServingConfig Optional. Config for online storage resources. The field should not co-exist with the field of `OnlineStoreReplicationConfig`. If both of it and OnlineStoreReplicationConfig are unset, the feature store will not have an online store and cannot be used for online serving.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Featurestore. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information on and examples of labels. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Featurestore(System labels are excluded)." System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of the Featurestore. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/featurestores/{featurestore}`
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Customer-managed encryption key spec for data storage. If set, both of the online and offline data storage will be secured by this key.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Featurestore was created.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Featurestore[]

---Configuration of how features in Featurestore are monitored.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfig
---@field categoricalThresholdConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigThresholdConfig Threshold for categorical features of anomaly detection. This is shared by all types of Featurestore Monitoring for categorical features (i.e. Features with type (Feature.ValueType) BOOL or STRING).
---@field importFeaturesAnalysis? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigImportFeaturesAnalysis The config for ImportFeatures Analysis Based Feature Monitoring.
---@field numericalThresholdConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigThresholdConfig Threshold for numerical features of anomaly detection. This is shared by all objectives of Featurestore Monitoring for numerical features (i.e. Features with type (Feature.ValueType) DOUBLE or INT64).
---@field snapshotAnalysis? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigSnapshotAnalysis The config for Snapshot Analysis Based Feature Monitoring.

---Configuration of the Featurestore's ImportFeature Analysis Based Monitoring. This type of analysis generates statistics for values of each Feature imported by every ImportFeatureValues operation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigImportFeaturesAnalysis
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigImportFeaturesAnalysisStateEnum|string Whether to enable / disable / inherite default hebavior for import features analysis.
---@field anomalyDetectionBaseline? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigImportFeaturesAnalysisAnomalyDetectionBaselineEnum|string The baseline used to do anomaly detection for the statistics generated by import features analysis.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigImportFeaturesAnalysisAnomalyDetectionBaselineEnum "BASELINE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LATEST_STATS"|"MOST_RECENT_SNAPSHOT_STATS"|"PREVIOUS_IMPORT_FEATURES_STATS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigImportFeaturesAnalysisStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DEFAULT"|"ENABLED"|"DISABLED"

---Configuration of the Featurestore's Snapshot Analysis Based Monitoring. This type of analysis generates statistics for each Feature based on a snapshot of the latest feature value of each entities every monitoring_interval.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigSnapshotAnalysis
---@field disabled? boolean The monitoring schedule for snapshot analysis. For EntityType-level config: unset / disabled = true indicates disabled by default for Features under it; otherwise by default enable snapshot analysis monitoring with monitoring_interval for Features under it. Feature-level config: disabled = true indicates disabled regardless of the EntityType-level config; unset monitoring_interval indicates going with EntityType-level config; otherwise run snapshot analysis monitoring with monitoring_interval regardless of the EntityType-level config. Explicitly Disable the snapshot analysis based monitoring.
---@field stalenessDays? number Customized export features time window for snapshot analysis. Unit is one day. Default value is 3 weeks. Minimum value is 1 day. Maximum value is 4000 days.
---@field monitoringIntervalDays? number Configuration of the snapshot analysis based monitoring pipeline running interval. The value indicates number of days.
---@field monitoringInterval? string Configuration of the snapshot analysis based monitoring pipeline running interval. The value is rolled up to full day. If both monitoring_interval_days and the deprecated `monitoring_interval` field are set when creating/updating EntityTypes/Features, monitoring_interval_days will be used.

---The config for Featurestore Monitoring threshold.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreMonitoringConfigThresholdConfig
---@field value? number Specify a threshold value that can trigger the alert. 1. For categorical feature, the distribution distance is calculated by L-inifinity norm. 2. For numerical feature, the distribution distance is calculated by Jensen–Shannon divergence. Each feature must have a non-zero threshold if they need to be monitored. Otherwise no alert will be triggered for that feature.

---OnlineServingConfig specifies the details for provisioning online serving resources.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreOnlineServingConfig
---@field fixedNodeCount? number The number of nodes for the online store. The number of nodes doesn't scale automatically, but you can manually update the number of nodes. If set to 0, the featurestore will not have an online store and cannot be used for online serving.
---@field scaling? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreOnlineServingConfigScaling Online serving scaling configuration. Only one of `fixed_node_count` and `scaling` can be set. Setting one will reset the other.

---Online serving scaling configuration. If min_node_count and max_node_count are set to the same value, the cluster will be configured with the fixed number of node (no auto-scaling).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreOnlineServingConfigScaling
---@field maxNodeCount? number The maximum number of nodes to scale up to. Must be greater than min_node_count, and less than or equal to 10 times of 'min_node_count'.
---@field minNodeCount? number Required. The minimum number of nodes to scale down to. Must be greater than or equal to 1.
---@field cpuUtilizationTarget? number Optional. The cpu utilization that the Autoscaler should be trying to achieve. This number is on a scale from 0 (no utilization) to 100 (total utilization), and is limited between 10 and 80. When a cluster's CPU utilization exceeds the target that you have set, Bigtable immediately adds nodes to the cluster. When CPU utilization is substantially lower than the target, Bigtable removes nodes. If not set or set to 0, default to 50.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeaturestoreStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STABLE"|"UPDATING"

---Feedback context is a resource that represents additional information about the conversation where the feedback was given, such as the conversation history, system instructions, etc. If provided, feedback context allows to correlate the feedback with the conversation, even if the original session is deleted or not available.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeedbackContext
---@field contextEvents? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SessionEventList Optional. The session events from the originating session.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name. Assigned by the server on create. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/feedbackEntries/{feedback_entry}/feedbackContext`

---FeedbackEntry is a resource that represents a user's feedback on a conversation with an agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeedbackEntry
---@field sessionId? string Required. The ID of the session that the feedback relates to.
---@field feedbackText? string Optional. Qualitative free-form comments provided by the user.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time at which the entry was created.
---@field userId? string Optional. A caller-supplied identifier for the user who provided the feedback. The semantics of this field (for example whether it is an opaque token, a hashed value, or a user-visible identifier) are determined by the calling application.
---@field eventId? string Required. The ID of the event within the session that the feedback relates to.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time at which the entry was most recently updated.
---@field source? string Optional. The surface that the feedback originated from.
---@field customMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Additional key-value metadata associated with the feedback.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name. Assigned by the server on create. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/feedbackEntries/{feedback_entry}`
---@field feedbackType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeedbackEntryFeedbackTypeEnum Required. The coarse-grained type of feedback provided by the user. Must be set to a value other than `FEEDBACK_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED`.
---@field feedbackLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeedbackEntryFeedbackTypeEnum "FEEDBACK_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"THUMBS_UP"|"THUMBS_DOWN"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeedbackEntryList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeedbackEntry[]

---Response message for ExampleStoreService.FetchExamples.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchExamplesResponse
---@field examples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExampleList The examples in the Example Store that satisfy the metadata filters.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token, which can be sent as FetchExamplesRequest.page_token to retrieve the next page. Absence of this field indicates there are no subsequent pages.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesRequestDataFormatEnum "FEATURE_VIEW_DATA_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"KEY_VALUE"|"PROTO_STRUCT"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesRequestFormatEnum "FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"KEY_VALUE"|"PROTO_STRUCT"

---Response message for FeatureOnlineStoreService.FetchFeatureValues
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponse
---@field protoStruct? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Feature values in proto Struct format.
---@field keyValues? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseFeatureNameValuePairList Feature values in KeyValue format.
---@field dataKey? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureViewDataKey The data key associated with this response. Will only be populated for FeatureOnlineStoreService.StreamingFetchFeatureValues RPCs.

---Response structure in the format of key (feature name) and (feature) value pair.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseFeatureNameValuePairList
---@field features? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseFeatureNameValuePairListFeatureNameValuePairList List of feature names and values.

---Feature name & value pair.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseFeatureNameValuePairListFeatureNameValuePair
---@field name? string Feature short name.
---@field value? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FeatureValue Feature value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseFeatureNameValuePairListFeatureNameValuePairList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseFeatureNameValuePairListFeatureNameValuePair[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponseList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FetchFeatureValuesResponse[]

---URI-based data. A FileData message contains a URI pointing to data of a specific media type. It is used to represent images, audio, and video stored in Google Cloud Storage.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FileData
---@field mimeType? string Required. The IANA standard MIME type of the source data.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the file. Used to provide a label or filename to distinguish files. This field is only returned in `PromptMessage` for prompt management. It is used in the Gemini calls only when server side tools (`code_execution`, `google_search`, and `url_context`) are enabled.
---@field fileUri? string Required. The URI of the file in Google Cloud Storage.

---RagFile status.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FileStatus
---@field errorStatus? string Output only. Only when the `state` field is ERROR.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FileStatusStateEnum Output only. RagFile state.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FileStatusStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"ERROR"

---Assigns input data to training, validation, and test sets based on the given filters, data pieces not matched by any filter are ignored. Currently only supported for Datasets containing DataItems. If any of the filters in this message are to match nothing, then they can be set as '-' (the minus sign). Supported only for unstructured Datasets.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FilterSplit
---@field validationFilter? string Required. A filter on DataItems of the Dataset. DataItems that match this filter are used to validate the Model. A filter with same syntax as the one used in DatasetService.ListDataItems may be used. If a single DataItem is matched by more than one of the FilterSplit filters, then it is assigned to the first set that applies to it in the training, validation, test order.
---@field trainingFilter? string Required. A filter on DataItems of the Dataset. DataItems that match this filter are used to train the Model. A filter with same syntax as the one used in DatasetService.ListDataItems may be used. If a single DataItem is matched by more than one of the FilterSplit filters, then it is assigned to the first set that applies to it in the training, validation, test order.
---@field testFilter? string Required. A filter on DataItems of the Dataset. DataItems that match this filter are used to test the Model. A filter with same syntax as the one used in DatasetService.ListDataItems may be used. If a single DataItem is matched by more than one of the FilterSplit filters, then it is assigned to the first set that applies to it in the training, validation, test order.

---A query to find a number of the nearest neighbors (most similar vectors) of a vector.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsRequestQuery
---@field neighborCount? number The number of nearest neighbors to be retrieved from database for each query. If not set, will use the default from the service configuration (https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/matching-engine/configuring-indexes#nearest-neighbor-search-config).
---@field approximateNeighborCount? number The number of neighbors to find via approximate search before exact reordering is performed. If not set, the default value from scam config is used; if set, this value must be > 0.
---@field rrf? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsRequestQueryRRF Optional. Represents RRF algorithm that combines search results.
---@field datapoint? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapoint Required. The datapoint/vector whose nearest neighbors should be searched for.
---@field fractionLeafNodesToSearchOverride? number The fraction of the number of leaves to search, set at query time allows user to tune search performance. This value increase result in both search accuracy and latency increase. The value should be between 0.0 and 1.0. If not set or set to 0.0, query uses the default value specified in NearestNeighborSearchConfig.TreeAHConfig.fraction_leaf_nodes_to_search.
---@field perCrowdingAttributeNeighborCount? number Crowding is a constraint on a neighbor list produced by nearest neighbor search requiring that no more than some value k' of the k neighbors returned have the same value of crowding_attribute. It's used for improving result diversity. This field is the maximum number of matches with the same crowding tag.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsRequestQueryList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsRequestQuery[]

---Parameters for RRF algorithm that combines search results.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsRequestQueryRRF
---@field alpha? number Required. Users can provide an alpha value to give more weight to dense vs sparse results. For example, if the alpha is 0, we only return sparse and if the alpha is 1, we only return dense.

---The response message for MatchService.FindNeighbors.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponse
---@field nearestNeighbors? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNearestNeighborsList The nearest neighbors of the query datapoints.

---Nearest neighbors for one query.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNearestNeighbors
---@field id? string The ID of the query datapoint.
---@field neighbors? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNeighborList All its neighbors.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNearestNeighborsList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNearestNeighbors[]

---A neighbor of the query vector.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNeighbor
---@field distance? number The distance between the neighbor and the dense embedding query.
---@field sparseDistance? number The distance between the neighbor and the query sparse_embedding.
---@field datapoint? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapoint The datapoint of the neighbor. Note that full datapoints are returned only when "return_full_datapoint" is set to true. Otherwise, only the "datapoint_id" and "crowding_tag" fields are populated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNeighborList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FindNeighborsResponseNeighbor[]

---FlexStart is used to schedule the deployment workload on DWS resource. It contains the max duration of the deployment.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FlexStart
---@field maxRuntimeDuration? string The max duration of the deployment is max_runtime_duration. The deployment will be terminated after the duration. The max_runtime_duration can be set up to 7 days.

---Input for fluency metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FluencyInput
---@field instance? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FluencyInstance Required. Fluency instance.
---@field metricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FluencySpec Required. Spec for fluency score metric.

---Spec for fluency instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FluencyInstance
---@field prediction? string Required. Output of the evaluated model.

---Spec for fluency result.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FluencyResult
---@field explanation? string Output only. Explanation for fluency score.
---@field confidence? number Output only. Confidence for fluency score.
---@field score? number Output only. Fluency score.

---Spec for fluency score metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FluencySpec
---@field version? number Optional. Which version to use for evaluation.

---Assigns the input data to training, validation, and test sets as per the given fractions. Any of `training_fraction`, `validation_fraction` and `test_fraction` may optionally be provided, they must sum to up to 1. If the provided ones sum to less than 1, the remainder is assigned to sets as decided by Vertex AI. If none of the fractions are set, by default roughly 80% of data is used for training, 10% for validation, and 10% for test.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FractionSplit
---@field validationFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to validate the Model.
---@field testFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to evaluate the Model.
---@field trainingFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to train the Model.

---Input for fulfillment metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FulfillmentInput
---@field metricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FulfillmentSpec Required. Spec for fulfillment score metric.
---@field instance? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FulfillmentInstance Required. Fulfillment instance.

---Spec for fulfillment instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FulfillmentInstance
---@field prediction? string Required. Output of the evaluated model.
---@field instruction? string Required. Inference instruction prompt to compare prediction with.

---Spec for fulfillment result.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FulfillmentResult
---@field score? number Output only. Fulfillment score.
---@field explanation? string Output only. Explanation for fulfillment score.
---@field confidence? number Output only. Confidence for fulfillment score.

---Spec for fulfillment metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FulfillmentSpec
---@field version? number Optional. Which version to use for evaluation.

---Resources for an fft model.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FullFineTunedResources
---@field modelInferenceUnitCount? number Optional. The number of model inference units to use for this deployment. This can only be specified for DEPLOYMENT_TYPE_PROD. The following table lists the number of model inference units for different model types: * Gemini 2.5 Flash * Foundation FMIU: 25 * Expansion FMIU: 4 * Gemini 2.5 Pro * Foundation FMIU: 32 * Expansion FMIU: 16 * Veo 3.0 (undistilled) * Foundation FMIU: 63 * Expansion FMIU: 7 * Veo 3.0 (distilled) * Foundation FMIU: 30 * Expansion FMIU: 10
---@field deploymentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FullFineTunedResourcesDeploymentTypeEnum|string Required. The kind of deployment.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FullFineTunedResourcesDeploymentTypeEnum "DEPLOYMENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DEPLOYMENT_TYPE_EVAL"|"DEPLOYMENT_TYPE_PROD"

---Tuning Spec for Full Fine Tuning.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FullFineTuningSpec
---@field hyperParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SupervisedHyperParameters Optional. Hyperparameters for Full Fine Tuning.
---@field validationDatasetUri? string Optional. Validation dataset used for tuning. The dataset can be specified as either a Cloud Storage path to a JSONL file or as the resource name of a Vertex Multimodal Dataset.
---@field trainingDatasetUri? string Required. Training dataset used for tuning. The dataset can be specified as either a Cloud Storage path to a JSONL file or as the resource name of a Vertex Multimodal Dataset.

---A predicted FunctionCall returned from the model that contains a string representing the FunctionDeclaration.name and a structured JSON object containing the parameters and their values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionCall
---@field partialArgs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartialArgList Optional. The partial argument value of the function call. If provided, represents the arguments/fields that are streamed incrementally.
---@field name? string Optional. The name of the function to call. Matches FunctionDeclaration.name.
---@field args? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. The function parameters and values in JSON object format. See FunctionDeclaration.parameters for parameter details.
---@field id? string Optional. The unique id of the function call. If populated, the client to execute the `function_call` and return the response with the matching `id`.
---@field willContinue? boolean Optional. Whether this is the last part of the FunctionCall. If true, another partial message for the current FunctionCall is expected to follow.

---Function calling config.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionCallingConfig
---@field mode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionCallingConfigModeEnum|string Optional. Function calling mode.
---@field allowedFunctionNames? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Function names to call. Only set when the Mode is ANY. Function names should match FunctionDeclaration.name. With mode set to ANY, model will predict a function call from the set of function names provided.
---@field streamFunctionCallArguments? boolean Optional. When set to true, arguments of a single function call will be streamed out in multiple parts/contents/responses. Partial parameter results will be returned in the `FunctionCall.partial_args` field.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionCallingConfigModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AUTO"|"ANY"|"NONE"|"VALIDATED"

---Structured representation of a function declaration as defined by the [OpenAPI 3.0 specification](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.3). Included in this declaration are the function name, description, parameters and response type. This FunctionDeclaration is a representation of a block of code that can be used as a `Tool` by the model and executed by the client.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclaration
---@field response? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema Optional. Describes the output from this function in JSON Schema format. Reflects the Open API 3.03 Response Object. The Schema defines the type used for the response value of the function.
---@field behavior? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclarationBehaviorEnum|string Optional. Specifies the function Behavior. If not specified, the system keeps the current function call behavior. This field is currently only supported by the BidiGenerateContent method.
---@field parametersJsonSchema? any Optional. Describes the parameters to the function in JSON Schema format. The schema must describe an object where the properties are the parameters to the function. For example: ``` { "type": "object", "properties": { "name": { "type": "string" }, "age": { "type": "integer" } }, "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["name", "age"], "propertyOrdering": ["name", "age"] } ``` This field is mutually exclusive with `parameters`.
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema Optional. Describes the parameters to this function in JSON Schema Object format. Reflects the Open API 3.03 Parameter Object. string Key: the name of the parameter. Parameter names are case sensitive. Schema Value: the Schema defining the type used for the parameter. For function with no parameters, this can be left unset. Parameter names must start with a letter or an underscore and must only contain chars a-z, A-Z, 0-9, or underscores with a maximum length of 64. Example with 1 required and 1 optional parameter: type: OBJECT properties: param1: type: STRING param2: type: INTEGER required: - param1
---@field responseJsonSchema? any Optional. Describes the output from this function in JSON Schema format. The value specified by the schema is the response value of the function. This field is mutually exclusive with `response`.
---@field description? string Optional. Description and purpose of the function. Model uses it to decide how and whether to call the function.
---@field name? string Required. The name of the function to call. Must start with a letter or an underscore. Must be a-z, A-Z, 0-9, or contain underscores, dots, colons and dashes, with a maximum length of 128.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclarationBehaviorEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"BLOCKING"|"NON_BLOCKING"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclarationList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclaration[]

---The result output from a FunctionCall that contains a string representing the FunctionDeclaration.name and a structured JSON object containing any output from the function is used as context to the model. This should contain the result of a `FunctionCall` made based on model prediction.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponse
---@field scheduling? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponseSchedulingEnum|string Optional. Specifies how the response should be scheduled in the conversation. Only applicable to NON_BLOCKING function calls, is ignored otherwise. Defaults to WHEN_IDLE.
---@field response? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Required. The function response in JSON object format. Use "output" key to specify function output and "error" key to specify error details (if any). If "output" and "error" keys are not specified, then whole "response" is treated as function output.
---@field name? string Required. The name of the function to call. Matches FunctionDeclaration.name and FunctionCall.name.
---@field id? string Optional. The id of the function call this response is for. Populated by the client to match the corresponding function call `id`.
---@field parts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponsePartList Optional. Ordered `Parts` that constitute a function response. Parts may have different IANA MIME types.

---Raw media bytes for function response. Text should not be sent as raw bytes, use the 'text' field.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponseBlob
---@field data? string Required. Raw bytes.
---@field mimeType? string Required. The IANA standard MIME type of the source data.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Display name of the blob. Used to provide a label or filename to distinguish blobs. This field is only returned in PromptMessage for prompt management. It is currently used in the Gemini GenerateContent calls only when server side tools (code_execution, google_search, and url_context) are enabled.

---URI based data for function response.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponseFileData
---@field mimeType? string Required. The IANA standard MIME type of the source data.
---@field fileUri? string Required. URI.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Display name of the file data. Used to provide a label or filename to distinguish file datas. This field is only returned in PromptMessage for prompt management. It is currently used in the Gemini GenerateContent calls only when server side tools (code_execution, google_search, and url_context) are enabled.

---A datatype containing media that is part of a `FunctionResponse` message. A `FunctionResponsePart` consists of data which has an associated datatype. A `FunctionResponsePart` can only contain one of the accepted types in `FunctionResponsePart.data`. A `FunctionResponsePart` must have a fixed IANA MIME type identifying the type and subtype of the media if the `inline_data` field is filled with raw bytes.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponsePart
---@field inlineData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponseBlob Inline media bytes.
---@field fileData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponseFileData URI based data.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponsePartList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponsePart[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponseSchedulingEnum "SCHEDULING_UNSPECIFIED"|"SILENT"|"WHEN_IDLE"|"INTERRUPT"

---Configuration for a single gateway.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GatewayConfig
---@field network? string Optional. The URI of the network resource where PSC-E will be provisioned. if not provided `default` network will be used. Format: projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}
---@field ipAddress? string Output only. The private IP address of the PSC endpoint.
---@field dnsZoneName? string Optional. Name of the private Cloud DNS managed zone in which to create the gateway's A-record. This is the managed zone's own name, not its DNS name: for a zone serving `example.internal.`, this field takes the zone name, such as `my-private-zone`. The zone's DNS name is combined with a generated per-gateway label to form the record's fully qualified name, which must stay within the 255-octet DNS limit. If the full name is too long, gateway provisioning fails when it attempts to create the DNS record.
---@field pscEndpoint? string Output only. The self-link or name of the Private Service Connect endpoint forwarding rule.
---@field dnsRecord? string Output only. The fully qualified record name of the created A-record in Cloud DNS.
---@field allowedProjects? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Additional consumer projects permitted to attach their own PSC endpoint to this gateway's ServiceAttachment. This is the "decoupled" mode, where the customer creates the PSC endpoint in a project other than this gateway's `network` project. Each listed project is VPC-SC enforced: it must be within the caller's service perimeter. The owning SemanticGovernancePolicyEngine's own project is always permitted implicitly and need not be listed. Format: `projects/{project}` (ID or number).
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GatewayConfigStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the Gateway configuration.
---@field subnetwork? string Optional. The URI of the subnetwork resource where PSC-E will be provisioned. if not provided `default` subnet will be used from the same {location} Format: projects/{project}/regions/{region}/subnetworks/{subnetwork}

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GatewayConfigMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GatewayConfig }

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GatewayConfigStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROVISIONING"|"ACTIVE"|"DEPROVISIONING"|"INACTIVE"|"FAILED"

---The Google Cloud Storage location where the output is to be written to.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination
---@field outputUriPrefix? string Required. Google Cloud Storage URI to output directory. If the uri doesn't end with '/', a '/' will be automatically appended. The directory is created if it doesn't exist.

---The Google Cloud Storage location for the input content.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource
---@field uris? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Google Cloud Storage URI(-s) to the input file(s). May contain wildcards. For more information on wildcards, see https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/wildcards.

