---@field syntheticExamples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SyntheticExampleList A list of generated synthetic examples, each containing a complete synthetic data instance generated based on your request.

---Response message for DataFoundryService.GenerateUserScenarios.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerateUserScenariosResponse
---@field userScenarios? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1UserScenarioList The generated user scenarios used to simulate multi-turn agent running results and agent evaluation.

---Configuration for content generation. This message contains all the parameters that control how the model generates content. It allows you to influence the randomness, length, and structure of the output.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfig
---@field enableAffectiveDialog? boolean Optional. If enabled, the model will detect emotions and adapt its responses accordingly. For example, if the model detects that the user is frustrated, it may provide a more empathetic response.
---@field responseMimeType? string Optional. The IANA standard MIME type of the response. The model will generate output that conforms to this MIME type. Supported values include 'text/plain' (default) and 'application/json'. The model needs to be prompted to output the appropriate response type, otherwise the behavior is undefined. Deprecated: Use `response_format` instead.
---@field temperature? number Optional. Controls the randomness of the output. A higher temperature results in more creative and diverse responses, while a lower temperature makes the output more predictable and focused. The valid range is (0.0, 2.0].
---@field topK? number Optional. Specifies the top-k sampling threshold. The model considers only the top k most probable tokens for the next token. This can be useful for generating more coherent and less random text. For example, a `top_k` of 40 means the model will choose the next word from the 40 most likely words.
---@field thinkingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigThinkingConfig Optional. Configuration for thinking features. An error will be returned if this field is set for models that don't support thinking.
---@field logprobs? number Optional. The number of top log probabilities to return for each token. This can be used to see which other tokens were considered likely candidates for a given position. A higher value will return more options, but it will also increase the size of the response.
---@field imageConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfig Optional. Config for image generation features. Deprecated: Use `response_format.image` instead.
---@field audioTimestamp? boolean Optional. If enabled, audio timestamps will be included in the request to the model. This can be useful for synchronizing audio with other modalities in the response.
---@field stopSequences? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. A list of character sequences that will stop the model from generating further tokens. If a stop sequence is generated, the output will end at that point. This is useful for controlling the length and structure of the output. For example, you can use ["\n", "###"] to stop generation at a new line or a specific marker.
---@field responseModalities? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigResponseModalitiesItemEnumList Optional. The modalities of the response. The model will generate a response that includes all the specified modalities. For example, if this is set to `[TEXT, IMAGE]`, the response will include both text and an image.
---@field topP? number Optional. Specifies the nucleus sampling threshold. The model considers only the smallest set of tokens whose cumulative probability is at least `top_p`. This helps generate more diverse and less repetitive responses. For example, a `top_p` of 0.9 means the model considers tokens until the cumulative probability of the tokens to select from reaches 0.9. It's recommended to adjust either temperature or `top_p`, but not both.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigModelConfig Optional. Config for model selection.
---@field frequencyPenalty? number Optional. Penalizes tokens based on their frequency in the generated text. A positive value helps to reduce the repetition of words and phrases. Valid values can range from [-2.0, 2.0].
---@field responseLogprobs? boolean Optional. If set to true, the log probabilities of the output tokens are returned. Log probabilities are the logarithm of the probability of a token appearing in the output. A higher log probability means the token is more likely to be generated. This can be useful for analyzing the model's confidence in its own output and for debugging.
---@field seed? number Optional. A seed for the random number generator. By setting a seed, you can make the model's output mostly deterministic. For a given prompt and parameters (like temperature, top_p, etc.), the model will produce the same response every time. However, it's not a guaranteed absolute deterministic behavior. This is different from parameters like `temperature`, which control the *level* of randomness. `seed` ensures that the "random" choices the model makes are the same on every run, making it essential for testing and ensuring reproducible results.
---@field presencePenalty? number Optional. Penalizes tokens that have already appeared in the generated text. A positive value encourages the model to generate more diverse and less repetitive text. Valid values can range from [-2.0, 2.0].
---@field responseFormat? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ResponseFormatList Optional. New response format field for the model to configure output formatting and delivery.
---@field responseSchema? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema Optional. Lets you to specify a schema for the model's response, ensuring that the output conforms to a particular structure. This is useful for generating structured data such as JSON. The schema is a subset of the [OpenAPI 3.0 schema object](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.3#schema) object. When this field is set, you must also set the `response_mime_type` to `application/json`. Deprecated: Use `response_format` instead.
---@field routingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfig Optional. Routing configuration.
---@field mediaResolution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigMediaResolutionEnum|string Optional. The token resolution at which input media content is sampled. This is used to control the trade-off between the quality of the response and the number of tokens used to represent the media. A higher resolution allows the model to perceive more detail, which can lead to a more nuanced response, but it will also use more tokens. This does not affect the image dimensions sent to the model.
---@field maxOutputTokens? number Optional. The maximum number of tokens to generate in the response. A token is approximately four characters. The default value varies by model. This parameter can be used to control the length of the generated text and prevent overly long responses.
---@field audioTranscriptionConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AudioTranscriptionConfig Optional. Configuration for audio transcription (speech recognition).
---@field candidateCount? number Optional. The number of candidate responses to generate. A higher `candidate_count` can provide more options to choose from, but it also consumes more resources. This can be useful for generating a variety of responses and selecting the best one.
---@field responseJsonSchema? any Optional. When this field is set, response_schema must be omitted and response_mime_type must be set to `application/json`. Deprecated: Use `response_format` instead.
---@field translationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TranslationConfig Optional. Config for translation.
---@field speechConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SpeechConfig Optional. The speech generation config.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigMediaResolutionEnum "MEDIA_RESOLUTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_LOW"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_MEDIUM"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_HIGH"

---Config for model selection.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigModelConfig
---@field featureSelectionPreference? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigModelConfigFeatureSelectionPreferenceEnum|string Required. Feature selection preference.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigModelConfigFeatureSelectionPreferenceEnum "FEATURE_SELECTION_PREFERENCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRIORITIZE_QUALITY"|"BALANCED"|"PRIORITIZE_COST"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigResponseModalitiesItemEnum "MODALITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"IMAGE"|"AUDIO"|"VIDEO"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigResponseModalitiesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigResponseModalitiesItemEnum|string)[]

---The configuration for routing the request to a specific model. This can be used to control which model is used for the generation, either automatically or by specifying a model name.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfig
---@field autoMode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfigAutoRoutingMode In this mode, the model is selected automatically based on the content of the request.
---@field manualMode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfigManualRoutingMode In this mode, the model is specified manually.

---The configuration for automated routing. When automated routing is specified, the routing will be determined by the pretrained routing model and customer provided model routing preference.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfigAutoRoutingMode
---@field modelRoutingPreference? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfigAutoRoutingModeModelRoutingPreferenceEnum|string The model routing preference.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfigAutoRoutingModeModelRoutingPreferenceEnum "UNKNOWN"|"PRIORITIZE_QUALITY"|"BALANCED"|"PRIORITIZE_COST"

---The configuration for manual routing. When manual routing is specified, the model will be selected based on the model name provided.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigRoutingConfigManualRoutingMode
---@field modelName? string The name of the model to use. Only public LLM models are accepted.

---Configuration for the model's thinking features. "Thinking" is a process where the model breaks down a complex task into smaller, manageable steps. This allows the model to reason about the task, plan its approach, and execute the plan to generate a high-quality response.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigThinkingConfig
---@field thinkingLevel? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigThinkingConfigThinkingLevelEnum|string Optional. The number of thoughts tokens that the model should generate.
---@field includeThoughts? boolean Optional. If true, the model will include its thoughts in the response. "Thoughts" are the intermediate steps the model takes to arrive at the final response. They can provide insights into the model's reasoning process and help with debugging. If this is true, thoughts are returned only when available.
---@field thinkingBudget? number Optional. The token budget for the model's thinking process. The model will make a best effort to stay within this budget. This can be used to control the trade-off between response quality and latency.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfigThinkingConfigThinkingLevelEnum "THINKING_LEVEL_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"MINIMAL"

---Contains information about the source of the models generated from Generative AI Studio.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenieSource
---@field baseModelUri? string Required. The public base model URI.

---A goal is an objective a Task works toward. A Task may pursue several concurrent goals . A goal could have one or more Verifiers as independent judges to validate the completion of it.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Goal
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoalStateEnum|string Output only. The goal's state.
---@field spec? string Required. The goal's objective. This is the "goal" and what the agent should pursue.
---@field id? string Output only. Server-assigned identifier, stable across the goal's lifetime.
---@field verifiers? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1VerifierList Optional. The verifier(s) that judge whether this goal is achieved. When all `required` verifiers pass, the goal will be marked `SUCCEEDED` in its `state`. If empty, the work is still checked against criteria written from the goal's `spec`, but the goal stays `ACTIVE`; add a required `auto_verification` to have it complete.
---@field displayName? string Optional. A human-readable title specifiable to the goal.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoalList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Goal[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoalStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"DROPPED"

