---@field domain? string The domain of the web page that contains the evidence. This can be used to filter out low-quality sources.
---@field title? string The title of the web page that contains the evidence.
---@field uri? string The URI of the web page that contains the evidence.

---Information about the sources that support the content of a response. When grounding is enabled, the model returns citations for claims in the response. This object contains the retrieved sources.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadata
---@field googleMapsWidgetContextToken? string Optional. Output only. Deprecated: The Google Maps contextual widget behavior in Grounding with Google Maps is being deprecated; this field is planned for removal and will no longer be populated once removed. A token that can be used to render a Google Maps widget with the contextual data. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@field retrievalQueries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The queries that were executed by the retrieval tools. This field is populated only when the grounding source is a retrieval tool, such as Vertex AI Search.
---@field retrievalMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RetrievalMetadata Optional. Output only. Metadata related to the retrieval grounding source.
---@field groundingSupports? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupportList Optional. A list of grounding supports that connect the generated content to the grounding chunks. This field is populated when the grounding source is Google Search or Vertex AI Search.
---@field groundingChunks? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkList A list of supporting references retrieved from the grounding source. This field is populated when the grounding source is Google Search, Vertex AI Search, or Google Maps.
---@field imageSearchQueries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The image search queries that were used to generate the content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search with the Image Search search_type enabled.
---@field searchEntryPoint? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SearchEntryPoint Optional. A web search entry point that can be used to display search results. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search.
---@field webSearchQueries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The web search queries that were used to generate the content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search.
---@field sourceFlaggingUris? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUriList Optional. Output only. A list of URIs that can be used to flag a place or review for inappropriate content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.

---A URI that can be used to flag a place or review for inappropriate content. This is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUri
---@field sourceId? string The ID of the place or review.
---@field flagContentUri? string The URI that can be used to flag the content.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUriList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUri[]

---A collection of supporting references for a segment or part of the model's response.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupport
---@field segment? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Segment The content segment that this support message applies to.
---@field confidenceScores? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DoubleList The confidence scores for the support references. This list is parallel to the `grounding_chunk_indices` list. A score is a value between 0.0 and 1.0, with a higher score indicating a higher confidence that the reference supports the claim. For Gemini 2.0 and before, this list has the same size as `grounding_chunk_indices`. For Gemini 2.5 and later, this list is empty and should be ignored.
---@field groundingChunkIndices? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.IntegerList A list of indices into the `grounding_chunks` field of the `GroundingMetadata` message. These indices specify which grounding chunks support the claim made in the content segment. For example, if this field has the values `[1, 3]`, it means that `grounding_chunks[1]` and `grounding_chunks[3]` are the sources for the claim in the content segment.
---@field renderedParts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.IntegerList Indices into the `rendered_parts` field of the `GroundingMetadata` message. These indices specify which rendered parts are associated with this support message.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupportList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupport[]

---Metadata for a Harbor dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborDataset
---@field gcsUri? string Optional. The GCS folder containing the Harbor dataset, e.g. "gs://BUCKET/PATH".

---Config for running an agent (a coding or custom agent) on a dataset in Harbor format in a sandboxed batch environment. Run metrics (`evaluation_config.metrics`) are optional for runs over Harbor tasks. Each metric scores a task's agent trajectory; the prompt and the response are empty. Predefined metrics that build their rubrics from the trajectory, such as `multi_turn_task_success_v1`, `multi_turn_trajectory_quality_v1` and `multi_turn_tool_use_quality_v1`, are supported. `evaluation_config.rubric_configs`, rubric-based metrics, and LLM-based metrics with a rubrics source are rejected. Metrics that need a text response or a reference, such as computation-based metrics, are accepted but fail on each task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborRunConfig
---@field codingAgent? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborRunConfigCodingAgent The coding agent to run.
---@field batchJobConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborRunConfigBatchJobConfig Optional. Configuration for the VM.

---Configuration for the VM that runs the Harbor tasks.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborRunConfigBatchJobConfig
---@field networkSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1NetworkSpec Optional. Network settings for the VM. If unset, the VM uses the project's default network with an external IP address, so it can reach Google APIs and the internet. To turn off internet access, set a network and a subnetwork that has Private Google Access, so that the VM can still reach Cloud Storage, Artifact Registry, and Vertex AI.

---A coding agent to run against the Harbor dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborRunConfigCodingAgent
---@field agentModel? string Optional. The Vertex AI model the coding agent calls. Only Gemini based Vertex AI models are supported. Accepts the full Vertex AI model resource name of the form projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}
---@field agentModelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerationConfig Optional. Generation settings of the model that the coding agent calls. If you do not set this field, the coding agent uses its default settings. Only `thinking_config.thinking_level` is supported. The valid levels are `MINIMAL`, `LOW`, `MEDIUM` and `HIGH`. `antigravity-cli` does not accept a level for Gemini 2.5 models. It accepts `MINIMAL` and `MEDIUM` only for Gemini Flash models. If you set a level that is not valid for the coding agent and the model, inference fails for the candidate.
---@field agent? string The coding agent to run, e.g. "antigravity-cli".

---Represents a Harbor task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HarborTask
---@field task? string Required. The Harbor task name, e.g. "django__django-15098".
---@field dataset? string Required. Harbor dataset name this task belongs to, in `org/name` format without a version, e.g. "my-org/swebench-verified".
---@field gcsUri? string The GCS folder containing the Harbor task, e.g. "gs://BUCKET/PATH".

---Represents a HyperparameterTuningJob. A HyperparameterTuningJob has a Study specification and multiple CustomJobs with identical CustomJob specification.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HyperparameterTuningJob
---@field trialJobSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomJobSpec Required. The spec of a trial job. The same spec applies to the CustomJobs created in all the trials.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field parallelTrialCount? number Required. The desired number of Trials to run in parallel.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob was created.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HyperparameterTuningJobStateEnum Output only. The detailed state of the job.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob was most recently updated.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the HyperparameterTuningJob. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field maxTrialCount? number Required. The desired total number of Trials.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the HyperparameterTuningJob.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key options for a HyperparameterTuningJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the HyperparameterTuningJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.
---@field endTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob entered any of the following states: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Time when the HyperparameterTuningJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.
---@field maxFailedTrialCount? number The number of failed Trials that need to be seen before failing the HyperparameterTuningJob. If set to 0, Vertex AI decides how many Trials must fail before the whole job fails.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize HyperparameterTuningJobs. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field studySpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1StudySpec Required. Study configuration of the HyperparameterTuningJob.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field trials? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TrialList Output only. Trials of the HyperparameterTuningJob.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. Only populated when job's state is JOB_STATE_FAILED or JOB_STATE_CANCELLED.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HyperparameterTuningJobList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HyperparameterTuningJob[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1HyperparameterTuningJobStateEnum "JOB_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"JOB_STATE_QUEUED"|"JOB_STATE_PENDING"|"JOB_STATE_RUNNING"|"JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED"|"JOB_STATE_FAILED"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLING"|"JOB_STATE_CANCELLED"|"JOB_STATE_PAUSED"|"JOB_STATE_EXPIRED"|"JOB_STATE_UPDATING"|"JOB_STATE_PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED"

---Matcher for Features of an EntityType by Feature ID.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IdMatcher
---@field ids? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. The following are accepted as `ids`: * A single-element list containing only `*`, which selects all Features in the target EntityType, or * A list containing only Feature IDs, which selects only Features with those IDs in the target EntityType.

---Configuration for image generation. This message allows you to control various aspects of image generation, such as the output format, aspect ratio, and whether the model can generate images of people.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfig
---@field imageSize? string Optional. Specifies the size of generated images. Supported values are `1K`, `2K`, `4K`. If not specified, the model will use default value `1K`.
---@field prominentPeople? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigProminentPeopleEnum|string Optional. Controls whether prominent people (celebrities) generation is allowed. If used with personGeneration, personGeneration enum would take precedence. For instance, if ALLOW_NONE is set, all person generation would be blocked. If this field is unspecified, the default behavior is to allow prominent people.
---@field imageOutputOptions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigImageOutputOptions Optional. The image output format for generated images.
---@field aspectRatio? string Optional. The desired aspect ratio for the generated images. The following aspect ratios are supported: "1:1" "2:3", "3:2" "3:4", "4:3" "4:5", "5:4" "9:16", "16:9" "21:9"
---@field personGeneration? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigPersonGenerationEnum|string Optional. Controls whether the model can generate people.

---The image output format for generated images.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigImageOutputOptions
---@field mimeType? string Optional. The image format that the output should be saved as.
---@field compressionQuality? number Optional. The compression quality of the output image.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigPersonGenerationEnum "PERSON_GENERATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW_ALL"|"ALLOW_ADULT"|"ALLOW_NONE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigProminentPeopleEnum "PROMINENT_PEOPLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW_PROMINENT_PEOPLE"|"BLOCK_PROMINENT_PEOPLE"

---Configuration for image-specific output formatting.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormat
---@field aspectRatio? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatAspectRatioEnum|string Optional. The aspect ratio for the image output.
---@field imageSize? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatImageSizeEnum|string Optional. The size of the image output.
---@field mimeType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatMimeTypeEnum|string Optional. The MIME type of the image output.
---@field delivery? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatDeliveryEnum|string Optional. Delivery mode for the generated content.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatAspectRatioEnum "ASPECT_RATIO_UNSPECIFIED"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_ONE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_TWO_BY_THREE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_THREE_BY_TWO"|"ASPECT_RATIO_THREE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_THREE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_FIVE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FIVE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_NINE_BY_SIXTEEN"|"ASPECT_RATIO_SIXTEEN_BY_NINE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_TWENTY_ONE_BY_NINE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_EIGHT"|"ASPECT_RATIO_EIGHT_BY_ONE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_ONE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatDeliveryEnum "DELIVERY_UNSPECIFIED"|"INLINE"|"URI"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatImageSizeEnum "IMAGE_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE_SIZE_FIVE_TWELVE"|"IMAGE_SIZE_ONE_K"|"IMAGE_SIZE_TWO_K"|"IMAGE_SIZE_FOUR_K"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatMimeTypeEnum "MIME_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE_JPEG"

---Describes the location from where we import data into a Dataset, together with the labels that will be applied to the DataItems and the Annotations.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportDataConfig
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource The Google Cloud Storage location for the input content.
---@field importSchemaUri? string Required. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the import format. Validation will be done against the schema. The schema is defined as an [OpenAPI 3.0.2 Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject).
---@field annotationLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Labels that will be applied to newly imported Annotations. If two Annotations are identical, one of them will be deduped. Two Annotations are considered identical if their payload, payload_schema_uri and all of their labels are the same. These labels will be overridden by Annotation labels specified inside index file referenced by import_schema_uri, e.g. jsonl file.
---@field dataItemLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Labels that will be applied to newly imported DataItems. If an identical DataItem as one being imported already exists in the Dataset, then these labels will be appended to these of the already existing one, and if labels with identical key is imported before, the old label value will be overwritten. If two DataItems are identical in the same import data operation, the labels will be combined and if key collision happens in this case, one of the values will be picked randomly. Two DataItems are considered identical if their content bytes are identical (e.g. image bytes or pdf bytes). These labels will be overridden by Annotation labels specified inside index file referenced by import_schema_uri, e.g. jsonl file.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportDataConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportDataConfig[]

---Source for loading Agent Engine sessions.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestAgentEngineSource
---@field location? string Required. Location for the Agent Engine sessions.
---@field reasoningEngineId? string Required. Reasoning Engine ID for the Agent Engine sessions.
---@field sessionIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. Session IDs for the Agent Engine sessions to retrieve.
---@field projectId? string Required. Project ID for the Agent Engine sessions.

---Source for loading traces directly from Cloud Trace.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestCloudTraceSource
---@field agentResource? string Optional. Restricts the imported spans to a single agent. Accepts either of two forms, matching `OnlineEvaluator.agent_resource`: * a project-scoped resource name, matched against the `cloud.resource_id` resource attribute that Vertex AI Agent Engine agents are stamped with; * an Agent Registry agent URN, matched against the `gen_ai.main_agent.id` resource attribute that agents on GKE, and any other runtime that stamps it, are identified by. Scopes `session_ids` selection only. Traces named explicitly in `trace_ids` are imported as given and are NOT filtered by this field, because the caller has already identified them. Setting this field with only `trace_ids` therefore has no effect. When unset, spans are selected by session or trace ID alone. That is the pre-existing behavior and it remains the correct one for a session whose agents run in several deployments, because each deployment stamps its own `gen_ai.main_agent.id` and filtering on one of them would silently truncate the trajectory.
---@field projectId? string Required. Project ID for the Cloud Trace.
---@field traceIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Trace IDs to import.
---@field sessionIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Session IDs to import traces for. If both trace_ids and session_ids are specified, the union of the two will be imported.

---Source for loading data from Cloud Storage.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestGcsSource
---@field importSchemaConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfig Required. Schema configuration for the input data.
---@field gcsUri? string Required. The Cloud Storage location of the input data.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportModeEnum "IMPORT_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"OVERWRITE"

---Configuration for the input data format.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfig
---@field dataFormat? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfigDataFormatEnum|string Required. The format of the input data.
---@field dataFormatVersion? string Optional. Version of the data format.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfigDataFormatEnum "DATA_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"OTEL_PROTO"|"OTEL_JSON"|"JSONL"

---Wrapper for inline data.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestInlineSource
---@field importSchemaConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestImportSchemaConfig Required. Schema configuration for the inline data.
---@field content? string Required. The content of the inline data.

---Source for importing interactions from the Interactions API into an EvaluationSet. The agent identity is specified once, with a list of interaction IDs to import.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportEvaluationSetRequestInteractionsSource
---@field interactions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Required. The interactions to import. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/interactions/{interaction}`.
---@field geminiAgentConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GeminiAgentConfig Optional. Gemini Agent (Vertex AI Agent resource).

---Defines the Feature value(s) to import.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportFeatureValuesRequestFeatureSpec
---@field sourceField? string Source column to get the Feature values from. If not set, uses the column with the same name as the Feature ID.
---@field id? string Required. ID of the Feature to import values of. This Feature must exist in the target EntityType, or the request will fail.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportFeatureValuesRequestFeatureSpecList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportFeatureValuesRequestFeatureSpec[]

---Configuration for importing data from an external source.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfig
---@field bigQuerySourceConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigBigQuerySourceConfig Configuration for importing data from a BigQuery table.

---Configuration for importing data from a BigQuery table.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigBigQuerySourceConfig
---@field datapointFieldMapping? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMapping Required. Mapping of datapoint fields to BigQuery column names.
---@field tablePath? string Required. The path to the BigQuery table containing the index data, in the format of `bq://..`.

---Mapping of datapoint fields to column names for columnar data sources.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMapping
---@field embeddingColumn? string Required. The column with the vector embeddings for each data point.
---@field restricts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingRestrictList Optional. List of restricts for string values.
---@field metadataColumns? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. List of columns containing metadata to be included in the index.
---@field numericRestricts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingNumericRestrictList Optional. List of restricts for numeric values.
---@field idColumn? string Required. The column with unique identifiers for each data point.

---Restrictions on numeric values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingNumericRestrict
---@field valueColumn? string Optional. The column containing the numeric value.
---@field namespace? string Required. The namespace of the restrict.
---@field valueType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingNumericRestrictValueTypeEnum|string Required. Numeric type of the restrict. Must be consistent for all datapoints within the namespace.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingNumericRestrictList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingNumericRestrict[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingNumericRestrictValueTypeEnum "VALUE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INT"|"FLOAT"|"DOUBLE"

---Restrictions on string values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingRestrict
---@field allowColumn? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The columns containing the allow values.
---@field namespace? string Required. The namespace of the restrict in the index.
---@field denyColumn? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The columns containing the deny values.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingRestrictList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportIndexRequestConnectorConfigDatapointFieldMappingRestrict[]

---Config for importing RagFiles.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImportRagFilesConfig
---@field partialFailureGcsSink? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage path to write partial failures to. Deprecated. Prefer to use `import_result_gcs_sink`.
---@field slackSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SlackSource Slack channels with their corresponding access tokens.
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource Google Cloud Storage location. Supports importing individual files as well as entire Google Cloud Storage directories. Sample formats: - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory/object_name/my_file.txt` - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory`
---@field importResultBigquerySink? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination The BigQuery destination to write import result to. It should be a bigquery table resource name (e.g. "bq://projectId.bqDatasetId.bqTableId"). The dataset must exist. If the table does not exist, it will be created with the expected schema. If the table exists, the schema will be validated and data will be added to this existing table.
---@field partialFailureBigquerySink? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination The BigQuery destination to write partial failures to. It should be a bigquery table resource name (e.g. "bq://projectId.bqDatasetId.bqTableId"). The dataset must exist. If the table does not exist, it will be created with the expected schema. If the table exists, the schema will be validated and data will be added to this existing table. Deprecated. Prefer to use `import_result_bq_sink`.
---@field ragFileParsingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfig Optional. Specifies the parsing config for RagFiles. RAG will use the default parser if this field is not set.
---@field jiraSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1JiraSource Jira queries with their corresponding authentication.
---@field ragFileTransformationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileTransformationConfig Specifies the transformation config for RagFiles.
---@field googleDriveSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoogleDriveSource Google Drive location. Supports importing individual files as well as Google Drive folders.
---@field maxEmbeddingRequestsPerMin? number Optional. The max number of queries per minute that this job is allowed to make to the embedding model specified on the corpus. This value is specific to this job and not shared across other import jobs. Consult the Quotas page on the project to set an appropriate value here. If unspecified, a default value of 1,000 QPM would be used.
---@field ragFileMetadataConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileMetadataConfig Specifies the metadata config for RagFiles. Including paths for metadata schema and metadata. Deprecated: Not in use.
---@field importResultGcsSink? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination The Cloud Storage path to write import result to.
---@field rebuildAnnIndex? boolean Rebuilds the ANN index to optimize for recall on the imported data. Only applicable for RagCorpora running on RagManagedDb with `retrieval_strategy` set to `ANN`. The rebuild will be performed using the existing ANN config set on the RagCorpus. To change the ANN config, please use the UpdateRagCorpus API. Default is false, i.e., index is not rebuilt.
---@field sharePointSources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SharePointSources SharePoint sources.
---@field ragFileChunkingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileChunkingConfig Specifies the size and overlap of chunks after importing RagFiles.
---@field globalMaxEmbeddingRequestsPerMin? number Optional. The max number of queries per minute that the indexing pipeline job is allowed to make to the embedding model specified in the project. Please follow the quota usage guideline of the embedding model you use to set the value properly.If this value is not specified, max_embedding_requests_per_min will be used by indexing pipeline job as the global limit.

---A representation of a collection of database items organized in a way that allows for approximate nearest neighbor (a.k.a ANN) algorithms search.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Index
---@field indexStats? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexStats Output only. Stats of the index resource.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for an Index. If set, this Index and all sub-resources of this Index will be secured by this key.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field indexUpdateMethod? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexIndexUpdateMethodEnum Immutable. The update method to use with this Index. If not set, BATCH_UPDATE will be used by default.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the Index.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Index. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field deployedIndexes? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DeployedIndexRefList Output only. The pointers to DeployedIndexes created from this Index. An Index can be only deleted if all its DeployedIndexes had been undeployed first.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Index was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Index was most recently updated. This also includes any update to the contents of the Index. Note that Operations working on this Index may have their Operations.metadata.generic_metadata.update_time a little after the value of this timestamp, yet that does not mean their results are not already reflected in the Index. Result of any successfully completed Operation on the Index is reflected in it.
---@field description? string The description of the Index.
---@field metadataSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing additional information about the Index, that is specific to it. Unset if the Index does not have any additional information. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Indexes. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.
---@field metadata? any An additional information about the Index; the schema of the metadata can be found in metadata_schema.

---A datapoint of Index.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapoint
---@field datapointId? string Required. Unique identifier of the datapoint.
---@field embeddingMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. The key-value map of additional metadata for the datapoint.
---@field sparseEmbedding? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapointSparseEmbedding Optional. Feature embedding vector for sparse index.
---@field restricts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapointRestrictionList Optional. List of Restrict of the datapoint, used to perform "restricted searches" where boolean rule are used to filter the subset of the database eligible for matching. This uses categorical tokens. See: https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/matching-engine/filtering
---@field numericRestricts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapointNumericRestrictionList Optional. List of Restrict of the datapoint, used to perform "restricted searches" where boolean rule are used to filter the subset of the database eligible for matching. This uses numeric comparisons.
---@field featureVector? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DoubleList Required. Feature embedding vector for dense index. An array of numbers with the length of [NearestNeighborSearchConfig.dimensions].
---@field crowdingTag? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1IndexDatapointCrowdingTag Optional. CrowdingTag of the datapoint, the number of neighbors to return in each crowding can be configured during query.

---Crowding tag is a constraint on a neighbor list produced by nearest neighbor search requiring that no more than some value k' of the k neighbors returned have the same value of crowding_attribute.
