---A file, folder, site or other item in a first-party or third-party store, as its `.link.json` file in the workspace records it. A link file is this message as proto JSON with the field names below, e.g. `{"source_artifact_id":"1AbC","provider":"GOOGLE_DRIVE","artifact_type": "GOOGLE_DRIVE_FILE","uri":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AbC/view"}`. A link file may hold fields this message does not have; they are ignored. `path` and `update_time` are not part of a link file: the service sets both on a link it lists, from the link file it read the link from, and `AddArtifact` clears both from a request.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LinkJsonMetadata
---@field provider? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LinkJsonMetadataProviderEnum|string Required. The store that holds the entity.
---@field uri? string Required. URI of the entity, e.g. "https://drive.google.com/file/d/FILE_ID/view". At most 2048 characters.
---@field path? string Output only. Absolute path of the link file in the workspace, e.g. `/workspace/userdata/{artifact_id}.link.json` in a task or `/workspace/project/{artifact_id}.link.json` in a collaborative project. Always under `/workspace` and never contains `..`. Set by `ArtifactService.ListWorkspaceArtifacts`. `ArtifactService.AddArtifact` clears it from a request, so it is never written to the link file.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Last modification time of the link file at `path`, as `ArtifactService.ListWorkspaceArtifacts` read it. Not part of a link file. It is what tells two listings of one entity apart after the entity was updated in place. Such an update leaves every other field alone -- the entity keeps its `uri` and its `source_artifact_id`, so the link file keeps its name -- and it leaves the link file's bytes alone too, because a link file records WHICH entity is linked and not what state that entity is in. The time the file was rewritten is the only thing that moves.
---@field sourceArtifactId? string Optional. The entity's ID in its store, unique within `provider`: a Drive file ID, a Jira issue ID, or, for OneDrive and SharePoint, whose item IDs are unique only within a drive, the drive ID and the drive item ID, e.g. "{drive-id}/{item-id}". At most 1024 characters. With `provider`, it identifies the entity: it names the link file and is the idempotency key for `AddArtifact`. When it is unset, `uri` takes its place, so two URIs of one entity, such as a Drive file's /view and /edit URIs, are two entities.
---@field mimeType? string Optional. The entity's media type, e.g. "application/vnd.ms-excel". Empty for an entity that has none, such as a SharePoint site.
---@field artifactType? string Optional. The provider-specific kind of entity, in upper snake case. Known values are GOOGLE_DRIVE_DOC, GOOGLE_DRIVE_SHEET, GOOGLE_DRIVE_SLIDES, GOOGLE_DRIVE_FILE, GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER, ONE_DRIVE_FILE, ONE_DRIVE_FOLDER, SHAREPOINT_FILE, SHAREPOINT_FOLDER and SHAREPOINT_SITE; a connector may use others. Must match `A-Z*`. At most 64 characters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LinkJsonMetadataProviderEnum "PROVIDER_UNSPECIFIED"|"GOOGLE_DRIVE"|"ONEDRIVE"|"SHAREPOINT"|"OUTLOOK"|"TEAMS"|"GMAIL"|"GOOGLE_CALENDAR"|"GOOGLE_CHAT"|"CONFLUENCE"|"JIRA"|"GITHUB"|"SALESFORCE"|"SERVICENOW"|"SLACK"

