---The log probabilities of the tokens generated by the model. This is useful for understanding the model's confidence in its predictions and for debugging. For example, you can use log probabilities to identify when the model is making a less confident prediction or to explore alternative responses that the model considered. A low log probability can also indicate that the model is "hallucinating" or generating factually incorrect information.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResult
---@field topCandidates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidatesList A list of the top candidate tokens at each decoding step. The length of this list is equal to the total number of decoding steps.
---@field chosenCandidates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidateList A list of the chosen candidate tokens at each decoding step. The length of this list is equal to the total number of decoding steps. Note that the chosen candidate might not be in `top_candidates`.

---A single token and its associated log probability.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidate
---@field tokenId? number The token's numerical ID. While the `token` field provides the string representation of the token, the `token_id` is the numerical representation that the model uses internally. This can be useful for developers who want to build custom logic based on the model's vocabulary.
---@field logProbability? number The log probability of this token. A higher value indicates that the model was more confident in this token. The log probability can be used to assess the relative likelihood of different tokens and to identify when the model is uncertain.
---@field token? string The token's string representation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidateList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidate[]

---A list of the top candidate tokens and their log probabilities at each decoding step. This can be used to see what other tokens the model considered.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidates
---@field candidates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidateList The list of candidate tokens, sorted by log probability in descending order.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidatesList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidates[]

---Configuration for the loss analysis job.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisConfig
---@field candidate? string Required. The candidate model/agent to analyze (e.g., "gemini-3.0-pro"). This targets the specific CandidateResult within the EvaluationResult.
---@field metric? string Required. The metric to analyze (e.g., "tool_use_quality"). This filters the EvaluationItems in the EvalSet to only those where EvaluationResult.metric matches this value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisConfig[]

---The top-level result for loss analysis, stored within an EvalSet.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisResult
---@field clusters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossClusterList The list of identified loss clusters.
---@field analysisTime? string The timestamp when this analysis was performed.
---@field config? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisConfig The configuration used to generate this analysis.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisResultList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossAnalysisResult[]

---Represents a semantic grouping of failures (e.g., "Hallucination of Action").
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossCluster
---@field itemCount? number The total number of EvaluationItems falling into this cluster.
---@field taxonomyEntry? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossTaxonomyEntry The structured definition of the loss taxonomy for this cluster.
---@field examples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossExampleList A list of examples that belong to this cluster. This links the cluster back to the specific EvaluationItems and Rubrics.
---@field clusterId? string Unique identifier for the loss cluster within the scope of the analysis result.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossClusterList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossCluster[]

---Represents a specific example of a loss pattern.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossExample
---@field evaluationResult? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EvaluationResult The full evaluation result object provided inline. Used when the analysis is performed on ephemeral data (without an EvaluationSet).
---@field evaluationItem? string Reference to the persisted EvalItem resource name. Format: projects/.../locations/.../evaluationItems/{item_id} Used when analysis is run on an EvalSet.
---@field failedRubrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FailedRubricList The specific rubric(s) that failed and caused this example to be classified here. An example might fail multiple rubrics, but only specific ones trigger this loss pattern.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossExampleList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossExample[]

---Defines a specific entry in the loss pattern taxonomy.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LossTaxonomyEntry
---@field l2Category? string The secondary category of the loss (e.g., "Hallucination of Action", "Incorrect Tool Selection").
---@field description? string A detailed description of this loss pattern. Example: "The agent verbally confirms an action without executing the tool."
---@field l1Category? string The primary category of the loss (e.g., "Hallucination", "Tool Calling"). This field is typically required.

---Represents a mount configuration for Lustre file system.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LustreMount
---@field instanceIp? string Required. IP address of the Lustre instance.
---@field mountPoint? string Required. Destination mount path. The Lustre file system will be mounted for the user under /mnt/lustre/
---@field filesystem? string Required. The name of the Lustre filesystem.
---@field volumeHandle? string Required. The unique identifier of the Lustre volume.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LustreMountList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LustreMount[]

---Specification of a single machine.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MachineSpec
---@field minGpuDriverVersion? string Optional. Immutable. The minimum GPU driver version that this machine requires. For example, "535.104.06". If not specified, the default GPU driver version will be used by the underlying infrastructure.
---@field acceleratorCount? number The number of accelerators to attach to the machine. For [accelerator optimized machine types](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/accelerator-optimized-machines), One may set the accelerator_count from 1 to N for machine with N GPUs. If accelerator_count is less than or equal to N / 2, Agent Platform co-schedules the replicas of the model into the same VM to save cost. For example, if the machine type is a3-highgpu-8g, which has 8 H100 GPUs, one can set accelerator_count to 1 to 8. If accelerator_count is 1, 2, 3, or 4, Agent Platform co-schedules 8, 4, 2, or 2 replicas of the model into the same VM to save cost. When co-scheduling, CPU, memory and storage on the VM will be distributed to replicas on the VM. For example, one can expect a co-scheduled replica requesting 2 GPUs out of a 8-GPU VM will receive 25% of the CPU, memory and storage of the VM. Note that the feature is not compatible with multihost_gpu_node_count. When multihost_gpu_node_count is set, the co-scheduling will not be enabled.
---@field gpuPartitionSize? string Optional. Immutable. The Nvidia GPU partition size. When specified, the requested accelerators will be partitioned into smaller GPU partitions. For example, if the request is for 8 units of NVIDIA A100 GPUs, and gpu_partition_size="1g.10gb", the service will create 8 * 7 = 56 partitioned MIG instances. The partition size must be a value supported by the requested accelerator. Refer to [Nvidia GPU Partitioning](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/gpus-multi#multi-instance_gpu_partitions) for the available partition sizes. If set, the accelerator_count should be set to 1.
---@field acceleratorType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MachineSpecAcceleratorTypeEnum|string Immutable. The type of accelerator(s) that may be attached to the machine as per accelerator_count.
---@field tpuTopology? string Immutable. The topology of the TPUs. Corresponds to the TPU topologies available from GKE. (Example: tpu_topology: "2x2x1").
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReservationAffinity Optional. Immutable. Configuration controlling how this resource pool consumes reservation.
---@field multihostGpuNodeCount? number Optional. Immutable. The number of nodes per replica for multihost GPU deployments.
---@field machineType? string Immutable. The type of the machine. See the [list of machine types supported for prediction](https://cloud.google.com/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform/machine-learning/predictions/configure-compute#machine-types) See the [list of machine types supported for custom training](https://cloud.google.com/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform/machine-learning/training/configure-compute#machine-types). For DeployedModel this field is optional, and the default value is `n1-standard-2`. For BatchPredictionJob or as part of WorkerPoolSpec this field is required.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MachineSpecAcceleratorTypeEnum "ACCELERATOR_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NVIDIA_TESLA_K80"|"NVIDIA_TESLA_P100"|"NVIDIA_TESLA_V100"|"NVIDIA_TESLA_P4"|"NVIDIA_TESLA_T4"|"NVIDIA_TESLA_A100"|"NVIDIA_A100_80GB"|"NVIDIA_L4"|"NVIDIA_H100_80GB"|"NVIDIA_H100_MEGA_80GB"|"NVIDIA_H200_141GB"|"NVIDIA_B200"|"NVIDIA_GB200"|"NVIDIA_RTX_PRO_6000"|"TPU_V2"|"TPU_V3"|"TPU_V4_POD"|"TPU_V5_LITEPOD"

---Manual batch tuning parameters.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ManualBatchTuningParameters
---@field batchSize? number Immutable. The number of the records (e.g. instances) of the operation given in each batch to a machine replica. Machine type, and size of a single record should be considered when setting this parameter, higher value speeds up the batch operation's execution, but too high value will result in a whole batch not fitting in a machine's memory, and the whole operation will fail. The default value is 64.

---A message representing a Measurement of a Trial. A Measurement contains the Metrics got by executing a Trial using suggested hyperparameter values.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Measurement
---@field metrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MeasurementMetricList Output only. A list of metrics got by evaluating the objective functions using suggested Parameter values.
---@field stepCount? string Output only. The number of steps the machine learning model has been trained for. Must be non-negative.
---@field elapsedDuration? string Output only. Time that the Trial has been running at the point of this Measurement.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MeasurementList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Measurement[]

---A message representing a metric in the measurement.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MeasurementMetric
---@field value? number Output only. The value for this metric.
---@field metricId? string Output only. The ID of the Metric. The Metric should be defined in StudySpec's Metrics.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MeasurementMetricList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MeasurementMetric[]

---A memory.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Memory
---@field scope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Required. Immutable. Represents the scope of the Memory. Memories are isolated within their scope. The scope is defined when creating or generating memories. Scope values cannot contain the wildcard character '*'.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was created.
---@field description? string Optional. Represents the description of the Memory.
---@field fact? string Optional. Represents semantic knowledge extracted from the source content.
---@field revisionTtl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for the revision. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field structuredContent? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryStructuredContent Optional. Represents the structured content of the memory.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for this resource. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field topics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryTopicIdList Optional. Represents the Topics of the Memory.
---@field name? string Identifier. Represents the resource name of the Memory. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/memories/{memory}`
---@field memoryType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMemoryTypeEnum Optional. Represents the type of the memory. If not set, the `NATURAL_LANGUAGE_COLLECTION` type is used. If `STRUCTURED_COLLECTION` or `STRUCTURED_PROFILE` is used, then `structured_data` must be provided.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Represents the display name of the Memory.
---@field expireTime? string Optional. Represents the timestamp of when this resource is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output when `expiration` is set on input, regardless of whether `expire_time` or `ttl` was provided.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was most recently updated.
---@field context? string Optional. Represents the context of the memory.
---@field revisionLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Represents the labels to apply to the Memory Revision created as a result of this request.
---@field revisionExpireTime? string Optional. Input only. Represents the timestamp of when the revision is considered expired. If not set, the memory revision will be kept until manually deleted.
---@field disableMemoryRevisions? boolean Optional. Input only. Indicates whether no revision will be created for this request.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMetadataValueMap Optional. Represents user-provided metadata for the Memory. This information was provided when creating, updating, or generating the Memory. It was not generated by Memory Bank.

---Represents configuration for organizing natural language memories for a particular scope.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfig
---@field memoryTopics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigMemoryTopicList Optional. Represents topics of information that should be extracted from conversations and stored as memories. If not set, then Memory Bank's default topics will be used.
---@field scopeKeys? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Represents the scope keys (i.e. 'user_id') for which to use this config. A request's scope must include all of the provided keys for the config to be used (order does not matter). If empty, then the config will be used for all requests that do not have a more specific config. Only one default config is allowed per Memory Bank.
---@field enableThirdPersonMemories? boolean Optional. Indicates whether the memories will be generated in the third person (i.e. "The user generates memories with Memory Bank."). By default, the memories will be generated in the first person (i.e. "I generate memories with Memory Bank.")
---@field generateMemoriesExamples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleList Optional. Provides examples of how to generate memories for a particular scope.
---@field consolidationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigConsolidationConfig Optional. Represents configuration for customizing how memories are consolidated together.
---@field disableNaturalLanguageMemories? boolean Optional. Indicates whether natural language memory generation should be disabled for all requests. By default, natural language memory generation is enabled. Set this to `true` when you only want to generate structured memories.

---Represents configuration for customizing how memories are consolidated.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigConsolidationConfig
---@field revisionsPerCandidateCount? number Optional. Represents the maximum number of revisions to consider for each candidate memory. If not set, then the default value (1) will be used, which means that only the latest revision will be considered.

---An example of how to generate memories for a particular scope.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExample
---@field conversationSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleConversationSource A conversation source for the example.
---@field generatedMemories? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleGeneratedMemoryList Optional. Represents the memories that are expected to be generated from the input conversation. An empty list indicates that no memories are expected to be generated for the input conversation.

---A conversation source for the example. This is similar to `DirectContentsSource`.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleConversationSource
---@field events? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleConversationSourceEventList Optional. Represents the input conversation events for the example.

---A single conversation event.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleConversationSourceEvent
---@field content? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Content Required. Represents the content of the event.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleConversationSourceEventList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleConversationSourceEvent[]

---A memory generated by the operation.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleGeneratedMemory
---@field topics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryTopicIdList Optional. Represents the list of topics that the memory should be associated with. For example, use `custom_memory_topic_label = "jargon"` if the extracted memory is an example of memory extraction for the custom topic `jargon`.
---@field fact? string Required. Represents the fact to generate a memory from.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleGeneratedMemoryList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleGeneratedMemory[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExampleList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigGenerateMemoriesExample[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfig[]

---A topic of information that should be extracted from conversations and stored as memories.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigMemoryTopic
---@field customMemoryTopic? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigMemoryTopicCustomMemoryTopic A custom memory topic defined by the developer.
---@field managedMemoryTopic? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigMemoryTopicManagedMemoryTopic A managed memory topic defined by Memory Bank.

---A custom memory topic defined by the developer.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryBankCustomizationConfigMemoryTopicCustomMemoryTopic
