---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringNotificationSpecNotificationChannelConfig
---@field notificationChannel? string Resource names of the NotificationChannels. Must be of the format `projects//notificationChannels/`

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringNotificationSpecNotificationChannelConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringNotificationSpecNotificationChannelConfig[]

---The objective configuration for model monitoring, including the information needed to detect anomalies for one particular model.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfig
---@field explanationConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigExplanationConfig The config for integrating with Vertex Explainable AI.
---@field predictionDriftDetectionConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigPredictionDriftDetectionConfig The config for drift of prediction data.
---@field trainingDataset? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigTrainingDataset Training dataset for models. This field has to be set only if TrainingPredictionSkewDetectionConfig is specified.
---@field trainingPredictionSkewDetectionConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigTrainingPredictionSkewDetectionConfig The config for skew between training data and prediction data.

---The config for integrating with Vertex Explainable AI. Only applicable if the Model has explanation_spec populated.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigExplanationConfig
---@field enableFeatureAttributes? boolean If want to analyze the Vertex Explainable AI feature attribute scores or not. If set to true, Vertex AI will log the feature attributions from explain response and do the skew/drift detection for them.
---@field explanationBaseline? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigExplanationConfigExplanationBaseline Predictions generated by the BatchPredictionJob using baseline dataset.

---Output from BatchPredictionJob for Model Monitoring baseline dataset, which can be used to generate baseline attribution scores.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigExplanationConfigExplanationBaseline
---@field bigquery? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination BigQuery location for BatchExplain output.
---@field predictionFormat? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigExplanationConfigExplanationBaselinePredictionFormatEnum|string The storage format of the predictions generated BatchPrediction job.
---@field gcs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination Cloud Storage location for BatchExplain output.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigExplanationConfigExplanationBaselinePredictionFormatEnum "PREDICTION_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED"|"JSONL"|"BIGQUERY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfig[]

---The config for Prediction data drift detection.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigPredictionDriftDetectionConfig
---@field driftThresholds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ThresholdConfigMap Key is the feature name and value is the threshold. If a feature needs to be monitored for drift, a value threshold must be configured for that feature. The threshold here is against feature distribution distance between different time windws.
---@field attributionScoreDriftThresholds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ThresholdConfigMap Key is the feature name and value is the threshold. The threshold here is against attribution score distance between different time windows.
---@field defaultDriftThreshold? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ThresholdConfig Drift anomaly detection threshold used by all features. When the per-feature thresholds are not set, this field can be used to specify a threshold for all features.

---Training Dataset information.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigTrainingDataset
---@field loggingSamplingStrategy? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SamplingStrategy Strategy to sample data from Training Dataset. If not set, we process the whole dataset.
---@field dataset? string The resource name of the Dataset used to train this Model.
---@field bigquerySource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQuerySource The BigQuery table of the unmanaged Dataset used to train this Model.
---@field dataFormat? string Data format of the dataset, only applicable if the input is from Google Cloud Storage. The possible formats are: "tf-record" The source file is a TFRecord file. "csv" The source file is a CSV file. "jsonl" The source file is a JSONL file.
---@field targetField? string The target field name the model is to predict. This field will be excluded when doing Predict and (or) Explain for the training data.
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource The Google Cloud Storage uri of the unmanaged Dataset used to train this Model.

---The config for Training & Prediction data skew detection. It specifies the training dataset sources and the skew detection parameters.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfigTrainingPredictionSkewDetectionConfig
---@field defaultSkewThreshold? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ThresholdConfig Skew anomaly detection threshold used by all features. When the per-feature thresholds are not set, this field can be used to specify a threshold for all features.
---@field attributionScoreSkewThresholds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ThresholdConfigMap Key is the feature name and value is the threshold. The threshold here is against attribution score distance between the training and prediction feature.
---@field skewThresholds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ThresholdConfigMap Key is the feature name and value is the threshold. If a feature needs to be monitored for skew, a value threshold must be configured for that feature. The threshold here is against feature distribution distance between the training and prediction feature.

---Monitoring objectives spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpec
---@field explanationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExplanationSpec The explanation spec. This spec is required when the objectives spec includes feature attribution objectives.
---@field targetDataset? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringInput Target dataset.
---@field tabularObjective? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecTabularObjective Tabular monitoring objective.
---@field baselineDataset? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringInput Baseline dataset. It could be the training dataset or production serving dataset from a previous period.

---Data drift monitoring spec. Data drift measures the distribution distance between the current dataset and a baseline dataset. A typical use case is to detect data drift between the recent production serving dataset and the training dataset, or to compare the recent production dataset with a dataset from a previous period.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecDataDriftSpec
---@field features? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Feature names / Prediction output names interested in monitoring. These should be a subset of the input feature names or prediction output names specified in the monitoring schema. If the field is not specified all features / prediction outputs outlied in the monitoring schema will be used.
---@field featureAlertConditions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringAlertConditionMap Per feature alert condition will override default alert condition.
---@field defaultCategoricalAlertCondition? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringAlertCondition Default alert condition for all the categorical features.
---@field defaultNumericAlertCondition? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringAlertCondition Default alert condition for all the numeric features.
---@field numericMetricType? string Supported metrics type: * jensen_shannon_divergence
---@field categoricalMetricType? string Supported metrics type: * l_infinity * jensen_shannon_divergence

---Feature attribution monitoring spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecFeatureAttributionSpec
---@field defaultAlertCondition? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringAlertCondition Default alert condition for all the features.
---@field features? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Feature names interested in monitoring. These should be a subset of the input feature names specified in the monitoring schema. If the field is not specified all features outlied in the monitoring schema will be used.
---@field batchExplanationDedicatedResources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BatchDedicatedResources The config of resources used by the Model Monitoring during the batch explanation for non-AutoML models. If not set, `n1-standard-2` machine type will be used by default.
---@field featureAlertConditions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringAlertConditionMap Per feature alert condition will override default alert condition.

---Tabular monitoring objective.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecTabularObjective
---@field predictionOutputDriftSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecDataDriftSpec Prediction output distribution drift monitoring spec.
---@field featureAttributionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecFeatureAttributionSpec Feature attribution monitoring spec.
---@field featureDriftSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpecDataDriftSpec Input feature distribution drift monitoring spec.

---Specification for the export destination of monitoring results, including metrics, logs, etc.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringOutputSpec
---@field gcsBaseDirectory? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsDestination Google Cloud Storage base folder path for metrics, error logs, etc.

---The Model Monitoring Schema definition.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchema
---@field featureFields? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchemaFieldSchemaList Feature names of the model. Vertex AI will try to match the features from your dataset as follows: * For 'csv' files, the header names are required, and we will extract the corresponding feature values when the header names align with the feature names. * For 'jsonl' files, we will extract the corresponding feature values if the key names match the feature names. Note: Nested features are not supported, so please ensure your features are flattened. Ensure the feature values are scalar or an array of scalars. * For 'bigquery' dataset, we will extract the corresponding feature values if the column names match the feature names. Note: The column type can be a scalar or an array of scalars. STRUCT or JSON types are not supported. You may use SQL queries to select or aggregate the relevant features from your original table. However, ensure that the 'schema' of the query results meets our requirements. * For the Vertex AI Endpoint Request Response Logging table or Vertex AI Batch Prediction Job results. If the instance_type is an array, ensure that the sequence in feature_fields matches the order of features in the prediction instance. We will match the feature with the array in the order specified in [feature_fields].
---@field predictionFields? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchemaFieldSchemaList Prediction output names of the model. The requirements are the same as the feature_fields. For AutoML Tables, the prediction output name presented in schema will be: `predicted_{target_column}`, the `target_column` is the one you specified when you train the model. For Prediction output drift analysis: * AutoML Classification, the distribution of the argmax label will be analyzed. * AutoML Regression, the distribution of the value will be analyzed.
---@field groundTruthFields? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchemaFieldSchemaList Target /ground truth names of the model.

---Schema field definition.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchemaFieldSchema
---@field dataType? string Supported data types are: `float` `integer` `boolean` `string` `categorical`
---@field repeated? boolean Describes if the schema field is an array of given data type.
---@field name? string Field name.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchemaFieldSchemaList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSchemaFieldSchema[]

---Monitoring monitoring job spec. It outlines the specifications for monitoring objectives, notifications, and result exports.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringSpec
---@field notificationSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringNotificationSpec The model monitoring notification spec.
---@field objectiveSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringObjectiveSpec The monitoring objective spec.
---@field outputSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringOutputSpec The Output destination spec for metrics, error logs, etc.

---Represents the collection of statistics for a metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelMonitoringStats
