---A datatype containing media that is part of a multi-part Content message. A `Part` consists of data which has an associated datatype. A `Part` must contain one of the accepted types in `Part.data`. For media types that are not text, `Part` must have a fixed IANA MIME type identifying the type and subtype of the media if `inline_data` or `file_data` field is filled with raw bytes.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Part
---@field inlineData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Blob Optional. The inline data content of the part. This can be used to include images, audio, or video in a request.
---@field mediaProcessing? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaProcessingEnum|string Optional. How the model processes this part's media for understanding. Only meaningful for video parts (`inline_data` or `file_data` with video mime). Non-video parts ignore this field.
---@field codeExecutionResult? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CodeExecutionResult Optional. The result of executing the ExecutableCode.
---@field speechMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SpeechMetadata Optional. Turn-level metadata for speech generation (e.g. Daikon speaker/style). May be set alongside `text` to attach speaker and style information to a text part.
---@field audioTranscription? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AudioTranscription Optional. Audio (input or output) transcription. This is only set when this `Part` contains audio data.
---@field executableCode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutableCode Optional. Code generated by the model that is intended to be executed.
---@field videoMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1VideoMetadata Optional. Video metadata. The metadata should only be specified while the video data is presented in inline_data or file_data.
---@field text? string Optional. The text content of the part. When sent from the VSCode Gemini Code Assist extension, references to @mentioned items will be converted to markdown boldface text. For example `@my-repo` will be converted to and sent as `**my-repo**` by the IDE agent.
---@field thought? boolean Optional. Indicates whether the `part` represents the model's thought process or reasoning.
---@field functionResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponse Optional. The result of a function call. This is used to provide the model with the result of a function call that it predicted.
---@field fileData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FileData Optional. The URI-based data of the part. This can be used to include files from Google Cloud Storage.
---@field thoughtSignature? string Optional. An opaque signature for the thought so it can be reused in subsequent requests.
---@field mediaResolution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolution per part media resolution. Media resolution for the input media.
---@field functionCall? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionCall Optional. A predicted function call returned from the model. This contains the name of the function to call and the arguments to pass to the function.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Part[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaProcessingEnum "MEDIA_PROCESSING_UNSPECIFIED"|"STATIC"|"AGENTIC"

---per part media resolution. Media resolution for the input media.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolution
---@field level? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolutionLevelEnum|string The tokenization quality used for given media.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolutionLevelEnum "MEDIA_RESOLUTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_LOW"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_MEDIUM"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_HIGH"|"MEDIA_RESOLUTION_ULTRA_HIGH"

---Partial argument value of the function call.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartialArg
---@field stringValue? string Optional. Represents a string value.
---@field nullValue? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartialArgNullValueEnum|string Optional. Represents a null value.
---@field jsonPath? string Required. A JSON Path (RFC 9535) to the argument being streamed. https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9535. e.g. "$.foo.bar[0].data".
---@field willContinue? boolean Optional. Whether this is not the last part of the same json_path. If true, another PartialArg message for the current json_path is expected to follow.
---@field numberValue? number Optional. Represents a double value.
---@field boolValue? boolean Optional. Represents a boolean value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartialArgList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartialArg[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartialArgNullValueEnum "NULL_VALUE"

---Tuning spec for Partner models.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartnerModelTuningSpec
---@field trainingDatasetUri? string Required. Cloud Storage path to file containing training dataset for tuning. The dataset must be formatted as a JSONL file.
---@field hyperParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Hyperparameters for tuning. The accepted hyper_parameters and their valid range of values will differ depending on the base model.
---@field validationDatasetUri? string Optional. Cloud Storage path to file containing validation dataset for tuning. The dataset must be formatted as a JSONL file.

