---Input for pointwise metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricInput
---@field instance? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricInstance Required. Pointwise metric instance.
---@field metricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricSpec Required. Spec for pointwise metric.

---Pointwise metric instance. Usually one instance corresponds to one row in an evaluation dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricInstance
---@field contentMapInstance? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ContentMap Key-value contents for the mutlimodality input, including text, image, video, audio, and pdf, etc. The key is placeholder in metric prompt template, and the value is the multimodal content.
---@field jsonInstance? string Instance specified as a json string. String key-value pairs are expected in the json_instance to render PointwiseMetricSpec.instance_prompt_template.

---Spec for pointwise metric result.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricResult
---@field customOutput? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomOutput Output only. Spec for custom output.
---@field score? number Output only. Pointwise metric score.
---@field explanation? string Output only. Explanation for pointwise metric score.

---Spec for pointwise metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PointwiseMetricSpec
---@field metricPromptTemplate? string Required. Metric prompt template for pointwise metric.
---@field systemInstruction? string Optional. System instructions for pointwise metric.
---@field customOutputFormatConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CustomOutputFormatConfig Optional. CustomOutputFormatConfig allows customization of metric output. By default, metrics return a score and explanation. When this config is set, the default output is replaced with either: - The raw output string. - A parsed output based on a user-defined schema. If a custom format is chosen, the `score` and `explanation` fields in the corresponding metric result will be empty.

---Represents a network port in a container.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Port
---@field containerPort? number The number of the port to expose on the pod's IP address. Must be a valid port number, between 1 and 65535 inclusive.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PortList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Port[]

---Post startup script config.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PostStartupScriptConfig
---@field postStartupScriptBehavior? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PostStartupScriptConfigPostStartupScriptBehaviorEnum|string Optional. Post startup script behavior that defines download and execution behavior.
---@field postStartupScript? string Optional. Post startup script to run after runtime is started.
---@field postStartupScriptUrl? string Optional. Post startup script url to download. Example: `gs://bucket/script.sh`

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PostStartupScriptConfigPostStartupScriptBehaviorEnum "POST_STARTUP_SCRIPT_BEHAVIOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"RUN_ONCE"|"RUN_EVERY_START"|"DOWNLOAD_AND_RUN_EVERY_START"

---A pre-tuned model for continuous tuning.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreTunedModel
---@field baseModel? string Output only. The name of the base model this PreTunedModel was tuned from.
---@field checkpointId? string Optional. The source checkpoint id. If not specified, the default checkpoint will be used.
---@field tunedModelName? string The resource name of the Model. E.g., a model resource name with a specified version id or alias: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@{version_id}` `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}@{alias}` Or, omit the version id to use the default version: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/models/{model}`

---Configuration for a prebuilt voice.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrebuiltVoiceConfig
---@field voiceName? string The name of the prebuilt voice to use.

---The spec for a pre-defined metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PredefinedMetricSpec
---@field stepAutoraterConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AutoraterConfigMap Optional. Per-step autorater overrides for this predefined metric. Keys are evaluation stage names (snake_case). Valid keys: "intent_extraction", "rubric_generation", "rubric_validation". Unknown keys return INVALID_ARGUMENT.
---@field metricSpecName? string Required. The name of a pre-defined metric, such as "instruction_following_v1" or "text_quality_v1".
---@field metricSpecParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. The parameters needed to run the pre-defined metric.

---Assigns input data to training, validation, and test sets based on the value of a provided key. Supported only for tabular Datasets.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PredefinedSplit
---@field key? string Required. The key is a name of one of the Dataset's data columns. The value of the key (either the label's value or value in the column) must be one of {`training`, `validation`, `test`}, and it defines to which set the given piece of data is assigned. If for a piece of data the key is not present or has an invalid value, that piece is ignored by the pipeline.

---Configuration for logging request-response to a BigQuery table.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PredictRequestResponseLoggingConfig
---@field errorSamplingRate? number Optional. Percentage of failed requests to be logged, expressed as a fraction in range [0,1]. Only non-transient errors will be logged (currently `500/Internal` errors).
---@field samplingRate? number Percentage of requests to be logged, expressed as a fraction in range(0,1].
---@field enableOtelLogging? boolean This field is used for large models. If true, in addition to the original large model logs, logs will be converted in OTel schema format, and saved in otel_log column. Default value is false.
---@field enabled? boolean If logging is enabled or not.
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BigQueryDestination BigQuery table for logging. If only given a project, a new dataset will be created with name `logging__` where will be made BigQuery-dataset-name compatible (e.g. most special characters will become underscores). If no table name is given, a new table will be created with name `request_response_logging`
---@field requestResponseLoggingSchemaVersion? string Output only. The schema version used in creating the BigQuery table for the request response logging. The versions are "v1" and "v2". The current default version is "v1".

---Response message for PredictionService.Predict.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PredictResponse
---@field model? string Output only. The resource name of the Model which is deployed as the DeployedModel that this prediction hits.
---@field deployedModelId? string ID of the Endpoint's DeployedModel that served this prediction.
---@field modelVersionId? string Output only. The version ID of the Model which is deployed as the DeployedModel that this prediction hits.
---@field metadata? any Output only. Request-level metadata returned by the model. The metadata type will be dependent upon the model implementation.
---@field modelDisplayName? string Output only. The display name of the Model which is deployed as the DeployedModel that this prediction hits.
---@field predictions? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentList The predictions that are the output of the predictions call. The schema of any single prediction may be specified via Endpoint's DeployedModels' Model's PredictSchemata's prediction_schema_uri.

---Contains the schemata used in Model's predictions and explanations via PredictionService.Predict, PredictionService.Explain and BatchPredictionJob.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PredictSchemata
---@field parametersSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the parameters of prediction and explanation via PredictRequest.parameters, ExplainRequest.parameters and BatchPredictionJob.model_parameters. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI, if no parameters are supported, then it is set to an empty string. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field instanceSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the format of a single instance, which are used in PredictRequest.instances, ExplainRequest.instances and BatchPredictionJob.input_config. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.
---@field predictionSchemaUri? string Immutable. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing the format of a single prediction produced by this Model, which are returned via PredictResponse.predictions, ExplainResponse.explanations, and BatchPredictionJob.output_config. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 [Schema Object](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.0.2.md#schemaObject). AutoML Models always have this field populated by Vertex AI. Note: The URI given on output will be immutable and probably different, including the URI scheme, than the one given on input. The output URI will point to a location where the user only has a read access.

---Statistics computed for datasets used for preference optimization.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationDataStats
---@field scoresDistribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for scores.
---@field userInputTokenDistribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for the user input tokens.
---@field droppedExampleReasons? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Output only. For each index in `dropped_example_indices`, the user-facing reason why the example was dropped.
---@field tuningDatasetExampleCount? string Output only. Number of examples in the tuning dataset.
---@field droppedExampleIndices? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Output only. A partial sample of the indices (starting from 1) of the dropped examples.
---@field scoreVariancePerExampleDistribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for scores variance per example.
---@field totalBillableTokenCount? string Output only. Number of billable tokens in the tuning dataset.
---@field tuningStepCount? string Output only. Number of tuning steps for this Tuning Job.
---@field userOutputTokenDistribution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DatasetDistribution Output only. Dataset distributions for the user output tokens.
---@field userDatasetExamples? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GeminiPreferenceExampleList Output only. Sample user examples in the training dataset.

---Hyperparameters for Preference Optimization.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParameters
---@field adapterSize? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParametersAdapterSizeEnum|string Optional. Adapter size for preference optimization.
---@field epochCount? string Optional. Number of complete passes the model makes over the entire training dataset during training.
---@field beta? number Optional. Weight for KL Divergence regularization.
---@field learningRateMultiplier? number Optional. Multiplier for adjusting the default learning rate.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParametersAdapterSizeEnum "ADAPTER_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_ONE"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_TWO"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_FOUR"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_EIGHT"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_SIXTEEN"|"ADAPTER_SIZE_THIRTY_TWO"

---Tuning Spec for Preference Optimization.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationSpec
---@field validationDatasetUri? string Optional. Cloud Storage path to file containing validation dataset for preference optimization tuning. The dataset must be formatted as a JSONL file.
---@field exportLastCheckpointOnly? boolean Optional. If set to true, disable intermediate checkpoints for Preference Optimization and only the last checkpoint will be exported. Otherwise, enable intermediate checkpoints for Preference Optimization. Default is false.
---@field trainingDatasetUri? string Required. Cloud Storage path to file containing training dataset for preference optimization tuning. The dataset must be formatted as a JSONL file.
---@field hyperParameters? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PreferenceOptimizationHyperParameters Optional. Hyperparameters for Preference Optimization.

---Preset configuration for example-based explanations
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Presets
---@field query? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PresetsQueryEnum|string Preset option controlling parameters for speed-precision trade-off when querying for examples. If omitted, defaults to `PRECISE`.
---@field modality? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PresetsModalityEnum|string The modality of the uploaded model, which automatically configures the distance measurement and feature normalization for the underlying example index and queries. If your model does not precisely fit one of these types, it is okay to choose the closest type.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PresetsModalityEnum "MODALITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE"|"TEXT"|"TABULAR"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PresetsQueryEnum "PRECISE"|"FAST"

---Represents an identity principal (user or service).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Principal
---@field id? string Optional. The system unique identifier of the principal.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrincipalTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of the principal.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrincipalTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER"

---PrivateEndpoints proto is used to provide paths for users to send requests privately. To send request via private service access, use predict_http_uri, explain_http_uri or health_http_uri. To send request via private service connect, use service_attachment.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrivateEndpoints
---@field healthHttpUri? string Output only. Http(s) path to send health check requests.
---@field predictHttpUri? string Output only. Http(s) path to send prediction requests.
---@field serviceAttachment? string Output only. The name of the service attachment resource. Populated if private service connect is enabled.
---@field explainHttpUri? string Output only. Http(s) path to send explain requests.

---Represents configuration for private service connect.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrivateServiceConnectConfig
---@field serviceAttachment? string Output only. The name of the generated service attachment resource. This is only populated if the endpoint is deployed with PrivateServiceConnect.
---@field enablePrivateServiceConnect? boolean Required. If true, expose the IndexEndpoint via private service connect.
---@field projectAllowlist? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList A list of Projects from which the forwarding rule will target the service attachment.
---@field enableSecurePrivateServiceConnect? boolean Optional. If set to true, enable secure private service connect with IAM authorization. Otherwise, private service connect will be done without authorization. Note latency will be slightly increased if authorization is enabled.
---@field pscAutomationConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PSCAutomationConfigList Optional. List of projects and networks where the PSC endpoints will be created. This field is used by Online Inference(Prediction) only.

---Probe describes a health check to be performed against a container to determine whether it is alive or ready to receive traffic.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Probe
---@field successThreshold? number Number of consecutive successes before the probe is considered successful. Defaults to 1. Minimum value is 1. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'successThreshold'.
---@field periodSeconds? number How often (in seconds) to perform the probe. Default to 10 seconds. Minimum value is 1. Must be less than timeout_seconds. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'periodSeconds'.
---@field exec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeExecAction ExecAction probes the health of a container by executing a command.
---@field initialDelaySeconds? number Number of seconds to wait before starting the probe. Defaults to 0. Minimum value is 0. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'initialDelaySeconds'.
---@field timeoutSeconds? number Number of seconds after which the probe times out. Defaults to 1 second. Minimum value is 1. Must be greater or equal to period_seconds. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'timeoutSeconds'.
---@field tcpSocket? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeTcpSocketAction TcpSocketAction probes the health of a container by opening a TCP socket connection.
---@field failureThreshold? number Number of consecutive failures before the probe is considered failed. Defaults to 3. Minimum value is 1. Maps to Kubernetes probe argument 'failureThreshold'.
---@field httpGet? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeHttpGetAction HttpGetAction probes the health of a container by sending an HTTP GET request.
---@field grpc? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeGrpcAction GrpcAction probes the health of a container by sending a gRPC request.

---ExecAction specifies a command to execute.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeExecAction
---@field command? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Command is the command line to execute inside the container, the working directory for the command is root ('/') in the container's filesystem. The command is simply exec'd, it is not run inside a shell, so traditional shell instructions ('|', etc) won't work. To use a shell, you need to explicitly call out to that shell. Exit status of 0 is treated as live/healthy and non-zero is unhealthy.

---GrpcAction checks the health of a container using a gRPC service.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeGrpcAction
---@field port? number Port number of the gRPC service. Number must be in the range 1 to 65535.
---@field service? string Service is the name of the service to place in the gRPC HealthCheckRequest. See https://github.com/grpc/grpc/blob/master/doc/health-checking.md. If this is not specified, the default behavior is defined by gRPC.

---HttpGetAction describes an action based on HTTP Get requests.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeHttpGetAction
---@field host? string Host name to connect to, defaults to the model serving container's IP. You probably want to set "Host" in httpHeaders instead.
---@field port? number Number of the port to access on the container. Number must be in the range 1 to 65535.
---@field httpHeaders? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeHttpHeaderList Custom headers to set in the request. HTTP allows repeated headers.
---@field path? string Path to access on the HTTP server.
---@field scheme? string Scheme to use for connecting to the host. Defaults to HTTP. Acceptable values are "HTTP" or "HTTPS".

---HttpHeader describes a custom header to be used in HTTP probes
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeHttpHeader
---@field name? string The header field name. This will be canonicalized upon output, so case-variant names will be understood as the same header.
---@field value? string The header field value

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeHttpHeaderList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeHttpHeader[]

---TcpSocketAction probes the health of a container by opening a TCP socket connection.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProbeTcpSocketAction
---@field port? number Number of the port to access on the container. Number must be in the range 1 to 65535.
---@field host? string Optional: Host name to connect to, defaults to the model serving container's IP.

---Spec for Veo data processing.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProcessDataRequestVeoSpec
---@field outpaintingMode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProcessDataRequestVeoSpecOutpaintingModeEnum|string Optional. The mode of Veo Outpainting data processing to perform. Required (`DATA_PREPARATION` or `OUTPAINTING`) when `process_type` is `VEO_OUTPAINTING` (`OUTPAINTING_MODE_UNSPECIFIED` is rejected with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`). Must not be set when `process_type` is not `VEO_OUTPAINTING` (rejected with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`).
---@field processType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProcessDataRequestVeoSpecProcessTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of data processing to perform.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProcessDataRequestVeoSpecOutpaintingModeEnum "OUTPAINTING_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DATA_PREPARATION"|"OUTPAINTING"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ProcessDataRequestVeoSpecProcessTypeEnum "VEO_V1_AND_V2_DEFAULT"|"VEO_V3"|"VEO_OUTPAINTING"

---PscAutomatedEndpoints defines the output of the forwarding rule automatically created by each PscAutomationConfig.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PscAutomatedEndpoints
---@field network? string Corresponding network in pscAutomationConfigs.
---@field projectId? string Corresponding project_id in pscAutomationConfigs
---@field matchAddress? string Ip Address created by the automated forwarding rule.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PscAutomatedEndpointsList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PscAutomatedEndpoints[]

---Configuration for PSC-I.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PscInterfaceConfig
---@field networkAttachment? string Optional. The name of the Compute Engine [network attachment](https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/about-network-attachments) to attach to the resource within the region and user project. To specify this field, you must have already [created a network attachment] (https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/create-manage-network-attachments#create-network-attachments). This field is only used for resources using PSC-I.
---@field dnsPeeringConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DnsPeeringConfigList Optional. DNS peering configurations. When specified, Vertex AI will attempt to configure DNS peering zones in the tenant project VPC to resolve the specified domains using the target network's Cloud DNS. The user must grant the dns.peer role to the Vertex AI Service Agent on the target project.

---A Model Garden Publisher Model.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PublisherModel
---@field versionState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PublisherModelVersionStateEnum Optional. Indicates the state of the model version.
