---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileChunkingConfig
---@field chunkSize? number The size of the chunks.
---@field fixedLengthChunking? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileChunkingConfigFixedLengthChunking Specifies the fixed length chunking config.
---@field chunkOverlap? number The overlap between chunks.

---Specifies the fixed length chunking config.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileChunkingConfigFixedLengthChunking
---@field chunkSize? number The size of the chunks.
---@field chunkOverlap? number The overlap between chunks.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFile[]

---Metadata config for RagFile.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileMetadataConfig
---@field gcsMetadataSchemaSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource Google Cloud Storage location. Supports importing individual files as well as entire Google Cloud Storage directories. Sample formats: - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory/object_name/metadata_schema.json` - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory` If the user provides a directory, the metadata schema will be read from the files that ends with "metadata_schema.json" in the directory.
---@field inlineMetadataSchemaSource? string Inline metadata schema source. Must be a JSON string.
---@field googleDriveMetadataSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoogleDriveSource Google Drive location. Supports importing individual files as well as Google Drive folders. If the user provides a directory, the metadata will be read from the files that ends with "metadata.json" in the directory.
---@field googleDriveMetadataSchemaSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoogleDriveSource Google Drive location. Supports importing individual files as well as Google Drive folders. If the user provides a folder, the metadata schema will be read from the files that ends with "metadata_schema.json" in the directory.
---@field inlineMetadataSource? string Inline metadata source. Must be a JSON string.
---@field gcsMetadataSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GcsSource Google Cloud Storage location. Supports importing individual files as well as entire Google Cloud Storage directories. Sample formats: - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory/object_name/metadata.json` - `gs://bucket_name/my_directory` If the user provides a directory, the metadata will be read from the files that ends with "metadata.json" in the directory.

---Specifies the parsing config for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfig
---@field useAdvancedPdfParsing? boolean Whether to use advanced PDF parsing.
---@field layoutParser? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfigLayoutParser The Layout Parser to use for RagFiles.
---@field advancedParser? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfigAdvancedParser The Advanced Parser to use for RagFiles.
---@field llmParser? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfigLlmParser The LLM Parser to use for RagFiles.

---Specifies the advanced parsing for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfigAdvancedParser
---@field useAdvancedPdfParsing? boolean Whether to use advanced PDF parsing.

---Document AI Layout Parser config.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfigLayoutParser
---@field globalMaxParsingRequestsPerMin? number The maximum number of requests the job is allowed to make to the Document AI processor per minute in this project. Consult https://cloud.google.com/document-ai/quotas and the Quota page for your project to set an appropriate value here. If this value is not specified, max_parsing_requests_per_min will be used by indexing pipeline as the global limit.
---@field maxParsingRequestsPerMin? number The maximum number of requests the job is allowed to make to the Document AI processor per minute. Consult https://cloud.google.com/document-ai/quotas and the Quota page for your project to set an appropriate value here. If unspecified, a default value of 120 QPM would be used.
---@field processorName? string The full resource name of a Document AI processor or processor version. The processor must have type `LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR`. If specified, the `additional_config.parse_as_scanned_pdf` field must be false. Format: * `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/processors/{processor_id}` * `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/processors/{processor_id}/processorVersions/{processor_version_id}`

---Specifies the LLM parsing for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileParsingConfigLlmParser
---@field globalMaxParsingRequestsPerMin? number The maximum number of requests the job is allowed to make to the LLM model per minute in this project. Consult https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/quotas and your document size to set an appropriate value here. If this value is not specified, max_parsing_requests_per_min will be used by indexing pipeline job as the global limit.
---@field maxParsingRequestsPerMin? number The maximum number of requests the job is allowed to make to the LLM model per minute. Consult https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/quotas and your document size to set an appropriate value here. If unspecified, a default value of 5000 QPM would be used.
---@field modelName? string The name of a LLM model used for parsing. Format: * `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}`
---@field customParsingPrompt? string The prompt to use for parsing. If not specified, a default prompt will be used.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileRagFileTypeEnum "RAG_FILE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RAG_FILE_TYPE_TXT"|"RAG_FILE_TYPE_PDF"

---Specifies the transformation config for RagFiles.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileTransformationConfig
---@field ragFileChunkingConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagFileChunkingConfig Specifies the chunking config for RagFiles.

---Configuration message for RagManagedDb used by RagEngine.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfig
---@field enterprise? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigEnterprise Sets the RagManagedDb to the Enterprise tier.
---@field scaled? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigScaled Deprecated: Use `mode` instead to set the tier under Spanner. Sets the RagManagedDb to the Scaled tier.
---@field unprovisioned? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigUnprovisioned Deprecated: Use `mode` instead to set the tier under Spanner. Sets the RagManagedDb to the Unprovisioned tier.
---@field basic? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigBasic Deprecated: Use `mode` instead to set the tier under Spanner. Sets the RagManagedDb to the Basic tier.
---@field spanner? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigSpanner Sets the RAG Engine backend to be RagManagedDb, built on top of Spanner. NOTE: This is the default mode (w/ Basic Tier) if not explicitly chosen.
---@field serverless? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigServerless Sets the backend to be the serverless mode offered by RAG Engine.

---Basic tier is a cost-effective and low compute tier suitable for the following cases: * Experimenting with RagManagedDb. * Small data size. * Latency insensitive workload. * Only using RAG Engine with external vector DBs. NOTE: This is the default tier under Spanner mode if not explicitly chosen.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigBasic

---Enterprise tier offers production grade performance along with autoscaling functionality. It is suitable for customers with large amounts of data or performance sensitive workloads.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigEnterprise

---Scaled tier offers production grade performance along with autoscaling functionality. It is suitable for customers with large amounts of data or performance sensitive workloads.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigScaled

---Message to configure the serverless mode offered by RAG Engine.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagManagedDbConfigServerless

