---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RetrieveSkillsResponseRetrievedSkillList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RetrieveSkillsResponseRetrievedSkill[]

---Configuration for rolling deployments.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RolloutOptions
---@field previousDeployedModel? string ID of the DeployedModel that this deployment should replace.
---@field revisionNumber? number Output only. Read-only. Revision number determines the relative priority of DeployedModels in the same rollout. The DeployedModel with the largest revision number specifies the intended state of the deployment.
---@field maxSurgeReplicas? number Absolute count of allowed additional replicas.
---@field maxUnavailableReplicas? number Absolute count of replicas allowed to be unavailable.
---@field maxUnavailablePercentage? number Percentage of replicas allowed to be unavailable. For autoscaling deployments, this refers to the target replica count.
---@field maxSurgePercentage? number Percentage of allowed additional replicas. For autoscaling deployments, this refers to the target replica count.

---Input for rouge metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeInput
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeInstanceList Required. Repeated rouge instances.
---@field metricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeSpec Required. Spec for rouge score metric.

---Spec for rouge instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeInstance
---@field reference? string Required. Ground truth used to compare against the prediction.
---@field prediction? string Required. Output of the evaluated model.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeInstanceList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeInstance[]

---Rouge metric value for an instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeMetricValue
---@field score? number Output only. Rouge score.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeMetricValueList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeMetricValue[]

---Results for rouge metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeResults
---@field rougeMetricValues? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeMetricValueList Output only. Rouge metric values.

---Spec for rouge score metric - calculates the recall of n-grams in prediction as compared to reference - returns a score ranging between 0 and 1.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RougeSpec
---@field splitSummaries? boolean Optional. Whether to split summaries while using rougeLsum.
---@field useStemmer? boolean Optional. Whether to use stemmer to compute rouge score.
---@field rougeType? string Optional. Supported rouge types are rougen[1-9], rougeL, and rougeLsum.

---Message representing a single testable criterion for evaluation. One input prompt could have multiple rubrics.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Rubric
---@field rubricId? string Unique identifier for the rubric. This ID is used to refer to this rubric, e.g., in RubricVerdict.
---@field content? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricContent Required. The actual testable criteria for the rubric.
---@field importance? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricImportanceEnum|string Optional. The relative importance of this rubric.
---@field type? string Optional. A type designator for the rubric, which can inform how it's evaluated or interpreted by systems or users. It's recommended to use consistent, well-defined, upper snake_case strings. Examples: "SUMMARIZATION_QUALITY", "SAFETY_HARMFUL_CONTENT", "INSTRUCTION_ADHERENCE".

---Instance and metric spec for RubricBasedInstructionFollowing metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricBasedInstructionFollowingInput
---@field instance? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricBasedInstructionFollowingInstance Required. Instance for RubricBasedInstructionFollowing metric.
---@field metricSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricBasedInstructionFollowingSpec Required. Spec for RubricBasedInstructionFollowing metric.

---Instance for RubricBasedInstructionFollowing metric - one instance corresponds to one row in an evaluation dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricBasedInstructionFollowingInstance
---@field jsonInstance? string Required. Instance specified as a json string. String key-value pairs are expected in the json_instance to render RubricBasedInstructionFollowing prompt templates.

---Result for RubricBasedInstructionFollowing metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricBasedInstructionFollowingResult
---@field score? number Output only. Overall score for the instruction following.
---@field rubricCritiqueResults? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricCritiqueResultList Output only. List of per rubric critique results.

---Spec for RubricBasedInstructionFollowing metric - returns rubrics and verdicts corresponding to rubrics along with overall score.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricBasedInstructionFollowingSpec

---Content of the rubric, defining the testable criteria.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricContent
---@field property? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricContentProperty Evaluation criteria based on a specific property.

---Defines criteria based on a specific property.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricContentProperty
---@field description? string Description of the property being evaluated. Example: "The model's response is grammatically correct."

---Rubric critique result.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricCritiqueResult
---@field verdict? boolean Output only. Verdict for the rubric - true if the rubric is met, false otherwise.
---@field rubric? string Output only. Rubric to be evaluated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricCritiqueResultList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricCritiqueResult[]

---Specification for how rubrics should be generated.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGenerationSpec
---@field rubricTypeOntology? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. An optional, pre-defined list of allowed types for generated rubrics. If this field is provided, it implies `include_rubric_type` should be true, and the generated rubric types should be chosen from this ontology.
---@field rubricContentType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGenerationSpecRubricContentTypeEnum|string The type of rubric content to be generated.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AutoraterConfig Configuration for the model used in rubric generation. Configs including sampling count and base model can be specified here. Flipping is not supported for rubric generation.
---@field promptTemplate? string Template for the prompt used to generate rubrics. The details should be updated based on the most-recent recipe requirements.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGenerationSpecRubricContentTypeEnum "RUBRIC_CONTENT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROPERTY"|"NL_QUESTION_ANSWER"|"PYTHON_CODE_ASSERTION"

---A group of rubrics, used for grouping rubrics based on a metric or a version.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGroup
---@field rubrics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricList Rubrics that are part of this group.
---@field displayName? string Human-readable name for the group. This should be unique within a given context if used for display or selection. Example: "Instruction Following V1", "Content Quality - Summarization Task".
---@field groupId? string Unique identifier for the group.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGroupMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricGroup }

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricImportanceEnum "IMPORTANCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"HIGH"|"MEDIUM"|"LOW"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Rubric[]

---Represents the verdict of an evaluation against a single rubric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricVerdict
---@field reasoning? string Optional. Human-readable reasoning or explanation for the verdict. This can include specific examples or details from the evaluated content that justify the given verdict.
---@field verdict? boolean Required. Outcome of the evaluation against the rubric, represented as a boolean. `true` indicates a "Pass", `false` indicates a "Fail".
---@field evaluatedRubric? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Rubric Required. The full rubric definition that was evaluated. Storing this ensures the verdict is self-contained and understandable, especially if the original rubric definition changes or was dynamically generated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricVerdictList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RubricVerdict[]

---The definition of a runtime artifact.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeArtifact
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ArtifactTypeSchema The type of the artifact.
---@field uri? string The URI of the artifact.
---@field properties? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ValueMap The properties of the artifact. Deprecated. Use RuntimeArtifact.metadata instead.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Properties of the Artifact.
---@field name? string The name of an artifact.
---@field customProperties? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ValueMap The custom properties of the artifact. Deprecated. Use RuntimeArtifact.metadata instead.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeArtifactList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeArtifact[]

---Runtime configuration to run the extension.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeConfig
---@field codeInterpreterRuntimeConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeConfigCodeInterpreterRuntimeConfig Code execution runtime configurations for code interpreter extension.
---@field defaultParams? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. Default parameters that will be set for all the execution of this extension. If specified, the parameter values can be overridden by values in [[ExecuteExtensionRequest.operation_params]] at request time. The struct should be in a form of map with param name as the key and actual param value as the value. E.g. If this operation requires a param "name" to be set to "abc". you can set this to something like {"name": "abc"}.
---@field vertexAiSearchRuntimeConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeConfigVertexAISearchRuntimeConfig Runtime configuration for Vertex AI Search extension.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeConfigCodeInterpreterRuntimeConfig
---@field fileInputGcsBucket? string Optional. The Cloud Storage bucket for file input of this Extension. If specified, support input from the Cloud Storage bucket. Vertex Extension Custom Code Service Agent should be granted file reader to this bucket. If not specified, the extension will only accept file contents from request body and reject Cloud Storage file inputs.
---@field fileOutputGcsBucket? string Optional. The Cloud Storage bucket for file output of this Extension. If specified, write all output files to the Cloud Storage bucket. Vertex Extension Custom Code Service Agent should be granted file writer to this bucket. If not specified, the file content will be output in response body.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RuntimeConfigVertexAISearchRuntimeConfig
---@field servingConfigName? string Optional. Vertex AI Search serving config name. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/servingConfigs/{serving_config}`
---@field engineId? string Optional. Vertex AI Search engine ID. This is used to construct the search request. By setting this engine_id, API will construct the serving config using the default value to call search API for the user. The engine_id and serving_config_name cannot both be empty at the same time.

---Input for safety metric.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SafetyInput
