---The specification of a SandboxEnvironmentTemplate. A SandboxEnvironmentTemplate defines a template for creating SandboxEnvironments.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplate
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this SandboxEnvironmentTemplate was created.
---@field egressControlConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateEgressControlConfig Optional. The configuration for egress control of this template.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the SandboxEnvironmentTemplate. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/sandboxEnvironmentTemplates/{sandbox_environment_template}`
---@field defaultContainerEnvironment? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateDefaultContainerEnvironment The sandbox environment for default container workloads.
---@field ingressControlConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PrivateServiceConnectConfig Optional. The configuration for private ingress (PSC-E) of this template. When set, the sandbox router is exposed privately via a PSC service attachment so VPC-SC customers can connect from their VPC over a private endpoint instead of the public internet. The resulting service attachment is surfaced on `SandboxEnvironment.connection_info.service_attachment`. Only the PSC-E (service-attachment/ingress) portion of `PrivateServiceConnectConfig` applies here: `enable_private_service_connect` and `project_allowlist` (the consumer projects allowed to connect). The nested `psc_interface_config` (PSC-I / egress) is not used for sandbox ingress; sandbox egress is configured via `egress_control_config` instead.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this SandboxEnvironmentTemplate was most recently updated.
---@field warmPoolConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateWarmPoolConfig Optional. The configuration for the warm pool of this template.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateStateEnum Output only. The state of the sandbox environment template.
---@field customContainerEnvironment? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateCustomContainerEnvironment The sandbox environment for custom container workloads.
---@field useGkeTd? boolean Optional. Immutable. Whether to provision the SandboxEnvironmentTemplate via the GKE TD pool.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the SandboxEnvironmentTemplate.
---@field persistentDiskConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplatePersistentDiskConfig Optional. Configuration for attaching a persistent disk (PD) to each SandboxEnvironment created from this template. When unset (or when `enabled` is `false`), sandboxes created from this template are not backed by a persistent disk and rely on ephemeral storage only. See PersistentDiskConfig for details.

---The customized sandbox runtime environment for BYOC.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateCustomContainerEnvironment
---@field customContainerSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateCustomContainerSpec The specification of the custom container environment.
---@field ports? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateNetworkPortList Ports to expose from the container.
---@field resources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateResourceRequirements Resource requests and limits for the container.

---Specification for deploying from a custom container image.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateCustomContainerSpec
---@field imageUri? string Required. The Artifact Registry Docker image URI (e.g., us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/my-project/my-repo/my-image:tag) of the container image that is to be run on each worker replica.

---The default sandbox runtime environment for default container workloads.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateDefaultContainerEnvironment
---@field defaultContainerCategory? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateDefaultContainerEnvironmentDefaultContainerCategoryEnum|string Required. The category of the default container image.
---@field resources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateResourceRequirements Optional. Resource requests and limits for the default container.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateDefaultContainerEnvironmentDefaultContainerCategoryEnum "DEFAULT_CONTAINER_CATEGORY_UNSPECIFIED"|"DEFAULT_CONTAINER_CATEGORY_COMPUTER_USE"|"DEFAULT_CONTAINER_CATEGORY_SHELL_SANDBOX"

---Configuration for egress control of sandbox instances.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateEgressControlConfig
---@field internetAccess? boolean Optional. Whether to allow internet access.
---@field dnsPeeringConfigs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateEgressControlConfigDnsPeeringConfigList Optional. DNS peering configurations that allow sandbox egress to resolve customer-internal domains via the customer VPC.
---@field networkAttachment? string Optional. The name of the customer VPC `NetworkAttachment` used to draw a PSC interface IP into the customer VPC for sandbox egress.

---Configuration for peering a customer's private DNS zone so that sandbox egress can resolve customer-internal domains via the customer VPC.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateEgressControlConfigDnsPeeringConfig
---@field targetNetwork? string Required. The VPC network name in the target_project where the DNS zone specified by `domain` is visible.
---@field targetProject? string Required. The project ID hosting the Cloud DNS managed zone that contains the `domain`. The Vertex AI Service Agent requires the dns.peer role on this project.
---@field domain? string Required. The DNS name suffix of the zone being peered to, e.g., "my-internal-domain.corp.". Must end with a dot.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateEgressControlConfigDnsPeeringConfigList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateEgressControlConfigDnsPeeringConfig[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplate[]

---Represents a network port in a container.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateNetworkPort
---@field port? number Optional. Port number to expose. This must be a valid port number, between 1 and 65535.
---@field protocol? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateNetworkPortProtocolEnum|string Optional. Protocol for port. Defaults to TCP if not specified.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateNetworkPortList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateNetworkPort[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateNetworkPortProtocolEnum "PROTOCOL_UNSPECIFIED"|"TCP"|"UDP"

---Configuration for attaching a persistent disk (PD) to each SandboxEnvironment created from this template. A persistent disk provides durable, per-sandbox block storage whose contents survive across the sandbox lifecycle events that this service supports (e.g. pause/resume), unlike ephemeral local storage which is lost when the underlying runtime is torn down.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplatePersistentDiskConfig
---@field enabled? boolean Optional. Whether a persistent disk is attached to sandboxes created from this template. Defaults to `false`. This flag lets a template carry (and preserve) disk configuration while keeping the disk detached, so it can be toggled on later without re-specifying the rest of the config. When `false`, the remaining fields in this message are ignored.
---@field mountPath? string Optional. The absolute path inside the sandbox container at which the persistent disk is mounted. Defaults to `/workspace` when unset. Ignored when `enabled` is `false`. Only writes beneath this path land on the disk. Writes elsewhere go to the container's writable layer, which counts against the container's ephemeral storage and is lost when the sandbox's runtime is torn down, so this should be the directory the workload actually writes to. Paths that would shadow the container's system directories (for example `/etc`, `/proc`, or `/usr` itself) are rejected.
---@field sizeGb? string Optional. The size of the persistent disk in GB. Must be non-negative. When `enabled` is `true`, a positive value is required; when unset or zero while enabled, the service applies a default size. Ignored when `enabled` is `false`.

---Message to define resource requests and limits (mirroring Kubernetes) for each sandbox instance created from this template.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateResourceRequirements
---@field requests? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The requested amounts of compute resources. Keys are resource names (e.g., "cpu", "memory"). Values are quantities (e.g., "250m", "512Mi").
---@field limits? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The maximum amounts of compute resources allowed. Keys are resource names (e.g., "cpu", "memory"). Values are quantities (e.g., "500m", "1Gi").

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateStateEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"PROVISIONING"|"ACTIVE"|"DEPROVISIONING"|"DELETED"|"FAILED"

---Configuration for a warm pool of sandbox instances.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateWarmPoolConfig
---@field targetInstanceCount? number Optional. The target number of pre-warmed instances to maintain.
---@field updateStrategy? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateWarmPoolConfigUpdateStrategyEnum|string Optional. The strategy for updating warm pool instances when the template is updated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SandboxEnvironmentTemplateWarmPoolConfigUpdateStrategyEnum "UPDATE_STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"ON_REPLENISH"|"RECREATE"

---A SavedQuery is a view of the dataset. It references a subset of annotations by problem type and filters.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SavedQuery
---@field problemType? string Required. Problem type of the SavedQuery. Allowed values: * IMAGE_CLASSIFICATION_SINGLE_LABEL * IMAGE_CLASSIFICATION_MULTI_LABEL * IMAGE_BOUNDING_POLY * IMAGE_BOUNDING_BOX * TEXT_CLASSIFICATION_SINGLE_LABEL * TEXT_CLASSIFICATION_MULTI_LABEL * TEXT_EXTRACTION * TEXT_SENTIMENT * VIDEO_CLASSIFICATION * VIDEO_OBJECT_TRACKING
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the SavedQuery.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when SavedQuery was last updated.
---@field annotationSpecCount? number Output only. Number of AnnotationSpecs in the context of the SavedQuery.
---@field supportAutomlTraining? boolean Output only. If the Annotations belonging to the SavedQuery can be used for AutoML training.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the SavedQuery. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field etag? string Used to perform a consistent read-modify-write update. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field metadata? any Some additional information about the SavedQuery.
---@field annotationFilter? string Output only. Filters on the Annotations in the dataset.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this SavedQuery was created.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SavedQueryList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SavedQuery[]

---One point viewable on a scalar metric plot.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Scalar
---@field value? number Value of the point at this step / timestamp.

---An instance of a Schedule periodically schedules runs to make API calls based on user specified time specification and API request type.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schedule
---@field endTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which no new runs can be scheduled. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either end_time is reached or when scheduled_run_count >= max_run_count. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field cron? string Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) to launch scheduled runs. To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or "TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, "CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *", or "TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *".
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule should schedule the next run. Having a next_run_time in the past means the runs are being started behind schedule.
---@field maxRunCount? string Optional. Maximum run count of the schedule. If specified, The schedule will be completed when either started_run_count >= max_run_count or when end_time is reached. If not specified, new runs will keep getting scheduled until this Schedule is paused or deleted. Already scheduled runs will be allowed to complete. Unset if not specified.
---@field maxConcurrentRunCount? string Required. Maximum number of runs that can be started concurrently for this Schedule. This is the limit for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable).
---@field createPipelineJobRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreatePipelineJobRequest Request for PipelineService.CreatePipelineJob. CreatePipelineJobRequest.parent field is required (format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}).
---@field catchUp? boolean Output only. Whether to backfill missed runs when the schedule is resumed from PAUSED state. If set to true, all missed runs will be scheduled. New runs will be scheduled after the backfill is complete. Default to false.
---@field createModelMonitoringJobRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateModelMonitoringJobRequest Request for ModelMonitoringService.CreateModelMonitoringJob.
---@field lastScheduledRunResponse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleRunResponse Output only. Response of the last scheduled run. This is the response for starting the scheduled requests and not the execution of the operations/jobs created by the requests (if applicable). Unset if no run has been scheduled yet.
---@field maxConcurrentActiveRunCount? string Optional. Specifies the maximum number of active runs that can be executed concurrently for this Schedule. This limits the number of runs that can be in a non-terminal state at the same time. Currently, this field is only supported for requests of type CreatePipelineJobRequest.
---@field startTime? string Optional. Timestamp after which the first run can be scheduled. Default to Schedule create time if not specified.
---@field createNotebookExecutionJobRequest? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CreateNotebookExecutionJobRequest Request for NotebookService.CreateNotebookExecutionJob.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was updated.
---@field lastPauseTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last paused. Unset if never paused.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleStateEnum Output only. The state of this Schedule.
---@field displayName? string Required. User provided name of the Schedule. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field startedRunCount? string Output only. The number of runs started by this schedule.
---@field lastResumeTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was last resumed. Unset if never resumed from pause.
---@field name? string Immutable. The resource name of the Schedule.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Schedule was created.
---@field allowQueueing? boolean Optional. Whether new scheduled runs can be queued when max_concurrent_runs limit is reached. If set to true, new runs will be queued instead of skipped. Default to false.

---Schedule configuration for the FeatureMonitor.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleConfig
---@field cron? string Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) to launch scheduled runs. To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or "TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, "CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *", or "TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *".

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schedule[]

---Status of a scheduled run.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleRunResponse
---@field scheduledRunTime? string The scheduled run time based on the user-specified schedule.
---@field runResponse? string The response of the scheduled run.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ScheduleStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"PAUSED"|"COMPLETED"

---All parameters related to queuing and scheduling of custom jobs.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Scheduling
---@field timeout? string Optional. The maximum job running time. The default is 7 days.
---@field restartJobOnWorkerRestart? boolean Optional. Restarts the entire CustomJob if a worker gets restarted. This feature can be used by distributed training jobs that are not resilient to workers leaving and joining a job.
---@field strategy? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchedulingStrategyEnum|string Optional. This determines which type of scheduling strategy to use.
---@field maxWaitDuration? string Optional. This is the maximum duration that a job will wait for the requested resources to be provisioned if the scheduling strategy is set to [Strategy.DWS_FLEX_START]. If set to 0, the job will wait indefinitely. The default is 24 hours.
---@field disableRetries? boolean Optional. Indicates if the job should retry for internal errors after the job starts running. If true, overrides `Scheduling.restart_job_on_worker_restart` to false.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchedulingStrategyEnum "STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"ON_DEMAND"|"LOW_COST"|"STANDARD"|"SPOT"|"FLEX_START"

---Defines the schema of input and output data. This is a subset of the [OpenAPI 3.0 Schema Object](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.3#schema-object).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema
---@field pattern? string Optional. If type is `STRING`, `pattern` specifies a regular expression that the string must match.
---@field items? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema Optional. If type is `ARRAY`, `items` specifies the schema of elements in the array.
---@field maximum? number Optional. If type is `INTEGER` or `NUMBER`, `maximum` specifies the maximum allowed value.
---@field default? any Optional. Default value to use if the field is not specified.
---@field enum? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Possible values of the field. This field can be used to restrict a value to a fixed set of values. To mark a field as an enum, set `format` to `enum` and provide the list of possible values in `enum`. For example: 1. To define directions: `{type:STRING, format:enum, enum:["EAST", "NORTH", "SOUTH", "WEST"]}` 2. To define apartment numbers: `{type:INTEGER, format:enum, enum:["101", "201", "301"]}`
---@field minItems? string Optional. If type is `ARRAY`, `min_items` specifies the minimum number of items in an array.
---@field minProperties? string Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `min_properties` specifies the minimum number of properties that can be provided.
---@field anyOf? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaList Optional. The instance must be valid against any (one or more) of the subschemas listed in `any_of`.
---@field properties? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaMap Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `properties` is a map of property names to schema definitions for each property of the object.
---@field maxLength? string Optional. If type is `STRING`, `max_length` specifies the maximum length of the string.
---@field minLength? string Optional. If type is `STRING`, `min_length` specifies the minimum length of the string.
---@field maxItems? string Optional. If type is `ARRAY`, `max_items` specifies the maximum number of items in an array.
---@field ref? string Optional. Allows referencing another schema definition to use in place of this schema. The value must be a valid reference to a schema in `defs`. For example, the following schema defines a reference to a schema node named "Pet": type: object properties: pet: ref: #/defs/Pet defs: Pet: type: object properties: name: type: string The value of the "pet" property is a reference to the schema node named "Pet". See details in https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/structuring
---@field type? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaTypeEnum|string Optional. Data type of the schema field.
---@field description? string Optional. Describes the data. The model uses this field to understand the purpose of the schema and how to use it. It is a best practice to provide a clear and descriptive explanation for the schema and its properties here, rather than in the prompt.
---@field maxProperties? string Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `max_properties` specifies the maximum number of properties that can be provided.
---@field example? any Optional. Example of an instance of this schema.
---@field title? string Optional. Title for the schema.
---@field format? string Optional. The format of the data. For `NUMBER` type, format can be `float` or `double`. For `INTEGER` type, format can be `int32` or `int64`. For `STRING` type, format can be `email`, `byte`, `date`, `date-time`, `password`, and other formats to further refine the data type.
---@field minimum? number Optional. If type is `INTEGER` or `NUMBER`, `minimum` specifies the minimum allowed value.
---@field nullable? boolean Optional. Indicates if the value of this field can be null.
---@field propertyOrdering? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Order of properties displayed or used where order matters. This is not a standard field in OpenAPI specification, but can be used to control the order of properties.
---@field defs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaMap Optional. `defs` provides a map of schema definitions that can be reused by `ref` elsewhere in the schema. Only allowed at root level of the schema.
---@field additionalProperties? any Optional. If `type` is `OBJECT`, specifies how to handle properties not defined in `properties`. If it is a boolean `false`, no additional properties are allowed. If it is a schema, additional properties are allowed if they conform to the schema.
---@field required? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `required` lists the names of properties that must be present.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema[]

