---A set of Shielded Instance options. See [Images using supported Shielded VM features](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/modifying-shielded-vm).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ShieldedVmConfig
---@field enableSecureBoot? boolean Defines whether the instance has [Secure Boot](https://cloud.google.com/compute/shielded-vm/docs/shielded-vm#secure-boot) enabled. Secure Boot helps ensure that the system only runs authentic software by verifying the digital signature of all boot components, and halting the boot process if signature verification fails.

---SingleReinforcementTuningRewardConfig defines a single reward function configuration for RL tuning. Each reward calculation/evaluation consists of two stages: 1. Stage 1: Parses the part of information important from sample response via regex extract, or simply takes the sample response unmodified. 2. Stage 2: Calls the configured reward scorer to compute the reward.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SingleReinforcementTuningRewardConfig
---@field autoraterScorer? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReinforcementTuningAutoraterScorer ReinforcementTuningAutoraterScorer is used to score parsed responses based on score computed by an autorater.
---@field rewardName? string A unique reward name for identifying each single reinforcement tuning reward.
---@field codeExecutionRewardScorer? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReinforcementTuningCodeExecutionRewardScorer ReinforcementTuningCodeExecutionRewardScorer is used to score parsed responses for code execution use cases.
---@field parseResponseConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReinforcementTuningParseResponseConfig Defines how to parse sample response. For example, given a sample response for evaluating the reward, users might want to extract the text only between `` and `` in the sample response, and keeps only the last one in case there are multiple such tags. To achieve such a purpose, they can define a regex `".*(.*?)"` using the ReinforcementTuningParseResponseConfig.ResponseParseType.REGEX_EXTRACT parse type.
---@field cloudRunRewardScorer? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReinforcementTuningCloudRunRewardScorer ReinforcementTuningCloudRunRewardScorer is used to score parsed responses by calling a Cloud Run service.
---@field stringMatchRewardScorer? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ReinforcementTuningStringMatchRewardScorer ReinforcementTuningStringMatchRewardScorer is used to score parsed responses for simple string matching use cases against reference answers.

---A skill.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Skill
---@field displayName? string Required. Provides the display name of the Skill. This should align with `name` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SkillStateEnum Output only. The state of the Skill.
---@field skillSource? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SkillSkillSourceEnum Output only. The source of the Skill.
---@field license? string Optional. Specifies the license of the Skill. This should be an SPDX license identifier (e.g., "MIT", "Apache-2.0"). See https://spdx.org/licenses/. This should align with `license` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the Skill. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/skills/{skill}`
---@field sha256? string Output only. The SHA256 checksum of the zipped filesystem.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Skill was created.
---@field zippedFilesystem? string Required. Provides the zipped filesystem of the Skill. This should contain the `SKILL.md` file at the root of the zip and optional directories for scripts, references, and assets. Directory should align with the directory structure specified at https://agentskills.io/specification#directory-structure.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize Skills.
---@field description? string Required. Describes the Skill. Should describe both what the skill does and when to use it. Should include specific keywords that help agents identify relevant tasks. This should align with `description` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field compatibility? string Optional. Specifies the compatibility of the Skill. Indicates environment requirements (intended product, system packages, network access, etc.). This should align with `compatibility` in the `SKILL.md` file.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Skill was most recently updated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SkillList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Skill[]

