---Server reply confirming a new task was created.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskCreatedEvent
---@field task? string Resource name of the created task. The client uses this id to reconnect (via a subscribe_task connect request) after a dropped stream. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}/tasks/{task}
---@field clientId? string The client identifier bound to this stream connection (either echoed from CreateTaskEvent or server-generated). Use this ID in SubscribeTaskEvent to resume after a disconnect.

---Defines a generation strategy based on a general task description.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskDescriptionStrategy
---@field taskDescription? string Required. A general description of the type of synthetic data you want to generate. For example, "Generate customer reviews for a new smartphone."

---An event that occurred for a task. Note that TaskEvent is just a record of task's change. Hence, it's not a Cloud resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskEvent
---@field eventData? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskEventData Required. The delta associated with the event.
---@field eventSequenceNumber? string Required. The sequence number of the event. This is used to uniquely identify the event within the task and order events chronologically. This is a id generated by the SDK.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The create time of the event.

---Data for a TaskEvent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskEventData
