---@field outputChange? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskOutputChange Optional. A change to the task's final outputs.
---@field metadataChange? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskMetadataChange Optional. A change to the task's metadata.
---@field stateChange? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStateChange Optional. A change in the task's state.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskEventList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskEvent[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Task[]

---Task-level memory settings: which sources memory draws from, and whether memory is active for this task at all.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskMemoryConfig
---@field knowledgeCatalogConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1KnowledgeCatalogConfig Optional. Configuration for enterprise Knowledge Catalog search.
---@field disableMemory? boolean Optional. If true, the agent neither reads existing memories into the prompt nor forms new ones from this task. Memory is on by default, and this can only turn it off, never back on: * Agent memory enabled, this true: off for this task. * Agent memory enabled, this false or unset: on. * Agent memory disabled: off, whatever this says. Because a task belongs to a single end user's interaction, a surface that knows the user can use this to turn memory off for one user of a shared agent; memory keeps working for the agent's other users. `Agent.memory_config.disable_memory` wins because it is the mutable one. It can be turned on after tasks have already been created, and a stored task spec keeps whatever it was created with — so if a spec could re-enable memory, the agent-level switch would be unable to cover the tasks that already exist. The two are therefore OR'ed, and the agent's current value is re-applied every time a session opens, including on a resume. Scoped to this task. Memories already stored for the agent are retained and stay readable by the agent's users; this governs only whether this task can access and modify them.

---Represents a single message in a conversation, compliant with the A2A specification.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskMessage
---@field parts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartList Required. The parts of the message.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Optional. A2A message may have extension_uris or reference_task_ids. They will be stored under metadata.
---@field role? string Required. The role of the sender of the message. e.g. "user", "agent"
---@field messageId? string Required. The unique identifier of the message.

---An event representing a change to the task's top-level metadata. example: metadata_change: { new_metadata: { "name": "My task", } update_mask: { paths: "name" } }
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskMetadataChange
---@field updateMask? string Optional. A field mask indicating which paths in the Struct were changed. If not set, all fields will be updated. go/aip-internal/cloud-standard/2412
---@field newMetadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.DocumentMap Required. The complete state of the metadata object *after* the change.

---Represents the final output of a task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskOutput
---@field artifacts? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskArtifactList Optional. A list of artifacts (files, data) produced by the task.

---An event representing a change to the task's outputs.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskOutputChange
---@field taskArtifactChange? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskArtifactChange Required. A granular change to the list of artifacts.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskScheduleStateEnum "SCHEDULE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SCHEDULE_ACTIVE"|"SCHEDULE_PAUSED"|"SCHEDULE_FINISHED"

---A single Server -> Client event. There is intentionally no non-terminal error/notice branch. Transient, retriable failures (tool-fetch retry, rate-limit, scheduler retry) are handled by runtime retry (bounded by TaskSpec.max_retries) and, if surfaced at all, appear as trajectory steps; the terminal error is reported once via TaskCompletedEvent.outcome.status (google.rpc.Status). This follows the Interactions events.proto, which deprecated its dedicated non-terminal InteractionPausedEvent and reports terminal status on InteractionCompletedEvent.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskServerEvent
---@field seqNum? string Required. 1-based, non-decreasing sequence number within the server direction, stable across reconnects, so it can be used to resume: a given event carries the same number however the stream is (re)connected. Gapless on a stream delivered from the beginning. Clients acknowledge receipt via ack_output_seq_num and resume via SubscribeTaskEvent.next_step_seq_num. A resume with next_step_seq_num = 0 (or unset) restarts from the first still available step. A number identifies a resume point, not an event, so it is not unique: consecutive events can share one. An event derived from another (an artifacts_changed delta carrying the plan its step just wrote) repeats its source's number rather than taking the next, which keeps the numbering a function of the stream alone and guarantees a cursor never lands between the two. Acknowledging a number acknowledges every event carrying it. A resume can begin AFTER the requested number. next_step_seq_num counts events, but a streamed step spans several of them, so a cursor can point inside a run; the server then suppresses that run's remaining step_delta/step_stop rather than deliver frames for a step the client never saw opened, and resumes at the next step boundary. Numbering is unchanged by that suppression -- keeping it stable is what makes a cursor meaningful across connections -- so the first delivered event may be a later number than asked for. Treat the sequence as monotonic, not densely contiguous, when resuming.
---@field timestampMicros? string Strictly increasing generation timestamp, in unix micros.
---@field taskUpdate? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskUpdateEvent A change to the task's details.
---@field statusChanged? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEvent A coarse status transition (e.g. WORKING -> REQUIRES_ACTION when the task is waiting on a human response).
---@field stepUsage? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiInteractionUsage Optional. Token usage for one model call. Populated on at most one event per model call regardless of `TaskSpec.delta_streaming`, and absent on non-model events (tool results, user-input echoes, status changes).
---@field continuationToken? string Optional. Opaque resume cursor covering everything delivered through this event, inclusive. A client that keeps the token from the last event it processed and passes it back on SubscribeTaskEvent.continuation_token or StreamTaskRequest.continuation_token resumes at the next event, with no gap and no duplicate. Opaque: the encoding is a server implementation detail and may change without notice. Do not parse it, compare two of them, or derive ordering from it -- order by `seq_num`. Carries no task id, because every RPC that redeems a token already names the task it applies to. It is a position, not a capability: it grants no access on its own, and the task's IAM check is what authorizes the read. This is the resume cursor. Resuming by number (next_step_seq_num on SubscribeTaskEvent and StreamTaskRequest) is slated for deprecation: a number cannot address a position inside a streamed step, while the token can, so a reconnect mid-answer does not re-send the part of that answer the client already rendered. `seq_num` remains for ordering only.
---@field stepStart? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiStepStart Opens a streamed step. Emitted only under `TaskSpec.delta_streaming`, which documents the two delivery modes in full. Under `delta_streaming` EVERY step arrives as a `step_start` / `step_delta`* / `step_stop` run sharing an `index`, and a bare `step` is never emitted. Reassembling a run yields the same Step that `step` above would otherwise have delivered. What follows a `step_start` depends on whether the content is generated progressively. Assistant text (and the citations on it) and thoughts stream across the run's `step_delta`s as they are produced, so for those this field carries the step's shape (role, type) with its generated content left empty. A step that arrives whole -- tool calls, tool results, elicitations, user-input echoes, errors -- carries no `step_delta` at all: the COMPLETE step rides this field, and `step_stop` closes the run.
---@field stepDelta? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiStepDelta One chunk of a streamed step, carrying only the content generated since the previous chunk. Chunks sharing an `index` belong to one step and concatenate in the order received.
---@field trajectoryId? string Optional. The runtime trajectory UUID that produced this event's step, e.g. "e9df8df3-d63a-4747-ad00-eaef837d7d31". A debugging correlation handle and the join key to the runtime's per-step trajectory record (for Sobi, the Trajectory Store viewer at sobi.corp.google.com/trajectory/). Set on the step-bearing events (`step` and the `step_start` of a streamed step); empty on status_changed / artifacts_changed and on the step_delta/step_stop frames continuing a run (correlate those by `index` with their step_start). Also empty on steps the Sobi converter did not build: the actor delivers `elicitation_call` as a native `Step` payload with no field 110, and `Session::ReadConverted` forwards it unchanged (`jetski_to_interaction_stream_converter.cc:1101-1104`), so a HITL turn reaches the client on `step` with `trajectory_id` empty even though a trajectory does exist for it. A whole turn shares one trajectory id. The server never derives behavior from it. See b/552010818.
---@field eventId? string Optional. The TaskClientEvent.event_id this event was derived from, echoed back verbatim. Set only on the events that carry a client input back out: the `step` echoing the input, and the `step_start` of a streamed step the input opened. Empty everywhere else -- on model-generated steps the server produced on its own, on the step_delta/step_stop frames continuing a run (correlate those by `index` with their step_start), and on any event whose client input carried no event_id. Purely a correlation handle: it does not order or acknowledge anything, and the server never derives behavior from it. Since the server does not enforce uniqueness, a client that reuses an id sees it on every echo it produced. Delivered to every client subscribed to the task, not just the one that sent the input, including on a later replay from storage.
---@field stepStop? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiStepStop Closes a streamed step, carrying its token usage. No further `step_delta` arrives for this `index`.
---@field step? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiStep A trajectory output step (thought, tool call, content, elicitation_call, etc.). Human-in-the-loop requests are just steps: the server emits an ElicitationCallStep (for an approval / choice) or a ToolCallStep (for a client-executed tool), and the client responds with the matching ElicitationResultStep / ToolResultStep, correlated by elicitation_id / call_id. The kind of action required is inferred from the step's type, so there is no separate "action required" event.

---Server -> Client message for TaskService.CreateTaskBidiStream. * The first message carries a connect_reply (task_created or task_subscribed). * The steady-state pattern is repeated `events` (steps, status). * The last message carries an end_signal.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskServerEventBatch
---@field taskSubscribed? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSubscribedEvent Reply to subscribe_task.
---@field ackInputSeqNum? string Optional. When non-zero, confirms cumulative receipt of client input through this seq_num (inclusive).
---@field taskCompleted? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskCompletedEvent The task reached a terminal status.
---@field taskCreated? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskCreatedEvent Reply to create_task: returns the new task name.
---@field assignedAgentIdentity? string Output only. The resolved Agent Identity (SPIFFE ID) of the `Agent` this task is assigned to. Populated on the first message of the stream.
---@field events? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskServerEventList Steady-state events from the server (trajectory steps -- including elicitation/tool-call HITL requests -- and status changes).

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskServerEventList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskServerEvent[]

---The centralized specification of a Task: the scoped context it runs in, when it runs, the resource guardrails, and the goal (with verifiers).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpec
---@field schedule? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskTrigger Optional. Optional schedule controlling when/how the task runs. If unset, the task runs immediately (one-off, now).
---@field subtaskConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecSubtaskConfig Optional. Configuration and limits for subtasks spawned by this task.
---@field budget? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Budget Optional. Optional holistic budget caps metered across the entire task lifetime.
---@field systemInstruction? string Optional. Optional standing instruction applied across the whole task.
---@field maxRetries? number Optional. Deprecated: tasks are not retried automatically. CreateTask and UpdateTask reject a non-zero value with INVALID_ARGUMENT.
---@field hitlConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecHitlConfig Optional. Immutable. Session-level HITL (human-in-the-loop) configuration for this task. Unset means every HITL knob takes its default; see `HitlConfig` above for the individual field defaults.
---@field inputs? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiStepList Optional. The prompt expressed as Interaction steps (e.g. a ContentStep with the user's request). Reuses the Interactions step model so the same content flows into the runtime unchanged. Required for a scheduled or PRIORITY_DEFERRED task, which starts with no caller attached. Otherwise it may be empty: * Unary CreateTask with no inputs creates the task IDLE and dispatches nothing. The task starts when a caller subscribes to it on CreateTaskBidiStream (`subscribe_task`) and sends the first input. * CreateTaskBidiStream `create_task` with no inputs is a connect-only / pre-warm create; the first input is sent later as a client step. Recommended pattern for giving a task files before it runs: 1. CreateTask with empty `inputs`. The task is IDLE; nothing runs yet. 2. UploadTaskArtifact each file to `/workspace/userdata/`. 3. CreateTaskBidiStream with `subscribe_task`, then send the first input, referring to the files by their `/workspace/userdata/` paths. This dispatches the task with the uploaded files in its workspace.
---@field deltaStreaming? boolean Optional. Whether incrementally generated content is delivered as it is produced, rather than once the step is finished. The two modes are exact duals. If false (default), every step arrives once, complete, in TaskServerEvent.step -- so a client that reads only `step` sees the whole conversation. Suited to non-chat callers that consume finished steps. If true, EVERY step instead arrives as a `step_start` / `step_delta`* / `step_stop` run sharing an index, so a chat client sees one uniform lifecycle and never a bare `step`; reassembling a run yields the same step that would otherwise have been delivered. Content the model generates progressively -- assistant text (and the citations on it) and thoughts -- streams natively across the run's `step_delta`s as it is produced. A step that arrives whole (tool calls, tool results, elicitations, user-input echoes, errors) carries no `step_delta`: the complete step rides `step_start` and `step_stop` closes the run, since nothing is generated incrementally. The field is deliberately not named for text: what streams progressively is an implementation detail that may widen, and a client asking for incremental delivery wants it for whatever supports it. Note per-step token usage rides `step_stop`, so it is reported only when this is true.
---@field priority? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecPriorityEnum|string Optional. Optional priority band. Concrete tiers and quota are out of scope and deferred to a follow-up.
---@field scope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ContextScope Optional. Optional scoped context: skills/tools/memory/artifacts for the task.
---@field expectedOutput? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GenaiResponseFormat Optional. Optional structured deliverable contract (reuses the Interactions ResponseFormat). When set, the agent's final output must conform to it.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecModelConfig Optional. Optional model configuration override for the task. When set, the task runs on this model configuration for its entire lifecycle.

---Session-level HITL (human-in-the-loop) configuration. Namespaces every HITL knob that a client may set at task creation, so new settings (per-tool overrides, timeout, allowed reviewers) can land without burning more top-level TaskSpec tags. `approval_mode` carries the wire default as its own `APPROVAL_MODE_UNSPECIFIED` enum value, which the server treats as `APPROVAL_MODE_ASK` (standard HITL, always prompt a human). That is also the pre-change behavior for every existing task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecHitlConfig
---@field approvalMode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecHitlConfigApprovalModeEnum|string Optional. Immutable. How the client wants elicitations on this task approved. Unset (or APPROVAL_MODE_UNSPECIFIED) is treated as APPROVAL_MODE_ASK.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecHitlConfigApprovalModeEnum "APPROVAL_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"APPROVAL_MODE_ASK"|"APPROVAL_MODE_AUTO"

---Selects the model the task runs on. Starts with just the model id/alias; extensible with further model parameters without a breaking change.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecModelConfig
---@field modelSelectionMode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecModelConfigModelSelectionModeEnum|string Optional. How the model in `model` was selected. Ignored when set on `LiveConfig.model_config`.
---@field model? string Optional. Publisher model resource name (an `aiplatform.googleapis.com/PublisherModel`) of the form "publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}", e.g. "publishers/anthropic/models/claude-opus-4-8" or "publishers/google/models/gemini-3-flash". The project-qualified form "projects/{project}/locations/{location}/publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}" is also accepted. When it is used, the project and location it carries take precedence over both dynamic project/location resolution and the actor config defaults. Model selection cannot be updated after task creation right now though it might be supported in the future. Empty means the actor's default gemini model.
---@field temperature? number Optional. Sampling temperature for the model's generation config (valid range (0.0, 2.0]); a value outside that range leaves the backend default standing.
---@field effortLevel? string Optional. Reasoning/thinking depth the model runs at, case-insensitive. Gemini takes "minimal", "low", "medium" or "high", and only on models that have a thinking level; other publishers define their own set. A value the resolved model does not accept leaves its own default standing.
---@field maxOutputTokens? number Optional. Maximum number of tokens the model may generate in each call, including any thinking tokens it spends before answering. Must not be negative; zero leaves the backend default standing. The cap also applies to the calls that summarize the task's history when its context is compacted, so a model that thinks at a high effort level may need a larger value to return a summary at all.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecModelConfigModelSelectionModeEnum "MODEL_SELECTION_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AUTO"|"USER_SELECTED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecPriorityEnum "PRIORITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRIORITY_REALTIME"|"PRIORITY_DEFERRED"

---Configuration and limits for subtasks spawned by this task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpecSubtaskConfig
---@field maxDepth? number Optional. The maximum depth of subtask hierarchy allowed under this task. Must be between 0 and 5, inclusive. When unset on a root task, defaults to 5. For a subtask, it is clamped to at most parent.max_depth - 1 (defaulting to parent.max_depth - 1 if unspecified). A value of 0 means this task cannot spawn any subtasks.

---A message representing a change in a task's state.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStateChange
---@field newState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStateChangeNewStateEnum|string Required. The new state of the task.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStateChangeNewStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUBMITTED"|"WORKING"|"COMPLETED"|"CANCELLED"|"FAILED"|"REJECTED"|"INPUT_REQUIRED"|"AUTH_REQUIRED"|"PAUSED"

---Why a task is in its current status, when the status alone is not enough to act on (today: `SUSPENDED`). Clients MUST treat an unrecognized `StatusReason` as an opaque block. Copied to the DB mirror by name and number, so a field or enum value added here without the matching DB-side addition is silently dropped on write. LINT.IfChange(status_detail)
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetail
---@field reason? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetailReasonEnum|string Machine-readable reason. Clients switch on this to pick a recovery affordance (upsell CTA, admin contact, retry).
---@field detail? string Optional human-readable explanation, so a surface can render something without its own StatusReason -> string table. Not localized; clients needing localization should render from `reason` instead. Not a `google.rpc.Status`: RPC codes do not map onto lifecycle states, and `TaskOutcome.status` already covers terminal failures.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetailReasonEnum "STATUS_REASON_UNSPECIFIED"|"QUOTA_EXHAUSTED"|"SPEND_CAP_REACHED"|"LICENSE_REQUIRED"|"ADMIN_SUSPENDED"|"PARENT_SUSPENDED"|"DEFERRED"|"CREDENTIALS_EXPIRED"|"BUDGET_EXHAUSTED"

---Represents the additional status details of a task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetails
---@field taskMessage? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskMessage Optional. The message associated with the single-turn interaction between the user and the agent or agent and agent.

---Represents a change to the task's status details.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetailsChange
---@field newTaskStatus? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetails Required. The complete state of the task's status *after* the change.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"IDLE"|"WORKING"|"REQUIRES_ACTION"|"COMPLETED"|"FAILED"|"CANCELLED"|"QUEUED"|"SUSPENDED"|"SUSPENDING"

---Signals a task status transition.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEvent
---@field statusDetail? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetail Machine-readable reason and details for why the task entered this status (e.g. `SUSPENDED`).
---@field taskStatus? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEventTaskStatusEnum The new coarse task status.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEventTaskStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"IDLE"|"WORKING"|"REQUIRES_ACTION"|"COMPLETED"|"FAILED"|"CANCELLED"|"QUEUED"|"SUSPENDED"|"SUSPENDING"

---Server reply confirming subscription to an existing task.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSubscribedEvent
---@field clientId? string The client identifier bound to this stream connection (either echoed from SubscribeTaskEvent or server-generated). Use this ID in subsequent SubscribeTaskEvent messages to maintain sequence continuity.
---@field nextStepSeqNum? string The next step sequence number the server will send: the position it resolved to from the subscribe request. The mirror of the same-named field on SubscribeTaskEvent -- there it is what the client asks for, here it is what the server settled on. Zero means no cursor was resolved: the request supplied neither next_step_seq_num nor ack_output_seq_num, so output replays from the oldest retained step.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSubscribedEventStatusEnum The current coarse status of the task at subscription time.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSubscribedEventStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"IDLE"|"WORKING"|"REQUIRES_ACTION"|"COMPLETED"|"FAILED"|"CANCELLED"|"QUEUED"|"SUSPENDED"|"SUSPENDING"

---Defines when and how a task runs.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskTrigger
---@field oneOff? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1OneOffSchedule Run exactly once (at an absolute time or after a delay).
---@field recurring? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RecurringSchedule Run the task spec repeatedly.

---A change to a task's details. Surfaces out the Task resource fields that change during execution.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskUpdateEvent
---@field updates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskUpdateEventTaskUpdateList The task detail changes carried by this event.

---A single task detail change.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskUpdateEventTaskUpdate
---@field title? string Concise title.
---@field summary? string Rolling progress/outcome summary.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskUpdateEventTaskUpdateList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskUpdateEventTaskUpdate[]

---One identity an agent is allowed to contact. A message rather than a bare string so a teammate can carry more than an address -- a display name, a group rather than a person, a scope limiting which surfaces the agent may reach them on -- without a breaking change to `AllowedTeammates`. Every field is optional, but a teammate identifying nobody is meaningless: at least one identifier must be set, and `UpdateAgent` rejects a teammate with none.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Teammate
---@field gaiaId? string Optional. Obfuscated Gaia id of the teammate. OBFUSCATED, never a raw Gaia id -- the same form as `Principal.id` and every other Gaia id this API surfaces, so the two are comparable. A string rather than an int64 for that reason: the obfuscated form is not a number.
---@field expansionMode? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TeammateExpansionModeEnum|string Optional. Expansion mode for group or space teammates.
---@field email? string Optional. Email address of the teammate.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TeammateExpansionModeEnum "EXPANSION_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INFER"|"EXPANDED"|"NON_EXPANDED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TeammateList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Teammate[]

