---Assigns input data to training, validation, and test sets based on a provided timestamps. The youngest data pieces are assigned to training set, next to validation set, and the oldest to the test set. Supported only for tabular Datasets.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TimestampSplit
---@field key? string Required. The key is a name of one of the Dataset's data columns. The values of the key (the values in the column) must be in RFC 3339 `date-time` format, where `time-offset` = `"Z"` (e.g. 1985-04-12T23:20:50.52Z). If for a piece of data the key is not present or has an invalid value, that piece is ignored by the pipeline.
---@field testFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to evaluate the Model.
---@field trainingFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to train the Model.
---@field validationFraction? number The fraction of the input data that is to be used to validate the Model.

---Tokens info with a list of tokens and the corresponding list of token ids.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TokensInfo
---@field role? string Optional. Optional fields for the role from the corresponding Content.
---@field tokens? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList A list of tokens from the input.
---@field tokenIds? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList A list of token ids from the input.

---@alias gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TokensInfoList gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TokensInfo[]

---Tool details that the model may use to generate response. A `Tool` is a piece of code that enables the system to interact with external systems to perform an action, or set of actions, outside of knowledge and scope of the model. A Tool object should contain exactly one type of Tool (e.g FunctionDeclaration, Retrieval or GoogleSearchRetrieval).
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Tool
---@field parallelAiSearch? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolParallelAiSearch Optional. If specified, Vertex AI will use Parallel.ai to search for information to answer user queries. The search results will be grounded on Parallel.ai and presented to the model for response generation
---@field computerUse? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolComputerUse Optional. Tool to support the model interacting directly with the computer. If enabled, it automatically populates computer-use specific Function Declarations.
---@field codeExecution? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolCodeExecution Optional. CodeExecution tool type. Enables the model to execute code as part of generation.
---@field googleMaps? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoogleMaps Optional. GoogleMaps tool type. Tool to support Google Maps in Model.
---@field googleSearchRetrieval? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoogleSearchRetrieval Optional. Specialized retrieval tool that is powered by Google Search.
---@field functionDeclarations? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionDeclarationList Optional. Function tool type. One or more function declarations to be passed to the model along with the current user query. Model may decide to call a subset of these functions by populating FunctionCall in the response. User should provide a FunctionResponse for each function call in the next turn. Based on the function responses, Model will generate the final response back to the user. Maximum 512 function declarations can be provided.
---@field exaAiSearch? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolExaAiSearch Optional. Uses Exa.ai to search for information to answer user queries. The search results will be grounded on Exa.ai and presented to the model for response generation
---@field googleSearch? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolGoogleSearch Optional. GoogleSearch tool type. Tool to support Google Search in Model. Powered by Google.
---@field urlContext? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1UrlContext Optional. Tool to support URL context retrieval.
---@field retrieval? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Retrieval Optional. Retrieval tool type. System will always execute the provided retrieval tool(s) to get external knowledge to answer the prompt. Retrieval results are presented to the model for generation.
---@field enterpriseWebSearch? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EnterpriseWebSearch Optional. Tool to support searching public web data, powered by Vertex AI Search and Sec4 compliance.

