---A set of tool references, each a tool's GCP resource name (`projects/.../mcpServers|endpoints/...`) with optional fine-grained method, CLI tool and resource guardrails. Wraps a repeated field so it can be used as an arm of the `ContextScope.tool_scope` oneof. LINT.IfChange(tool_refs)
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolRefs
---@field methods? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Optional fine-grained method selectors for the referenced tools. Format: "/methods/".
---@field cliToolScope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolRefsCliToolScope Optional. Optional CLI tool scope that the task is restricted to. Unset means all CLI tools are allowed. Set with an empty `cli_tools` list means all CLI tools are denied.
---@field resources? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ResourceRefList Optional. Optional resource identifiers that the task is restricted to interact with.
---@field toolNames? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Tool GCP resource names. For example: * MCP server: `projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/mcpServers/jira` * Endpoint: `projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/endpoints/drive`

---A CLI tool boundary restricting a subtask to designated CLI commands.
---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ToolRefsCliToolScope
---@field cliTools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Allowed CLI tools for the task. Example: ["gmail send_message", "calendar list_events"].

