---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.ListProjectsLocationsTasksRequest
---@field parent string Required. The parent to list tasks under. Both forms are accepted and scope the listing differently: * projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent} -- tasks assigned to that agent. * projects/{project}/locations/{location} -- all tasks in the location.
---@field filter? string Optional. A filter expression, e.g. "status=WORKING". Lineage filters pick how much of a task tree to fetch: * "parent_task_id=" -- direct children only (progressive disclosure, one level per call). * "root_task_id=" -- the whole tree in one flat collection. Label filters support filtering by task labels: * "labels.=" -- match tasks with the given label key and value. Multiple label filters can be combined with AND. Multiple values for the same key can be combined with OR, e.g., "labels.foo=bar OR labels.foo=baz". Status filters restrict the listing to tasks in the given statuses: * "status=" -- e.g. "status=WORKING". Multiple statuses can be combined with OR, e.g., "status=WORKING OR status=IDLE". Both page normally via `page_size`/`page_token`, and both are ordered by `order_by` (default "create_time desc"), not by tree shape. A whole-tree page is therefore not a subtree: a child can arrive before its parent, so the client buffers by `parent_task_id` and renders as parents resolve.
---@field pageToken? string Optional. A page token from a previous ListTasks call.
---@field pageSize? number Optional. The maximum number of tasks to return. The service may return fewer. If unspecified (or <= 0), at most 50 are returned. The maximum is 100; larger values are capped to 100.
---@field orderBy? string Optional. Sort order, e.g. "create_time desc". The sortable fields are `create_time` and `update_time`. Defaults to "create_time desc".

