---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.PatchDatasetsRequest
---@field metadata? any Required. Additional information about the Dataset.
---@field savedQueries? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SavedQueryList All SavedQueries belong to the Dataset will be returned in List/Get Dataset response. The annotation_specs field will not be populated except for UI cases which will only use annotation_spec_count. In CreateDataset request, a SavedQuery is created together if this field is set, up to one SavedQuery can be set in CreateDatasetRequest. The SavedQuery should not contain any AnnotationSpec.
---@field description? string The description of the Dataset.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Customer-managed encryption key spec for a Dataset. If set, this Dataset and all sub-resources of this Dataset will be secured by this key.
---@field modelReference? string Optional. Reference to the public base model last used by the dataset. Only set for prompt datasets.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Dataset was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Dataset was last updated.
---@field metadataArtifact? string Output only. The resource name of the Artifact that was created in MetadataStore when creating the Dataset. The Artifact resource name pattern is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/metadataStores/{metadata_store}/artifacts/{artifact}`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The user-defined name of the Dataset. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters.
---@field metadataSchemaUri? string Required. Points to a YAML file stored on Google Cloud Storage describing additional information about the Dataset. The schema is defined as an OpenAPI 3.0.2 Schema Object. The schema files that can be used here are found in gs://google-cloud-aiplatform/schema/dataset/metadata/.
---@field etag? string Used to perform consistent read-modify-write updates. If not set, a blind "overwrite" update happens.
---@field dataItemCount? string Output only. The number of DataItems in this Dataset. Only apply for non-structured Dataset.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap The labels with user-defined metadata to organize your Datasets. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. No more than 64 user labels can be associated with one Dataset (System labels are excluded). See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels. System reserved label keys are prefixed with "aiplatform.googleapis.com/" and are immutable. Following system labels exist for each Dataset: * "aiplatform.googleapis.com/dataset_metadata_schema": output only, its value is the metadata_schema's title.
---@field name string Output only. Identifier. The resource name of the Dataset. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}`
---@field updateMask? string Required. The update mask applies to the resource. For the `FieldMask` definition, see google.protobuf.FieldMask. Updatable fields: * `display_name` * `description` * `labels`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.PatchMemoryBanksMemoriesRequest
---@field scope? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Required. Immutable. Represents the scope of the Memory. Memories are isolated within their scope. The scope is defined when creating or generating memories. Scope values cannot contain the wildcard character '*'.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was created.
---@field description? string Optional. Represents the description of the Memory.
---@field fact? string Optional. Represents semantic knowledge extracted from the source content.
---@field revisionTtl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for the revision. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field structuredContent? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryStructuredContent Optional. Represents the structured content of the memory.
---@field ttl? string Optional. Input only. Represents the TTL for this resource. The expiration time is computed: now + TTL.
---@field topics? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryTopicIdList Optional. Represents the Topics of the Memory.
---@field memoryType? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMemoryTypeEnum|string Optional. Represents the type of the memory. If not set, the `NATURAL_LANGUAGE_COLLECTION` type is used. If `STRUCTURED_COLLECTION` or `STRUCTURED_PROFILE` is used, then `structured_data` must be provided.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Represents the display name of the Memory.
---@field expireTime? string Optional. Represents the timestamp of when this resource is considered expired. This is *always* provided on output when `expiration` is set on input, regardless of whether `expire_time` or `ttl` was provided.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the timestamp when this Memory was most recently updated.
---@field context? string Optional. Represents the context of the memory.
---@field revisionLabels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Represents the labels to apply to the Memory Revision created as a result of this request.
---@field revisionExpireTime? string Optional. Input only. Represents the timestamp of when the revision is considered expired. If not set, the memory revision will be kept until manually deleted.
---@field disableMemoryRevisions? boolean Optional. Input only. Indicates whether no revision will be created for this request.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MemoryMetadataValueMap Optional. Represents user-provided metadata for the Memory. This information was provided when creating, updating, or generating the Memory. It was not generated by Memory Bank.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Mask specifying which fields to update. The following fields are immutable: * `scope` * `memory_type`
---@field name string Identifier. Represents the resource name of the Memory. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/reasoningEngines/{reasoning_engine}/memories/{memory}`

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.PatchProjectsLocationsAgentsRequest
---@field created? string Output only. The time the agent was created.
---@field memoryConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentMemoryConfig Optional. Memory settings for the agent.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. The metadata for the agent.
---@field effectiveIdentity? string Output only. The resolved Agent Identity (SPIFFE principal) of the agent.
---@field base_agent? string Required. Immutable. The base agent for the agent. Supported values: * `antigravity-preview-05-2026` Immutable: `UpdateAgent` rejects a change, including clearing it. The kind of agent this is gets derived from this field when the agent is created and is recorded then; nothing recomputes it afterwards, so a later change would leave the agent described as one kind and behaving as another. Create a new agent instead.
---@field modelConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentModelConfig Optional. Model configuration for the agent. When set, tasks running under this agent default to this model configuration if they do not specify their own.
---@field persona? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Persona Optional. The persona (presentation) of the agent. Mutable: presentation only, not an archetype-derivation signal.
---@field id? string Immutable. The user-specified ID for the agent. This ID becomes the final component of the agent resource name. If not provided, Vertex AI will generate a value for this ID. The ID can be up to 63 characters and must match the regular expression `[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?`.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the agent.
---@field agentIdentity? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentIdentity Optional. Immutable. The identity configuration of the agent. Immutable: the agent's own identity determines the A2 (CoWorker) archetype and the minted SPIFFE, so it cannot change after creation (no A1<->A2 transition).
---@field object? string Output only. The object type of the resource. For agents, the value is `agent`.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability settings for this agent's sessions.
---@field updated? string Output only. The time the agent was last updated.
---@field encryptionSpec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1EncryptionSpec Optional. Immutable. Customer-managed encryption key spec for an Agent. If set, this agent's user data will be secured by this key; if not set, it is secured by a Google-managed key. Cannot be changed after the agent is created.
---@field base_environment? any Optional. The base environment configuration for the agent. Valid types: * A string value for the environment ID, or `remote` for the default. * A struct value for the `environment_config`.
---@field owner? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Principal Optional. The human owner (principal) the agent acts on behalf of (A1 Personal). Mutable by design: ownership is meant to be reassignable (e.g. by an admin). On create an A1 (Personal) agent may omit it and the control plane defaults it to the caller; an A2 (CoWorker) agent must set it explicitly. `owner.id` must be an *obfuscated* Gaia id. A raw Gaia id is rejected with INVALID_ARGUMENT naming the rule -- both forms are strings of decimal digits, so the surface would otherwise have two indistinguishable spellings of one identity. Not yet: `UpdateAgent` currently rejects a change to this field. The control plane authorizes every agent method against the owner Gaia id it persists internally at create time, and the update path does not maintain that copy — so a field write here would move the reported owner without moving the one access control uses. The guard comes out once reassignment moves both, along with the Workspace identity provisioned under the owner.
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentToolList Optional. The tools available to the agent.
---@field aiApplication? string Output only. The resource name of the AI Application provisioned for this agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/aiApplications/{ai_application}`.
---@field system_instruction? string Optional. The instructions for the agent to follow. These instructions are passed to the LLM as a system instruction.
---@field allowedTeammates? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AllowedTeammates Optional. The identities this agent is allowed to contact outbound (for example over Gmail or Chat). Stored on the agent and always returned by `GetAgent`; see the field comments on `AllowedTeammates`.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentStatus Output only. The current operational state of the agent.
---@field name string Identifier. The resource name of the agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to update. If not present, all fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.PatchProjectsLocationsAgentsTasksRequest
---@field summary? string Output only. A rolling, system-generated summary of the task's progress/result.
---@field statusDetail? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusDetail Output only. Explanation for the current state, when the state alone is not enough to act on (today: `SUSPENDED`). Cleared when the task leaves that state.
---@field scheduleState? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskScheduleStateEnum|string Output only. Scheduling lifecycle of a recurring template. Unset unless `spec.schedule.recurring` is set.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskStatusEnum|string Output only. The coarse, durable status of the task.
---@field rootTaskId? string Output only. Lineage group key: the root of this task's tree, materialized from `parent_task_id` (a root task's own short-form name). Same short form, and for the same reason, as `parent_task_id`. One `ListTasks(filter: "root_task_id=")` returns the whole tree as a flat, paginated collection, instead of a level-by-level walk that costs one round trip per depth. The client reassembles the tree from `parent_task_id`; a page may therefore contain a task whose parent lands on a later page.
---@field spec? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TaskSpec Required. The full specification of what to do, how to run it, and how to know it is done.
---@field budgetConsumptionDetail? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1BudgetConsumptionDetail Output only. Current budget consumption detail of the Task.
---@field assignedAgentIdentity? string Output only. The resolved Agent Identity (SPIFFE ID) of the `Agent` this task is assigned to. Populated on single-task RPCs (`CreateTask`, `GetTask`, `UpdateTask`, `SuspendTask`, `ResumeTask`, `CancelTask`); not populated by `ListTasks`.
---@field runCount? string Output only. Runs minted so far by a recurring template, so a client can show progress against `RecurringSchedule.max_run_count`.
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Next scheduled firing of a recurring template. Unset once the template is `SCHEDULE_FINISHED`, and for cron-less (event) schedules.
---@field goals? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GoalList Output only. Goals of the Task, including both active and completed/failed. A Task may pursue several concurrently active goals .
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the task was created.
---@field assignedAgent? string Output only. The resource name of the `Agent` this task is assigned to, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}`. It is derived from the create parent; any value set by the client is ignored.
---@field statusUpdateTime? string Output only. The time the task's status was last updated.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Optional caller-supplied labels. Must follow the unified cloud labels spec (keys/values lowercase `[a-z0-9_-]`, <=63 chars). Stored as-is and returned verbatim on Get/ListTask, so the caller owns what goes in and reads back. Label names starting with `goog-` or `google-` are reserved for predefined labels. Besides user-defined billing/reporting labels, callers may stamp non-PII operational traffic annotations here under the reserved prefix (persisted on the task, so they apply to every turn and survive reconnection). Predefined: `goog-golden-query-id`: stable golden-query / CUJ id (e.g. `hello-world`); absent for organic traffic. Lets per-CUJ latency be trended independently.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the task was last updated.
---@field parentTaskId? string Optional. If this task is a subtask, the parent task's short-form, agent-independent resource name: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tasks/{task} The short form is used here on purpose (NOT the agent-scoped .../agents/{agent}/tasks/{task}): it stays stable when the parent is reassigned to another agent, so subtasks never need rewriting, and the task tree does not imply agent relationships .
---@field title? string Optional. Optional human-readable title for listing surfaces.
---@field name string Identifier. Resource name of the task.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The list of fields to update.

