---@class gcp.unstable.aiplatform_v1beta1.StreamProjectsLocationsAgentsTasksRequest
---@field name string Required. The name of the task to stream. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}/tasks/{task}
---@field snapshot? boolean Optional. If true, streams only the events produced up to the current point in time and terminates the stream once all existing events are sent, rather than tailing and waiting for future events.
---@field nextStepSeqNum? string Optional. The next step sequence number to resume from. When zero, streams from the beginning of the available trajectory.
---@field continuationToken? string Optional. Opaque resume cursor, as issued on TaskServerEvent.continuation_token. Replay continues immediately after the event that carried the token. Takes precedence over next_step_seq_num when both are set. A token this stream cannot redeem is rejected with INVALID_ARGUMENT rather than silently falling back to the numeric cursor, so a client cannot mistake a rejected resume for a replay from the start; reconnect without a token instead. That covers a malformed token, one issued by a connection whose delta streaming differs from this one's (see TaskSpec.delta_streaming), one issued while the server derived task status differently, and any token on a recurring task. A token names a position in the task it was issued on; send it only to that task. It carries no task id, so a token from another task is not rejected, and what it returns is undefined. A token whose position is past the events stored so far is not an error either, because storage can trail the live stream that issued the token: the replay skips everything up to that position, so a snapshot may return no events.

